    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "The University Of Nebraska At Lincoln: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:employment.unl.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs The University Of Nebraska At Lincoln: All Jobs 2026-08-05T10:18:17-05:00 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101633 2026-08-05T10:18:16-05:00 2026-08-05T10:18:17-05:00 Assistant Project Editor, Journals <div>The Assistant Project Editor, Journals, has the primary responsibility of coordinating all phases of journals workflow—including editorial, production, and manufacture, ensuring timely production of high-quality journals. The Assistant Project Editor is required to prioritize work appropriately and meet steady turnaround demands while maintaining high-quality standards for publications with minimal supervision. This position will maintain continuous communication with journal editors, freelancers, print vendors, and internal staff members and will supervise student interns.<br><br>This position may be considered for remote work in accordance with the University of Nebraska’s Alternative Worksite program. More information is available at <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/alternative-worksite\"><strong>https://nebraska.edu/alternative-worksite</strong></a>. <br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> University Press-0933 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102001 2026-08-25T11:23:52-05:00 2026-08-25T11:23:52-05:00 Athletic Certification Manager <div>Responsible for reviewing academic records of student-athletes and documenting compliance with progress-toward-degree and other NCAA, Big Ten, and institutional academic eligibility rules in support of the Assistant Registrar and overall eligibility certification process. Remains familiar with curricular requirements across the University’s Colleges and uses Degree Audit and other reporting software to maintain NCAA eligibility database and projections of future eligibility considerations. Supports Husker Academics counseling staff and frequently handles individual questions from counselors to ensure both UNL degree progress and satisfaction of NCAA and Big Ten academic eligibility requirements for student-athletes. Generates, evaluates, and distributes daily enrollment reporting for academic status and enrollment changes. Serves as a member of AEC (Academics, Eligibility, Compliance) Committee alongside Athletics staff. Act on behalf of Assistant Registrar of Athletic Certification in cases of absence, while maintaining absolute confidentiality with highly sensitive student-athlete information.<br><br><strong>Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</strong><br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Office of the University Registrar-0961 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101089 2026-07-07T15:21:33-05:00 2026-07-07T15:21:34-05:00 Systems Administrator <div>Ranked as one of <strong>the best employers in the state of Nebraska</strong>, the University of Nebraska is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. <br><br><strong>We invest in our employees:</strong></div><ul><li>Vacation, sick, and holiday pay</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance</li><li>No-cost life insurance</li><li>Employee Assistance Program</li><li>Retirement plans with University match</li><li>Tuition assistance for full-time employees and dependents</li><li>Exclusive staff discounts</li><li>Continuous improvement and innovation</li><li>Professional development through training and education</li><li>A diverse and inclusive workplace</li><li>And much more!</li></ul><div><br>As the <strong>Systems Administrator</strong> you will:</div><ul><li>Manage the UNL Police servers, desktop computing systems, and security systems.</li><li>Provide expert advice regarding security system configuration and design. Administer processes and procedures for all systems.</li><li>Responsible for all first-tier technical assistance for all systems, including desktop computing equipment, access control, and CCTV.</li></ul><div><br></div><ul><li>This position is not eligible for work sponsorship</li></ul><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment.</div> University Police-0823 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101885 2026-08-19T10:29:48-05:00 2026-08-19T10:29:49-05:00 Director of Global Partnerships & Initiatives <div>The Director of Global Partnerships &amp; Initiatives works with the Assistant Vice Chancellor for Global Affairs and Senior International Officer to support strategic and operational leadership and implementation of University priorities. The Director is responsible for leading the management, and expansion of international partnerships, supporting enrollment growth through partnership pathways, and nurturing academic collaborations that strengthen the university’s institutional global profile.<br><br>The Director is also responsible for project management and event coordination for strategic international activities.<br><br>The role requires building and sustaining strong relationships with external stakeholders and international alumni, while also collaborating with academic and institutional leadership to ensure partnerships are aligned with institutional priorities and deliver meaningful, measurable impact.<br><br>Responsibilities include: managing outgoing and incoming international delegations, international agreements, and annual reporting on all UNL global engagement efforts; and overseeing Global Affairs communication efforts, as well as events hosted by Global Affairs, Global Partnerships &amp; Initiatives and the SIO. Additional duties include providing strategic insight and support for UNL's international student (graduate and undergraduate) enrollment goals and outreach; and serving as the primary liaison with external strategic partners.<br><br>Successful candidates will demonstrate a strong understanding of international education best practices and organizations, possess a record of advancing institution-wide strategies, as well as experience managing agreements, mobility and exchange programs, sponsored student programs, and grants. The ideal candidate will have excellent communication and organizational skills.<br><br>The Director will also serve as a key advisor and representative for the SIO and Global Affairs unit in engagement with key external stakeholders, including federal and state institutions, foundations, and alumni. This role will manage a development portfolio in alignment with university priorities and unit mission areas and strategic priorities.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Global Partnerships & Initiatives-8376 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102093 2026-08-28T15:19:46-05:00 2026-08-28T15:19:46-05:00 Finance Coordinator - AVE Business Center <div>Join the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) Business Centers, where we strive to deliver exceptional service, innovative solutions, and responsible stewardship that advance IANR’s teaching, research, and extension missions.</div><div><br>As a <strong>Finance Coordinator</strong>, you will coordinate a wide range of financial transactions across multiple fund types, providing responsive support and ensuring compliance with university policies.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities Include</strong>:</div><ul><li>Reviewing expenditures for funding allowability across a variety of account types and preparing payment and transfer requests when appropriate.</li><li>Processing and reviewing accounts payable (A/P) and accounts receivable (A/R) transactions, including reimbursements, non-employee payments, invoices, refunds, internal charges, and outstanding receivables.</li><li>Monitoring assigned accounts, reviewing cost object balances, and preparing standard financial reports.</li><li>Providing guidance and customer support to faculty and staff regarding financial policies, procedures, and business processes.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>This position is located on UNL's East Campus in Lincoln, NE. Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule with a minimum of 3 days per week working onsite. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Note: </strong>Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</div><div><br>We seek a collaborative, service-oriented professional with strong organizational and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate builds positive relationships, communicates effectively with a variety of stakeholders, and is committed to delivering accurate, timely, and compliant financial services.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace </strong>certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> AVE Business Center-3026 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101445 2026-07-27T12:06:54-05:00 2026-07-27T12:06:55-05:00 Assistant Paralegal (2 positions available) <div>Assistant Paralegal in the Clinical Law Programs (CLP) at the University of Nebraska College of Law. Performs primarily paralegal duties in a law office and clinical teaching environment in support of one or more in-house clinics, which may include the Debtor Defense Clinic, Estate Planning Clinic, First Amendment Clinic, Housing Justice Clinic, Nebraska Innocence Clinic, and Weibling Entrepreneurship Clinic. Provides case support, legal clerical support, administrative support related to clinical operations, and assistance to clinical faculty and student attorneys. Works closely with supervising attorneys, students, clients, courts, agencies, and community partners while maintaining strict confidentiality and supporting the educational mission of the Clinical Law Programs.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong><br><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it's a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> College of Law-0899 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101951 2026-08-21T09:01:38-05:00 2026-08-21T09:01:39-05:00 IT Support Associate <div>The <strong>IT Support Associate</strong> provides responsive, customer-focused technology support for faculty, staff, and students across the Hixson-Lied College of Fine and Performing Arts. This position coordinates day-to-day help desk operations and works collaboratively with college and NU Information Technology Services partners to ensure reliable technology services and support.</div><div><br><strong>Responsibilities Include:</strong></div><ul><li>Providing end-user, classroom, and help desk support, including troubleshooting and resolving routine and intermediate technology issues.</li><li>Coordinating help desk operations by triaging support requests, escalating complex issues as appropriate, and ensuring timely follow-up and resolution.</li><li>Supervising 2–3 student workers, including hiring, training, scheduling, assigning work, and ensuring consistent help desk coverage and service quality.</li><li>Supporting a variety of college and NU Information Technology Services systems and services through cross-training and collaboration with technology partners.</li><li>Identifying opportunities to improve technology support by analyzing service trends, researching solutions, documenting procedures, and implementing approved improvements.</li></ul><div><br><strong>We Seek:</strong><br>A service-oriented technology professional who enjoys solving problems and helping others. The successful candidate is an effective communicator who is organized, dependable, and able to balance hands-on technical support with coordinating help desk operations and supervising student employees.</div><div><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> Hixson Lied Fine & Performing Arts-0898 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102154 2026-09-02T13:36:19-05:00 2026-09-02T13:36:19-05:00 Funding Opportunity Coordinator <div>The Office of Research and Innovation (R&amp;I) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) is committed to promoting a culture and environment for success in research, scholarship, creative endeavors, and economic development. Conducting novel and impactful research that generates new knowledge, solves real-world problems, and enhances lives is among the most fundamental purposes of the institution. <br><br>The funding opportunity coordinator will contribute to Nebraska’s land-grant mission in significant and essential ways by: 1) curating and disseminating funding opportunities that align with institutional eligibility and expertise; 2) providing targeted funding opportunity searches for individual scholars and projects; 3) managing and innovating limited submission; and 4) conducting research and outreach around funding opportunities to enhance faculty competitiveness and advance institutional priorities. <br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Research Development-13276 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100401 2026-05-06T10:35:41-05:00 2026-05-06T10:35:41-05:00 Asst/Assoc Professor - Agricultural Banking and Finance <div>The Department of Agricultural Economics at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) is seeking applications for an Agricultural Banking and Finance position at the rank of assistant or associate professor. This 9-month (academic year), tenure-track appointment will develop and maintain nationally and internationally recognized research, teaching, and outreach programs in agricultural banking and finance, including oversight of the undergraduate Agricultural Banking and Finance Program. Located in Lincoln, Nebraska, the position apportionment is 50% research and 50% teaching.<br><br>The successful candidate will provide leadership for the Agricultural Banking and Finance Program in the Department of Agricultural Economics. This includes recruiting, advising, and mentoring approximately 30 to 40 students in the program, along with fostering scholarship and internship support from the Nebraska Banking Association.<br><br>Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate courses in areas such as rural appraisal, agricultural banking, and finance, with opportunities to develop additional undergraduate complementary courses in financial management and analysis. The faculty member is also expected to contribute to graduate education and support the development and strengthening of graduate offerings in agricultural banking and finance.<br><br>The incumbent will develop a research program that addresses key issues in agricultural finance. Areas of emphasis may include capital markets, financial institutions, and risk management within the agricultural sector. The research program is expected to advance understanding of financial performance, resilience, and decision‑making across farms, agribusinesses, and rural economies. While grounded in issues relevant to Nebraska and the region, the program should also contribute to broader national and international discussions in agricultural finance.<br><br>The faculty member will engage with industry and stakeholders to enhance the relevance and impact of research and teaching, contributing to the department’s mission of serving agricultural producers, agribusinesses, and rural communities.<br><br>The successful candidate will be expected to obtain and leverage external research support for these activities and to publish in appropriate high-impact journals. Activities include collaborating with the Nebraska banking industry, including being an active participant in the various state, regional, and national banking conferences.<br><br>Partnerships are expected with other IANR and UNL entities, regional university faculty, and public and private organizations focused on agricultural banking and finance. This includes opportunities to participate in the Center for Agricultural Profitability, Rural Prosperity Nebraska, Engler Agribusiness Entrepreneurship Program, Bureau of Business Research and other academic units within IANR.<br><br>All faculty with a CASNR academic appointment are expected to contribute to the instructional mission of the college. Specific course assignments may be changed over time based on academic unit need. Expectations for this position also include supporting unit recruitment efforts, the IANR science literacy initiative and their individual engagement in the scholarship of teaching and learning. Service expectations include consulting with public programs (extension education and outreach) in the department and public relations (e.g., giving public lectures and writing popular articles). Opportunities exist for science literacy programming for PK-12 teachers and their students. The incumbent will also be expected to contribute to University, Institute, College and Department programs through service on committees.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Agricultural Economics are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR, we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Agricultural Economics-0828 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101790 2026-08-13T14:55:15-05:00 2026-08-13T14:55:17-05:00 Assistant Program Coordinator <div>The Assistant Program Coordinator supports the Tax Credit Alliance of Nebraska (TCAN) Volunteer Income Tax Assistance (VITA) Program through tax site operations, volunteer support, tax preparation, client services, inventory management, and community outreach. This position serves as a key member of the VITA program team and works closely with the Program Coordinator to ensure high-quality tax preparation services are available to eligible individuals and families throughout Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Program Coordinator will learn all aspects of the VITA program, including tax law, site operations, volunteer support, client services, and community engagement. This position is expected to obtain and maintain all required IRS certifications and progressively develop the skills necessary to independently support and manage VITA sites.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Ctr on Children Families & the Law-1082 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102025 2026-08-25T12:33:45-05:00 2026-08-25T12:33:45-05:00 Survey Hydrogeologist <div>The Conservation and Survey Division (Nebraska Geological Survey), the natural resource survey component of the School of Natural Resources, is a unique, multi-disciplinary research, service and data-resource organization. The Division's mission is to investigate and record information about Nebraska's geologic history, its rock and mineral resources, the quantity and quality of its water resources, land cover and other aspects of its geography, as well as the nature, distribution and uses of its soils.<br><br><strong>As a Survey Hydrogeologist, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Conduct applied research on hydrogeology and geology .</li><li>Assist in implementing and maintaining Conservation and Survey Division’s databases, web services, and ongoing research programs to be used in water resources management, research, and education.</li><li>Provide technical support to state and local agencies, including the Natural Resources Districts across Nebraska</li><li>Participate in the geologic mapping program.</li><li>Prepare formal and informal technical reports and presentations on water resources projects and issues. Develop and deliver programs/activities related to hydrogeology, sustainable use of groundwater, and quantity and quality of groundwater.</li><li>Provide water resources service to governmental and educational agencies, industry, and the general public.</li><li>Assist public and governmental agencies in developing programs to monitor and manage water and other natural resources.</li><li>Respond to questions by evaluating and interpreting data.</li><li>Present findings at various venues including seminars, workshops, guest lectures, and national scientific meetings.</li><li>Work collaboratively with School of Natural Resources Environmental Science faculty and Conservation and Survey Division personnel.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> Survey Division - School of Nat Res-0887 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101650 2026-08-05T15:56:50-05:00 2026-08-05T15:56:50-05:00 Office Associate <div>The Department of Food Science and Technology is advancing multi-disciplinary approaches for safe, sustainable and healthy foods through innovative research, teaching and outreach. The Food Innovation Center is located on Nebraska Innovation Campus in Lincoln, NE. <br><br><strong>As the Office Associate, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide administrative support to the graduate program, including responding to inquiries and maintaining applicant and student records.</li><li>Provide professional communication and assist students with program requirements.</li><li>Assist faculty members with roster, textbook, and evaluation functions.</li><li>Coordinate departmental scholarships, fellowships, and assistantship application procedures, deadlines, and files.</li><li>Take on additional responsibilities as needed to support the team and department.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> Food Science & Technology-0836 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102003 2026-08-25T11:24:52-05:00 2026-08-25T11:24:53-05:00 Plumber <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. We invest in our staff by offering fantastic benefits like vacation, sick, and holiday pay, a variety of insurance options, retirement plans, and numerous others. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.<br><br>Building Systems Maintenance has four levels of Plumbers, and the level is determined by a candidate’s knowledge, skills, abilities, and applicable licensure.<br><br><strong>Plumber I, II, III, and IV:</strong> All levels of Plumbers periodically inspect, clean, and perform preventative maintenance of plumbing equipment and spaces to identify and repair and/or report any potential problems, maintain and repair general plumbing equipment, components, and mechanical parts and systems, and perform phases of general, aesthetic, and preventive maintenance of equipment. Additionally, Plumbers assist trade-based or licensed technicians to complete daily tasks, assist with maintenance and repair of complex hydronic and piping systems and equipment, ensure cleanliness and organization in assigned work areas and compliance with regulations and guidelines, and complete work orders and operate an electronic timekeeping system.<br><br><strong>Plumber II:</strong> In addition to the duties and responsibilities above, a level II will work more independently and be given more complex duties including using schematics, blueprint drawings, trade tools, and applicable systems, maintaining and installing new plumbing systems with minimal supervision, communicating and coordinating with outside vendors and manufacturers relative to repair and replacement of building components, and learn the basics of equipment management controls (EMCS) to be able to start, stop, seek status, or change conditions on HVAC and hydronic systems.<br><br><strong>Plumber III:</strong> In conjunction with the duties and responsibilities above, a level III will maintain and repair backflow prevention devices, assist with the maintenance, repair, commission, and installation of complex hydronic and piping systems and equipment, communicate and coordinate with external parties, manufacturers, engineers, and consultants relative to repair and replacement of building components and projects, trend data and reset building maintenance meters utilizing an EMCS, and generate activity and outage notifications.<br><br><strong>Plumber/Pipefitter IV: </strong>In conjunction with the duties and responsibilities above, a level IV ensures proper daily operations, maintenance, repair, commission, and installation of complex hydronic and piping systems and equipment, utilizes life safety decisions for installation and maintenance of natural gas equipment and to locate and repair natural gas leaks, and also trains, mentors, and verifies work of others, contributes to fostering a positive work environment, motivates and encourages staff to improve, supports leadership, and contributes to the development and implementation of departmental vision and goals.<br><br>All levels will be assigned to a rotating on-call schedule and urgent situations occasionally require after-hours work.<br><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> UO Building Systems Maintenance-1004 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101128 2026-07-09T15:51:03-05:00 2026-07-09T15:51:05-05:00 Department Head - Biological Systems Engineering <div>The Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln invites applications for the position of Head of the Department of Biological Systems Engineering (BSE). IANR is seeking an innovative, dynamic, and collaborative person who will provide intellectual and strategic leadership for the department. We are looking for a strong leader who understands university teaching, research, and Extension and who will be able to use their knowledge and skills to help the department maximize its impact. The successful department head will be one who puts the success of the team and department above their individual accomplishments in the role. The incumbent will be one who appreciates the unique contributions of agricultural, biological, and biomedical engineering research and education and how faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders can work together to address the most important challenges facing society. The successful candidate will be committed to excellence wherever it is on the discovery-to-practice continuum. The incumbent will be a collaborative and inspiring department head who will hold fast to the university’s core values of accountability, inclusiveness, integrity, respect, and social responsibility. We seek a leader who recognizes the variety of expertise within our department and is committed to promoting the kind of teamwork and collaboration that enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and belongingness.<br><br>Biological Systems Engineering consists of over 250 undergraduate and graduate students, 38 faculty members, 16 staff members, and 8 postdoctoral fellows committed to high quality, innovative research and scholarship, accessible student-focused education, and impactful Extension programming. In IANR, we aspire to treat every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission. The department head must be one who models and encourages this ethos.<br><br>The department is uniquely positioned for transdisciplinary work at the intersection of biological systems, agriculture, engineering, and biomedical research. BSE resides within IANR and also maintains a close working relationship and collaborations with administrators and faculty in the College of Engineering. The successful candidate will have the technical and interpersonal skills needed to manage the complexities of these relationships in ways that facilitate collaboration.<br><br><strong>Position Overview</strong><br>The head of the Department of Biological Systems Engineering is charged with coordinating and promoting all aspects of the land-grant mission within the department. The incumbent provides leadership and oversight of all BSE programming and initiatives. The department has three undergraduate degree programs, two of which are granted through the College of Engineering and one of which is granted through the College of Agricultural Sciences and Natural Resources (CASNR). While the department maintains a strong working relationship with the College of Engineering, administrative reporting lines, department finances and personnel are managed through IANR.<br><br>The incumbent manages financial and physical resources responsibly to maximize the effectiveness of those resources, exhibiting fiscal discipline and transparency. The head synthesizes a vision for BSE with input from faculty, staff, and stakeholders that encompasses all expertise areas, seeks and deploys personnel and financial resources strategically, and ensures that the strategic vision is continuously examined for relevancy, and refreshed as needed.<br><br>This is an 70% administrative appointment, with the remaining 30% being negotiable based on research, teaching, and Extension interests. This position will be located in Lincoln, Nebraska. The department head will be appointed to a five-year renewable term, subject to satisfactory annual reviews and a formal reappointment process.<br><br>UNL offers an attractive compensation and benefits package, commensurate with the successful candidate’s background and experience. <br> <br> The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Biological Systems Engineering-0833 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101887 2026-08-19T10:30:38-05:00 2026-08-19T10:30:39-05:00 Advisor <div>Serving as an energetic and engaged member of the College of Architecture’s Student Success team, the position will advise undergraduate students in the College of Architecture using knowledge of advising policies and procedures of the college as well as university programs. The staff and faculty are committed to supporting the success of students by providing professional advising and mentoring. These advising efforts contribute to the College’s mission to empower students to successfully enter the workforce as articulate, intellectually aware, self-realizing design professionals capable of performing effectively in evolving design professions.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> College of Architecture-0896 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102096 2026-08-28T17:05:55-05:00 2026-08-28T17:05:56-05:00 Quick Service Team Leader: Slim Chickens (1:00pm-9:30pm, M-F) <div>The <strong>Quick Service Team Leader</strong> will provide guidance and supervision within one of Abel Dining’s mobile order quick service concepts and ensure that orders are accurate, timely and up to the high standards of the University Dining Services.<br><br>The <strong>Quick Service Team Leader</strong> will:</div><ul><li>Provide outstanding customer service</li><li>Ensure that food quality meets and/or exceeds University Dining’s and franchise standards</li><li>Assign daily tasks and assignments to student workers and staff during their shift</li><li>Oversee work in kitchen, dish room, and/or dining area</li><li>Train student workers and staff on recipes, production processes, and University dining standards</li><li>Perform all tasks in all areas/functions, such as; setting up, closing down stations, food production, restocking, daily food prep, cashiering, taking inventory food waste management, cleaning and monitoring food quality</li><li>Troubleshoot and solve concerns directly with customers as they arise</li></ul><div><br>This position is considered essential and schedule may include weekend, evening, or early morning shifts.</div><div><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Housing: AS Dining Service-1135 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102037 2026-08-26T07:58:29-05:00 2026-08-26T07:58:29-05:00 Assistant Director <div>Coordinate and integrate SUNAPSIS including building e-forms, integrating with other university systems and maintaining data between SUNAPSIS and the Student and Exchange Visitors Information System (SEVIS), a federal government system for the tracking of international students and scholars. Prepare immigration documents for F-1 students and J-1 exchange visitors. Coordinate with the Assistant Director, Data Management and Compliance to manage data, provide informational reports (enrollment, census) and submit annual data reports. Advise international students, scholars and employees on federal immigration regulations and their responsibilities for maintaining status. Will work with federal government systems (USCIS, USDHS, USDOL). Will develop procedures to streamline services.</div><div><br>Serve as Designated School Official and Alternate Responsible Officer for <strong>UNL, </strong>having signing authority to issue I-20's and DS-2019's. Perform other duties as necessary for the smooth operation of the International Student and Scholar Office. Develop website material and workshops/trainings/webinars to provide information to international students and scholars. Collaborate with a broad base of offices to ensure that the unique needs of international students and scholars are met.</div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> Intl Student & Scholar Office-8401 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101456 2026-07-27T15:56:22-05:00 2026-07-27T15:56:22-05:00 Ag Research Technician I - (Temporary Part-Time) <div>At the UNL Pandhandle Research, Extension and Education Center in Scottsbluff, NE we innovate and conduct research to make life better for Nebraska ag producers and rural communities. <br><br><strong>As a Part-Time, Temporary Ag Research Technician I, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with research activities in the Entomology lab at UNL's Panhandle Research, Extension and Education Center (PREEC), which includes but is not limited to collecting samples in the field, counting insects under a microscope, processing plant and insect samples in the lab, maintaining field trials, and housekeeping tasks such as cleaning lab supplies in the lab.</li><li>This position will be under the supervision of Dr. Pin-Chu Lai, assistant professor and extension entomologist at PREEC, while working with research technician and graduate students on multiple research project.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us:</strong><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the<strong>Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div><strong>Temporary employees may be appointed for a period of up to two years. Those appointed for more than six months are eligible for benefits from the beginning of the appointment, provided the position is half-time (.50 FTE) or greater. Those appointed for six months or less are not eligible for benefits.</strong></div><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Panhandle Research, Extension and Education Center-0942 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101971 2026-08-24T09:06:26-05:00 2026-08-24T09:06:27-05:00 Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (Flexible Day Shift) <div>At the University of Nebraska where every person and every interaction matters, the Hospitality Service team plays a meaningful role in maintaining safe, healthy, and welcoming environments for students, staff, faculty, and/or guests in a variety of settings.<br><br>In this role you will:</div><ul><li>Perform routine cleaning and upkeep across housing facilities</li><li>Maintain offices, residential halls, public areas, bathrooms, conference rooms, and dining centers</li><li>Ensure a clean, safe environment for all guests</li><li>Clean hard floors and carpets</li><li>Mix cleaning solutions as directed</li><li>Assist with event setup and conference operations as needed</li></ul><div><br>The Hospitality Services position may be hired at a higher level depending upon candidate qualifications.<br><br>Depending upon level assigned, this position may:</div><ul><li>Train and oversee work of others</li><li>Respond to on-call duties and other emergency situations during shifts</li><li>Use all non-riding and non-autonomous equipment</li><li>Order supplies</li></ul><div><br></div><div>When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Attendant</strong>, the position will receive continuous supervision and specific guidelines in the process of training and development.<br><br>When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Assistant, Hospitality Services Associate or Hospitality Services Sr. Associate</strong> the position will routinely perform the skills associated with that level.<br><br>Performance will be continuously assessed to determine ability to perform these skills at an acceptable level.<br><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing Facilities Custodial-11051 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102173 2026-09-03T13:41:21-05:00 2026-09-03T13:41:22-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - 4-H Youth Development (Garden County) <div><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></div><div>This position is based in Oshkosh, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Garden and Morrill Counties. The major responsibility of this position is to provide regional leadership for Nebraska Extension’s 4-H and Youth Development Program. This extension professional is expected to interact closely with 4-H clientele in these communities and deliver programs in their geographic area.</div><div><br></div><div>The Positive Youth Development – 4-H extension professional will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home unit and the IANR as an effective scholar and citizen, including supporting student recruitment and IANR science literacy. In 4-H, we believe in the power of young people. We see that every child has valuable strengths and real influence to improve the world around us. We are America’s largest youth development organization, empowering nearly six million young people across the U.S. with the skills to lead for a lifetime. Nebraska Extension is an organization that values excellence and as a member of the Nebraska Extension team you will create and deliver world-class learning experiences focused on critical issues that empower Nebraskans to improve their lives.<br><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an open rank educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress towards and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%)</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., schools or community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs entrepreneurial practices to obtain funding and partnerships, enhancing Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%)</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator </strong></a>document as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<ul><li>Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.</li><li>Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.</li><li>Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li></ul></li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR, we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective well-being and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 1-12350 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100523 2026-05-15T12:19:30-05:00 2026-05-15T12:19:31-05:00 Director, CYFS and Full Professor <div>The Nebraska Center for Research on Children, Youth, Families, and Schools (CYFS), in partnership with the College of Education and Human Sciences (CEHS) at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, seeks an accomplished research leader to serve as Director. This opportunity is ideally suited for a senior principal investigator or current research center director with a strong record of externally funded, interdisciplinary research and experience leading a large, complex research enterprise.<br><br></div><div>CYFS is a nationally recognized, revenue-generating research center advancing high-impact scholarship in the social, behavioral, and educational sciences. For more than two decades, CYFS has played a central role in driving research excellence, external funding, and interdisciplinary collaboration across the University of Nebraska system. As the sole collegewide research center in CEHS, CYFS provides critical research infrastructure and expert pre- and post-award grantsmanship support—driving faculty productivity, securing competitive external funding, promoting research partnerships, and ensuring high-impact research implementation and outcomes. Learn more at <a href=\"https://cyfs.unl.edu/\"><strong>https://cyfs.unl.edu/</strong></a>.</div><div><br><strong>Why this role, why now.</strong></div><div>CYFS is entering a pivotal leadership transition following more than two decades of sustained growth and success under its founding director. The Center is financially stable, highly productive, and supported by an experienced research and administrative team. At a time when federal funding increasingly favors interdisciplinary, multi-institutional research, this role offers a rare opportunity for an established leader to build on a strong foundation, scale major research initiatives, and shape the next phase of CYFS’s national impact. The Director will provide strategic leadership for a mature, high-performing research organization operating in an increasingly competitive federal funding environment.</div><div><br><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Sustaining and expanding external funding.</li><li>Guiding long-term strategic planning.</li><li>Strengthening interdisciplinary research collaborations.</li><li>Overseeing fiscal and administrative operations.</li><li>Positioning CYFS for continued growth, visibility, and scholarly impact.</li><li>Play a central role in shaping research priorities and mentoring research faculty and staff.</li><li>Cultivating internal and external partnerships at the university, community, state, and national levels.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The position is expected to be a fiscal year (FY) appointment with a split FTE of up to 0.75 FTE as Director apportioned as 100% administration and supported with an administrative stipend. The position is expected to have an apportionment that is aligned with teaching a minimum of one course a year. The Director will report to the CEHS Dean and will hold a faculty appointment within CEHS, commensurate with disciplinary background and scholarly accomplishments. The successful candidate should have academic and scholarly achievements that support the rank of Full Professor with tenure, according to CEHS and UNL standards. In addition to providing administrative and strategic leadership for the Center, the Director is expected to maintain an active program of externally funded research and to lead CYFS faculty, staff, and university-wide affiliates in advancing a vibrant, interdisciplinary research enterprise with sustained national prominence.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ctr Research on Youth, Fam & School-4425 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101799 2026-08-14T07:15:31-05:00 2026-08-14T07:15:31-05:00 Student Conduct Specialist <div>Reporting to the Associate Director of Student Conduct &amp; Community Standards, this position is responsible for the various elements of student conduct investigations and related procedures. The Student Conduct Specialist oversees investigations related to the standards of academic integrity and responsible conduct allegations for all UNL students. Position provides prompt, equitable, and impartial investigations into allegations regarding violations of the Student Code of Conduct; meeting with students who have allegedly violated the Student Code of Conduct; meeting with witnesses, complainants, and/or victims to gather information and evidence; and determining educational outcomes. Gathers and assesses evidence relevant to the investigation and identifies University policies and/or Student Code of Conduct provisions relevant to a referral. Coordinates education, prevention, and training efforts. Participates in presenting information to Conduct Board Hearings. Responsible for keeping current in the field of student conduct investigations by participating in conferences, workshops, and professional training.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Student Conduct & Community Standard-0963 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/97613 2025-07-15T16:58:13-05:00 2025-07-15T16:58:14-05:00 Food Service Associate (On-Call; Curtis, NE) <div>The Nebraska College of Technical Agriculture (NCTA), located in Curtis, NE, is nationally ranked as one of the best two-year colleges, and Forbes Business Magazine placed us among the top 30 trade schools in the nation. Our programs have high academic quality, are affordable and guarantee career success for graduates.<br><br><strong>Position Overview</strong><br>NCTA is seeking a reliable, customer-focused <strong>Food Service Associate</strong> to serve in a flexible, <strong>on-call capacity</strong>. Work hours may be scheduled in advance or requested on an as-needed basis, depending on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Duties and Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Perform a variety of food service tasks across cafeteria, deli, catering, and related areas.</li><li>Set up and close down stations; cook, prep ingredients, and restock supplies.</li><li>Maintain food quality and presentation standards; monitor temperature, taste, and appearance.</li><li>Operate dish machines and perform general cleaning and light custodial duties.</li><li>Control food costs and waste; assist with inventory and recipe prep.</li><li>Provide excellent customer service and assist with cashiering and computer use.</li><li>Train others as needed; perform additional duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Position requires obtaining a Food Handler's permit (can be earned by passing Safety and Sanitation test). Position requires the ability to push/pull heavy carts that may exceed 50 pounds and requires lifting and moving of heavy items, including on stairs. On-Call employees may work up to 693 hours per fiscal year and are not eligible for paid leave or any other university benefits. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as O/S On Call Hourly.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential.<br></em><br></div><div><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> NE College of Technical Agriculture-0928 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101655 2026-08-06T08:38:07-05:00 2026-08-06T08:38:08-05:00 Catering Prep Chef/Driver <div>The <strong>Catering Prep Chef/Driver</strong> is an integral member of the catering team. This position will assist the entire Catering department.<br><br></div><div>In this role you will:</div><ul><li>Safely operate the catering box truck, or other University vehicles in all weather conditions.</li><li>Oversee and execute the pickup, drop off and delivery of food, materials, and equipment necessary for events.</li><li>Support the culinary and front of house teams with operational assistance, including food preparation, dishwashing, event set up, tear down, and clean up.</li><li>Ensure the Catering vehicles are following proper maintenance schedules in accordance with University protocols.</li><li>Have a customer service focus, ability to utilizes effective time management skills, and a strong attention to detail with high accuracy are vital to this position.</li></ul><div><br><br><strong>Schedule varies and includes early morning, evenings, late night, and weekend shifts.</strong><em><br><br></em><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: Catering-12429 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102007 2026-08-25T11:28:14-05:00 2026-08-25T11:28:15-05:00 Paleontology Collection Manager <div>Principal responsibilities are organization, management, preservation, conservation, and supervision of use of paleontological specimens in the collections of the UNSM Paleontology Department, including the Invertebrate Paleontology and Vertebrate Paleontology Divisions. This position also maintains archives related to the collections and other important documents. Responsibilities include maintenance of the Paleontology databases and collection digitization – photography, data records, archived catalogues, field notebooks, and additional metadata (provenance, identifications, etc.). Duties include monitoring the storage environment and security, monitoring for pests and taking appropriate pest management actions, conducting object condition reports, coordinating incoming and outgoing loans, and processing new acquisitions.<br><br>This position assists and supervises visiting researchers, trains and supervises collection volunteers, UNL student interns, student employees, nonstudent employees and other users of the collections in collaboration with paleontology staff and curators to ensure proper maintenance of collections. An additional set of responsibilities centers on supporting the museum’s public education mission by assisting with exhibit curation (selection of objects, drafting text, installing/de-installing exhibit objects), assisting with educational programs as a content expert and speaker, and contributing to the museum’s digital presence by providing content for social media posts and website.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> University Museum-0932 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101222 2026-07-14T14:55:06-05:00 2026-07-14T14:55:07-05:00 Feedlot Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The <strong>U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC)</strong> is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.</div><div><br><strong>As a Feedlot Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 6,500 head at the feedlot.</li><li>Maintain pens, machinery and fences.</li><li>Collect research data.</li></ul><div><br>Experience in the care and riding of horses preferred but not required. Position requires irregular hours and work in inclement weather. Travel between feeding locations and facilities is required.<br><br>Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a pen rider or feed truck driver.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101889 2026-08-19T10:31:24-05:00 2026-08-19T10:31:24-05:00 News and Public Relations Writer/Editor <div>Reporting to the senior director of strategic communications, this position serves as a primary editorial partner for the university’s news and strategic communications operation. This role supports the university’s strategic communication efforts by contributing advanced editorial expertise to the creation, coordination and dissemination of news and information that enhances the institution’s reputation, engages key stakeholders and aligns with university goals.<br><br></div><div>Working closely with the senior director of strategic communications, this position provides continuity for day-to-day newsroom operations and exercises delegated editorial authority in support of established priorities. The role requires exceptional news judgment, strong collaboration skills and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced newsroom environment.<br><br><strong>Please include 3-5 examples of authored stories or link to online portfolio with application.</strong><br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Office of University Communication-0852 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102100 2026-08-31T08:00:58-05:00 2026-08-31T08:00:58-05:00 Academic Pathway Advisor <div>Are you passionate about empowering first-generation and low-income students to reach their full potential? Join our team as an <strong>Academic Pathway Advisor</strong> and be a driving force in shaping brighter futures for youth in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>As the<strong> Academic Pathway Advisor</strong>, you will:<br><br></div><ul><li>Recruit, advise and support students in the program and monitor their success.</li><li>Build relationships with school counselors, families and community partners within the Lincoln/Waverly surrounding area.</li><li>Host interactive workshops, provide one-on -one advising, tutoring, and facilitate enrichment programs.</li><li>Assist int the planning and execution of the summer program.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Regular travel within the service area is required.<br><br></div><div>About Us:</div><div><strong>Educational Talent Search </strong>(ETS) engages, empowers and supports potential first generation college and under-served scholars who have the desire and potential to pursue an education beyond high school. We provide access to academic, social, and financial resources to students across five Nebraska Service Areas.<br><br></div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> <br> <br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> TRIO Programs-0962 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101828 2026-08-17T07:45:16-05:00 2026-08-17T07:45:16-05:00 Instructional Services Coordinator <div>Provide project and Instructional Services clerical support to all initiatives involving the University of Nebraska High School. Support includes inter- and intra-departmental, external client and vendor project and or program organization, coordination, communications, maintenance, and tracking to ensure all projects and student support items are effectively completed on-time.<br><br></div><div><strong>Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br></strong><br></div><pre>#LI-DNI</pre> University of Nebraska System https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102053 2026-08-27T08:39:55-05:00 2026-08-27T08:39:56-05:00 Chick-fil-A Shift Lead (Part-Time) <div>As a<strong> Chick-fil-A Shift Lead</strong> you will:</div><ul><li>Serve as a member of the management team by providing leadership, direction and supervision to Team Members during their shift and ensuring a high – quality experience for guests.</li><li>Provide day-to-day operational leadership:<ul><li>By delegating shift duty assignments to staff/students.</li><li>Oversee front end and back of restaurant operations.</li><li>Ensure products and ingredients are stocked and available based on forecasting.</li><li>Training new team members.</li><li>Ensure presentation, quality, and food standards are met.</li></ul></li><li>Provide excellent customer service to all guest through front end and back-end operations which may include:<ul><li>Greeting all guests in a friendly manner and addressing guest concerns</li><li>Accurately entering orders into the POS system and cashier duties</li><li>Food preparation and monitoring food quality and safety</li><li>Front end and kitchen stocking</li><li>Ingredient preparation</li><li>Inventory, dish machine operation, cleaning duties, opening, and closing procedures.</li></ul></li></ul><div><br><em>A job as a shift lead is more than just a job. It’s a stepping-stone to a successful future in the world of business.<br><br></em><strong>Schedule varies and includes evenings, late nights, and weekend shifts.</strong> <em><br><br></em><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: Chick-fil-A-12426 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101487 2026-07-29T09:44:50-05:00 2026-07-29T09:44:51-05:00 Reading Teacher Coach Specialist (Full-time) <div>The Nebraska Center for Research on Children, Youth, Families and Schools is seeking a full-time Reading Teacher Coach Specialist for work on the Nebraska Workshops on Reading Development Strategies (WORDS) Project, a program funded by the Nebraska Department of Education and Institute of Education Sciences that aims to provide rural schools with professional development and support to prepare all students for reading success by systematically delivering high-quality instruction tailored to meet their needs.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities include</strong>:</div><div>• Serve as an active member of the WORDS project</div><div>• Conduct reading observations and evaluate reading instruction in schools across the state</div><div>• Provide consultation, training, and on-site implementation support services to school districts</div><div>• Provide reading professional development opportunities for school district and ESU staff and community professionals</div><div>• Work in close collaboration with the Reading Teacher Coach Lead to ensure all WORDS activities align with broader WORDS project goals</div><div>• Work in close collaboration with WORDS Reading Teacher Coach Lead to tailor training and supports to individual school needs</div><div>• Maintain the WORDS Resource Library with current publications related to the field of continuous improvement.</div><div>• Stay informed of evidence-based instructional materials, strategies, interventions, assessments, and technology for improved reading outcomes for ALL students.</div><div>• Be aware of new research and best practices around reading within Multi-tiered Systems of Support</div><div>• Maintain a database of all contacts and training and supports provided</div><div>• Contribute to the enhancement of the WORDS Website</div><div>• Participate in ongoing professional learning opportunities at the state and national level.</div><div>• Work involves travel to schools, but some work can be done remotely and through virtual conferencing.</div><div><br><strong>About Us<br></strong>The College of Education and Human Sciences strives to be a vibrant, welcoming, and caring community driven by our mission to enhance the lives of individuals, families, schools, and communities, and strengthening the relationships among them.<br><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> NE Ctr Research on Youth, Fam & School-4425 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101979 2026-08-24T15:45:36-05:00 2026-08-24T15:45:37-05:00 Office Associate <div>As the<strong> Office Associate,</strong> you will provide administrative assistance to the Department of Special Education and Communication Disorders, and serve as a liaison between the Administrative Coordinator, Department Office, the College, University administrative units, students, and the public.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Assisting the chairperson in the planning, organizing, administering, and monitoring of the administration of the Department and the Barkley Memorial Center</li><li>Preparing and submitting various reports as required by the Department, College, and University.</li><li>Maintaining data and files related to departmental activities and processes.</li><li>Managing class scheduling for the Department, coordinating with faculty, advisors, and other University offices.</li><li>Making travel arrangements.</li><li>Scheduling meetings and organizing their agendas and documentation.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us<br></strong>The College of Education and Human Sciences strives to be a vibrant, welcoming, and caring community driven by our mission to enhance the lives of individuals, families, schools, and communities, and strengthening the relationships among them.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace </strong>certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> Special Ed & Communic Disorders-1049 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102178 2026-09-03T21:57:44-05:00 2026-09-03T21:57:44-05:00 Senior Retail Associate (6:00am 2:30pm, M-F) <div>The<strong> Sr. Retail Associate</strong> is an integral part of the success of our Abel Hall Herbie’s Market team. In this role you will manage and lead the store operations and provide excellent customer service to all patrons.<br><br>As the <strong>Sr. Retail Associate</strong> you will be responsible for:</div><ul><li>Hiring, training, and supervising student employees</li><li>Ordering and maintaining inventory</li><li>Basic accounting duties such as reconciling sales receipts, cash controls, and inventory balancing</li><li>Ensure that the store meets the presentation standards by cleaning and sanitizing equipment</li></ul><div><br>Schedule may vary due to the needs of the store.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em> .</em></div> Housing: AS C Store-2305 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100595 2026-05-22T12:19:47-05:00 2026-05-22T12:19:47-05:00 Open Rank Geoscientist <div>The School of Natural Resources (SNR) Conservation and Survey Division (CSD) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) is seeking applications for an open rank geoscientist position. This 12-month (calendar year), non-tenure track appointment will develop a research program and educate the public on issues related to groundwater resources and the hydrogeology of Nebraska and the surrounding region. Located in Lincoln, Nebraska, the apportionment is 75% research and 25% extension.<br><br><strong>Specific Duties<br></strong><em>Research (75%)</em></div><ul><li>Build and maintain a successful applied research program with innovative and complimentary water related focus (<a href=\"https://snr.unl.edu/csd/\"><strong>https://snr.unl.edu/csd/</strong></a>).</li><li>Plan and conduct basic and applied research on hydrogeology and geology.</li><li>Generate external research grants.</li><li>Collaborate with governmental agencies, municipalities, industry, and educational institutions.</li><li>Develop and maintain working relationships with stakeholders to address water-related research and issues.</li><li>Respond to inquiries by evaluating and interpreting data and applying current research understandings.</li><li>Present findings at various venues including seminars, workshops, guest lectures, and national scientific meetings.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><em>Extension (25%)</em></div><ul><li>Publish manuscripts and present on groundwater issues in Nebraska to the appropriate audiences.</li><li>Educate the public and stakeholders on groundwater issues.</li><li>Support the CSD team’s survey efforts and mission with expert interactions and reporting (Annual Groundwater levels report).</li><li>Work in conjunction with SNR Geology, Soil, and Water Survey faculty to provide services to clientele.</li></ul><div><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and the School of Natural Resources Conservation and Survey Division are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate. <br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> School of Natural Resources-0844 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/99159 2026-01-30T11:28:16-06:00 2026-01-30T11:28:16-06:00 Research Assistant Professor <div>The Rural Drug Addiction Research (RDAR) Center at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) seeks to hire a Research Assistant Professor. This scholar will work closely with Center leadership, including the co-directors of the research core (Longitudinal Network Core [LNC]). The individual in this position will be responsible for hypothesis driven analysis of RDAR Center data with outcomes from these being presented and published in key outlets. This individual will also have the opportunity to develop distinct areas of scholarship in substance use research and compete for extramural funding.</div><div><br></div><div>The RDAR Center, funded by NIH, brings together basic and health scientists across disciplines that span synapse to society. In doing so, we address the causes and consequences of substance use and misuse along with the assessment, prevention, and treatment of this critical public health challenge. The individual in the position will also have the opportunity to develop collaborations with other members of the Center and the broader university community.</div><div><br></div><div>This is a full-time, 12-month position with the possibility of renewal, contingent upon performance and funding. Anticipated start date is April 1, 2026, but is flexible depending on availability. Learn more about the Rural Drug Addiction Research Center at <a href=\"https://rdar.unl.edu/\"><strong>https://rdar.unl.edu/</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Rural Drug Addiction Research Center-10950 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101676 2026-08-06T14:53:19-05:00 2026-08-06T14:53:19-05:00 Sous Chef <div>The Sous Chef provides operational and culinary leadership to UNL's Kosher kitchen and multiple dining operations across campus.<br><br>The Sous Chef will:</div><ul><li>Help lead kitchen operations with experience and passion for food service and high level of customer engagement.</li><li>Serve as a key member within the dining center and culinary leadership team.</li><li>Assist in the creation and execution of developing a culture within dining locations that prioritizes quality, innovation, nutrition, and sustainability while serving the residential and campus community.</li><li>Make data driven decisions for menu planning, labor forecasting to ensure fiscal responsibility.</li><li>Support campus events, themed meals, and outreach programming.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a><strong><em>.</em></strong></div> Housing Dining Service-1131 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102009 2026-08-25T11:31:01-05:00 2026-08-25T11:31:02-05:00 Dining Service Production Manager (1:00pm-9:30pm, Tues-Sat) <div>The <strong>Dining Service Production Manager</strong> is responsible for the supervision of the food production areas within a university residence hall dining center.<br><br></div><div>The <strong>Dining Service Production Manager</strong> will:</div><ul><li>Assist with the management and supervision of other operational areas of the university residence hall dining center</li><li>Plan and coordinate the production of menu items for student meal service and special events by providing hands-on participation of safe and high quality meal preparation</li><li>Ensure adherence to recipes and food production policies and procedures for overall product consistency, quality, freshness and appearance</li><li>Work in conjunction with the manager, assistant manager(s) and team leaders on product evaluation and in using the menu management system to develop, improve, evaluate/standardize recipes</li><li>Maintain a positive working environment for employees</li><li>Provide a safe and inviting atmosphere, healthful meal choices, and quality service in an environment that promotes community, growth, and education of our students, staff, faculty and guests</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: AS Dining Service-1135 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101231 2026-07-15T08:39:44-05:00 2026-07-15T08:39:45-05:00 Graduate Admission Support Associate (Temporary) <div>This is a temporary data entry and online customer service position that supports the processing of electronic applications for graduate study at UNL. The responsibilities of this position are essential to maintain the integrity and continuity of key quality control functions related to admissions data. Accurate and timely data entry at the point of application is critical, as it directly impacts identity management, enrollment, student accounts, and university reporting. Ensuring these data points are correctly entered at the start of the student-university relationship is vital to the institution's operational and reporting accuracy.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential.<br></em><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Graduate Studies-0900 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101891 2026-08-19T10:32:02-05:00 2026-08-19T10:32:02-05:00 Associate Director <div>The Associate Director leads undergraduate admissions recruitment for first-time freshmen both nationally and within Nebraska. This role coordinates high school visits, college fairs, and outreach with counselors and educators outside Nebraska in primary, secondary, and tertiary markets, under the guidance of the Executive Director of Admissions. The Office of Admissions is part of the Academic Services and Enrollment Management (ASEM) division. As a member of the Admissions Leadership Team, the Associate Director collaborates with peers across the division, leveraging data to guide recruitment efforts and provide leadership to achieve enrollment goals. Responsibilities include analyzing graduation rates in states bordering Nebraska and in key markets.<br><br></div><div>The Associate Director oversees a recruitment team and directly supervises Assistant Directors. They guide staff to meet enrollment goals and provide regular progress updates to the Executive Director of Admissions. Key responsibilities include training staff in territory management, monitoring performance, and supporting professional growth. This role plans and implements yield activities and territory strategies to convert prospects into enrollments. The Associate Director reviews recruitment data and territory outcomes, making data-driven adjustments to strengthen strategies and increase market share. In collaboration with the Executive Director, Admissions Leadership, and campus partners, the Associate Director develops reports and plans to drive strategy and achieve enrollment targets.<br><br></div><div>The Associate Director exercises independent judgment in interpreting admissions policies, making recruitment decisions, and overseeing functional initiatives aligned with strategic priorities. The position collaborates with units within ASEM and across campus to align recruitment objectives with university initiatives. Additionally, the Associate Director works closely with Visitor Experience to ensure effective resource allocation for recruitment events and activities, and builds strong relationships with high school counselors, community contacts, and key influencers to expand student access and support recruitment. As needed, this role provides leadership support to the broader admissions team and may serve as a proxy for the Executive Director of Admissions.</div><div>Regular travel, including evenings and weekends, is required.<br><br>This position is based in Lincoln, Nebraska, and provides leadership for the national recruitment team, with travel to key recruitment markets across the country expected.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Admissions-0959 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102108 2026-08-31T11:20:24-05:00 2026-08-31T11:20:24-05:00 Electrician III (Ithaca, NE) <div>The Eastern Nebraska Research, Extension and Education Center (ENREEC) in Ithaca, Nebraska is a leading hub for agricultural research, education, and innovation. Spanning nearly 9,700 acres of row crops and pasture and home to over 6,000 livestock animals, ENREEC plays a vital role in advancing modern farming. ENREEC is located close to Mead, Fremont, Ashland, and Wahoo and is just 30 minutes from Omaha or Lincoln.<br><br><strong>As an Electrician III, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Install and maintain electrical power systems at ENREEC.</li><li>Plan, perform, and supervise electrical installations including circuitry, sizing of wire, switching, mains and junction boxes for new and repair of existing single phase and three phase electrical systems.</li><li>Perform diagnostics, repair, and maintenance on electrical equipment and controls.</li><li>Prepare and obtain state electrical permits and perform follow-through inspections to ensure all electrical work is completed correctly and complies with current local, state and federal electrical codes.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>Looking for a job where you can advance professionally and <strong>have time for life outside work?</strong><br><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Eastern Nebraska Research, Extension and Education Center-9750 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101847 2026-08-18T09:30:54-05:00 2026-08-18T09:30:54-05:00 Grants Specialist <div>Join the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) Business Centers, where we strive to deliver exceptional service, innovative solutions, and responsible stewardship that advance IANR’s teaching, research, and extension missions.</div><div><br>As a<strong> Grants Specialist,</strong> you will serve as a trusted resource to faculty and departments, providing expert guidance and administrative support throughout the sponsored research proposal process.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Partnering with faculty and departments to support the successful development and submission of sponsored research proposals.</li><li>Providing consultative guidance on grants administration policies, procedures, and best practices.</li><li>Coordinating proposal budgets, documentation, submissions, and grant startup activities.</li><li>Collaborating with university partners to deliver exceptional service and promote effective, compliant research administration.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>We seek a proactive, service-oriented professional with strong problem-solving skills and a commitment to helping faculty and departments navigate the sponsored research proposal process. The ideal candidate builds collaborative relationships, communicates effectively with diverse stakeholders, and thrives in a fast-paced environment where attention to detail, organization, and sound judgment are essential.</div><div><br>This position is located on UNL’s East Campus in Lincoln, NE, home to the beautiful Maxwell Arboretum, the UNL Dairy Store, and plenty of parking! Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with a minimum of 3 days per week worked on campus. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and determined based on operational needs.<br><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Natural Resources Business Center-0914 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102066 2026-08-27T13:48:42-05:00 2026-08-27T13:48:43-05:00 Utility Steamfitter/Pipefitter <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska and certified as a Lincoln Family-Friendly workplace, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. <br><br><strong>We invest in our employees:</strong></div><ul><li>Vacation, sick, and holiday pay.</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance.</li><li>No-cost life insurance.</li><li>Employee Assistance Program.</li><li>Parental leave</li><li>Retirement plans.</li><li>Tuition assistance for employees and dependents.</li><li>Exclusive employee discounts.</li><li>Professional development through training and education.</li><li>And many more!!</li></ul><div><br><strong>As a Utility Steamfitter/Pipefitter, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Responsible for layout, design, installation, assembly, maintenance, testing, and repair of mechanical utility piping systems.</li><li>Work with high-pressure boilers and chillers, encompassing various systems such as hot water, chilled water, steam, and more.</li><li>Follow local and state codes for all piping and fitting tasks.</li><li>Operate welding equipment to perform Arc, GMAW, Tig, and oxy fuel welding and cutting tasks.</li><li>Read and interpret system prints and schematics accurately.</li><li>Flexibility to work beyond normal shifts, 24/7 availability for emergencies, shift coverage, or other operational demands, sometimes on short notice.</li></ul><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> UO Husker Energy & Power-12300 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101492 2026-07-29T11:33:34-05:00 2026-07-29T11:33:35-05:00 Academic Advisor <div>Advise current and prospective students in one or more majors in the College of Arts and Sciences on academic program planning in person through drop-ins and appointments, and by phone and email. Participate in recruitment and retention efforts, including New Student Enrollment. Encourage overall well-being and adjustment to the University as well as exploration of interests as they relate to majors and careers. Assist students in identifying quality real-world experience through internships, research, education abroad, service, and leadership. <br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>As an EO employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a></div> College of Arts & Sciences-0906 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101984 2026-08-25T08:15:57-05:00 2026-08-25T08:15:57-05:00 Chick-fil-A Operations Manager <div>Ranked as one of <strong>the best employers in the state of Nebraska</strong>, the University of Nebraska is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.</div><div>We invest in our employees:</div><div>• Vacation, sick, and holiday pay</div><div>• Medical, dental, and vision insurance</div><div>• No-cost life insurance</div><div>• Employee Assistance Program</div><div>• Retirement plans with University match</div><div>• Tuition assistance for full-time employees and dependents</div><div>• Exclusive staff discounts</div><div>• Continuous improvement and innovation</div><div>• Professional development through training and education</div><div>• And much more!</div><div><br>The Operations Manager is an integral member of the leadership team by assisting the General Manager in the overall supervision and operation of the restaurant.<br><strong><br>As the Chick-fil-A Operations Manager you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Help drive an operation that provides a safe and inviting atmosphere for all guests, staff, and student workers.</li><li>Provides high-quality customer service to all guests.</li><li>Ensure orders are accurate and meet all University Dining and franchise standards.</li><li>Create an environment that promotes diversity and growth for student workers, staff, and guests.</li><li>Assist in the facilitation of the hiring and training process.</li><li>Complete supply ordering, administrate maintenance schedules, and are able to assist in daily duties and tasks.</li></ul><div><br><em>At Chick-fil-A, the Operations Manager role is more than just a job, it’s an opportunity.</em></div><div><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: Chick-fil-A-12426 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102180 2026-09-04T09:11:02-05:00 2026-09-04T09:11:02-05:00 Events Coordinator <div>Coordinate social functions at the Lied Center or any other venue as assigned, such as meetings, luncheons/dinners, receptions, weddings, tailgates and mainstage rental events. Coordinate all areas of event presentation with artist, agents and rental venue clients; serve as primary point of contact and coordinate all event requirements, information and changes with other Lied Center departments to fulfill all contractual obligations for all parties with artist or user. Coordinate event schedules, rental equipment, provide artist transportation and acquire hospitality supplies from vendors. Monitor event budget and submit costs for event close-out. Assist in organization of outreach/education programs including all logistical arrangements. Coordinate event promotions and media events with Marketing department. Make sure all Lied Center and University policies and procedures are followed as part of each event.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> Lied Center for Performing Arts-0854 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100708 2026-06-02T10:41:04-05:00 2026-06-02T10:41:05-05:00 Farm Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Farm Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Perform all activities associated with irrigated forage production including but not limited to tillage, planting, chemical applications, irrigation and harvesting operations.</li><li>Perform routine equipment maintenance and repair.</li><li>Assist other operational areas including but not limited to livestock feeding and care, fence installation and repair, building /facility maintenance.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather required. Due to the size of the facility, a valid driver's license is required to travel between sites.<br><br>Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I.&nbsp;</div><div><br><strong>Note: Sponsorships will not be offered for this position. <br></strong><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102115 2026-08-31T16:18:30-05:00 2026-08-31T16:18:30-05:00 Supply Control Clerk (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility located near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As the Supply Control Clerk, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Check all incoming supplies and equipment against receiving documents for agreement as to quantity, description, size, weight, etc.</li><li>Pack and ship by most economical methods, any damaged or other merchandise to be returned.</li><li>Perform typical warehouse functions, such as receiving, stocking shelves, filling orders and delivering ordered goods.</li><li>Operate organization vehicles to move materials to and from work locations.</li><li>Perform clerical functions such as typing requisitions, maintaining computerized inventory system and filing.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/99689 2026-03-10T16:31:47-05:00 2026-03-10T16:31:48-05:00 Assistant Controller <div>Ranked as one of <strong>the best employers in the state of Nebraska</strong>, the University of Nebraska is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.<br><br> We invest in our employees:</div><ul><li>Vacation and sick leave pay</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance</li><li>No-cost life insurance</li><li>Employee Assistance Program</li><li>Exclusive staff discounts</li><li>Continuous improvement and innovation</li><li>Professional development through training and education</li><li>A diverse and inclusive workplace</li><li>And much more!</li></ul><div><br>The University of Nebraska - Lincoln seeks a highly skilled and detail-oriented <strong>Assistant Controller</strong> to oversee financial reporting and drive process efficiencies. This critical role ensures accurate financial statements, enhances reporting capabilities, and identifies automation opportunities.<br> <br><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Assist the Controller in managing financial processes, ensuring accuracy, and implementing best practices.</li><li>Support student accounts, bursar, audits, and internal controls to uphold sound financial stewardship.</li><li>Collaborate with cross-functional teams to improve financial data integrity and reporting accuracy.</li><li>Drive process improvements and automation to enhance efficiency across administrative systems.</li><li>Strong understanding of data and ability to translate to operations.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment.</em></div> Business and Finance-50000084 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101697 2026-08-10T09:12:31-05:00 2026-08-10T09:12:32-05:00 Civil Rights Investigator <div>UNL is committed to creating a campus free from discrimination and harassment. The Civil Rights Investigator will play an important role in the University's education, prevention and response efforts pursuant to Title VII, Title VI, Title IX and related statutes. The Civil Rights Investigator will report to the Title IX Coordinator and the Associate to the Chancellor for Institutional Equity and Compliance. The Civil Rights Investigator will assist with, among other duties: creation and implementation of policies and procedures; education and training for the university community; and investigation of discrimination and harassment complaints.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Institutional Equity and Compliance-0851 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102011 2026-08-25T11:31:50-05:00 2026-08-25T11:31:50-05:00 Assistant Athletic Trainer - Spirit Squad <div>Perform a variety of duties involved in the administration, evaluation, treatment, care, and rehabilitation of student-athletes within the University of Nebraska Athletic Department. The focus of responsibilities will be with the Nebraska Spirit Squad including practice and event coverage, and any required travel. Working with the teams will involve some non-traditional hours, nights, weekends, some holidays. Adherence to all NCAA, conference, and institutional rules and regulations will be required.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> Athletics-0850 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101285 2026-07-17T10:51:42-05:00 2026-07-17T10:51:43-05:00 Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide a variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle.</li><li>Maintain machinery and fences,</li><li>Assist with pasture management</li><li>Assist with the collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather required. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101898 2026-08-19T10:37:37-05:00 2026-08-19T10:37:38-05:00 NCPA Program Associate <div>Under the supervision of the Associate Director, this position is responsible for providing personalized academic support and guidance for Nebraska College Preparatory Academy (NCPA) students in Omaha, as well as coordinating all multi-day summer programming for NCPA high school students at UNL. Position will also coordinate recruitment programs in Omaha. Position will meet with school counselors and prospective students; interact with community organization and agency staff; plan and implement special events and programs for recruitment/retention of first generation/low-income students; and serve as liaison between UNL, Omaha and other communities. This is a grant-funded position.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Nebraska College Preparatory Academy-10850 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100715 2026-06-02T10:46:15-05:00 2026-06-02T10:46:16-05:00 Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide a variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle.</li><li>Maintain machinery and fences.</li><li>Assist with pasture management.</li><li>Assist with the collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Position requires irregular hours and work in inclement weather. Due to the size of the facility, a valid driver's license and ability to meet University driver eligibility criteria is required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.<br><br><strong>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</strong><br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>Looking for a job where you can advance professionally and <strong>have time for life outside work?</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101849 2026-08-18T09:33:49-05:00 2026-08-18T09:33:50-05:00 Finance Specialist <div>Join the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) Business Centers, where we strive to deliver exceptional service, innovative solutions, and responsible stewardship that advance IANR's teaching, research, and extension missions.</div><div><br>As a <strong>Finance Specialist </strong>with focus on financial management, you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial functions.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Managing an assigned portfolio, serving as a trusted advisor on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources including but not limited to state accounts, grants, service centers, and revolving accounts.</li><li>Supporting sponsored research through post-award grant financial management and administration.</li><li>Providing consultative guidance on university financial policies, sponsored programs, and business processes, helping departments navigate complex issues and identify practical, compliant solutions.</li><li>Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>We seek a collaborative, service-oriented professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate builds trusted relationships, communicates effectively with diverse stakeholders, and exercises sound judgment to make and communicate decisions that support responsible stewardship, compliance, and exceptional service.<br><br>This position is located on Nebraska Innovation Campus in Lincoln, NE. Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with a minimum of 3 days per week worked on campus. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Note:</strong> Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> NE Innovation Campus Business Ctr-3028 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102073 2026-08-27T16:46:31-05:00 2026-08-27T16:46:32-05:00 Quick Service Team Member: Slim Chickens (8:00am-4:30pm, M-F) <div>The <strong>Quick Service Team Member</strong> is an key position within Dining Services. This position will work within Abel Dining Center, which is one of the quick serve made to order concepts that relies on the mobile ordering platform for orders.<br><br>As a <strong>Quick Service Team Member</strong> you will:</div><ul><li>Provide excellent customer service</li><li>Perform all back of the house kitchen duties, including ingredient and food preparation, inventory, cooking and assembling orders, setting up and closing down stations, recipe preparation, dish machine operations and cleaning</li><li>Build orders based on established processes, procedures, guidelines and recipes</li><li>Monitor food quality, food presentation and control food waste</li><li>Assist within other areas as needed and other duties assigned</li></ul><div><br>This position is considered essential and may have weekend or evening shifts.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Housing: AS Dining Service-1135 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101548 2026-07-31T11:10:16-05:00 2026-07-31T11:10:17-05:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate <div>The Department of Entomology at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) is seeking applications for a highly motivated and enthusiastic postdoctoral research associate. This 12-month (calendar year), special appointment will lead multiple research projects on EPN and/or EPF, including but not limited to projects targeting corn rootworm in corn and red sunflower seed weevil and head moth in sunflower. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to grant proposal preparation, project reporting, presenting research results at scientific conferences, manuscript drafting and publishing, as well as mentoring graduate and undergraduate students. The postdoctoral research associate will have opportunities to assist with extension programing and material development if interested. The apportionment is 100% research. This position will be located in Scottsbluff, Nebraska.<strong> <br><br></strong>Research may require frequent travel to research sites throughout western Nebraska. The initial appointment is for a one-year term with the possibility to extend depending on performance and funding availability.<br><br></div><div>The postdoctoral research associate will be working under the supervision of the principal investigator, Dr. Pin-Chu Lai in the <a href=\"https://lai-lab-unlpreec-entomology.weebly.com/\"><strong>Crops IPM Entomology Lab</strong></a> at Panhandle Research, Extension and Education Center (PREEC). The program focuses on research in applied ecology, arthropod pest biology and management in major crops in the central high plains including sugar beets, dry beans, winter wheat, sunflower, corn, and alfalfa. Please visit the lab website for more information.</div><div><br></div><div>In addition to the above-described duties, the individual will be expected to accept committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</div><div><br></div><div>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and the Department of Entomology are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.</div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Entomology-0834 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101990 2026-08-25T11:05:05-05:00 2026-08-25T11:05:06-05:00 Homelessness Prevention Manager <div>Homelessness Prevention Manager will support the planning, launch, implementation, and ongoing operation of Nebraska’s Right at Home homelessness prevention initiative. The position will coordinate project timelines, provider readiness, community based service HUB technical assistance, service coordination, collaborate on HMIS operational workflows, payment processing via external common fund holder, evaluation support, and supervision of assigned Right at Home staff.<br><br></div><div>The position will work with UNL-CCFL Community Services leadership, Continuum of Care partners, participating HUBs, HMIS and Coordinated Entry staff, the Common Fund Holder, public-sector and philanthropic partners, Right at Home technical assistance partners, and evaluation partners. The position requires practical planning ability, disciplined follow-through, strong communication, careful documentation, and professional judgment in a complex, multi-partner implementation environment.<br><br><strong>About Us: </strong><br>https://community-services.unl.edu/<br><br>The University of Nebraska-Lincoln Center on Children, Families, and the Law works with public systems, nonprofit providers, and community partners to strengthen services for children, families, and vulnerable populations. Within CCFL, the Community Services Division supports homelessness response system planning, HMIS, Coordinated Entry, Continuum of Care work, technical assistance, data-informed planning, and implementation support across Nebraska.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> Ctr on Children Families & the Law-1082 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102185 2026-09-04T11:54:50-05:00 2026-09-04T11:54:50-05:00 Utility Operator <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. We invest in our staff by offering fantastic benefits like vacation, sick, and holiday pay, a variety of insurance options, retirement plans, and numerous others. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.<br><br><strong>As a Utility Operator, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Assess daily steam, electricity, and chilled water load demands and identify and operate equipment to meet campus needs.</li><li>Monitor plant equipment through observation, data analysis, and remote systems to ensure safe and reliable operation.</li><li>Observe and interpret equipment conditions (sound, vibration, temperature, pressure, flow, electrical readings) and make necessary adjustments.</li><li>Record data accurately in required written and electronic formats to meet regulatory and internal standards.</li><li>Communicate with team members to support coordinated operations, such as detailed shift turnover information, equipment status, load changes, operational issues, and corrective actions.</li><li>Submit and follow up on work orders for maintenance support.</li><li>Assist maintenance personnel with preventive maintenance and equipment repairs.</li></ul><div><br><em>Husker Energy and Power has five levels of Utility Operator positions. Placement within a specific level is based on a candidate’s demonstrated knowledge, skills, abilities, relevant experience, and required licensure. Operators at higher levels are assigned expanded responsibilities and more complex duties aligned with the scope and expectations of that level.<br><br></em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> UO Husker Energy & Power-12300 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101905 2026-08-19T10:40:47-05:00 2026-08-19T10:40:47-05:00 Financial Accountant II <div>The Financial Accountant II provides financial accounting oversight for the Utilities department projects and operations, Breslow Ice Hockey Center and the Service Centers at UNL. Perform and coordinate financial processes with all UNL Business Center staff. Assists senior management with budgeting, financial reporting and analyses. This position applies acumen and understanding of business concepts and processes to provide senior management with actionable decision making analytics. Will assist with other miscellaneous accounting functions, as needed or assigned.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Accounting-0977 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102118 2026-08-31T16:53:45-05:00 2026-08-31T16:53:46-05:00 Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide a variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle.</li><li>Maintain machinery and fences,</li><li>Assist with pasture management</li><li>Assist with the collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather is required. Due to the size of the facility, a valid driver's license and ability to meet University driver eligibility criteria is required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Learn more about UNL benefits and your total compensation at: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/99958 2026-03-26T14:26:33-05:00 2026-03-26T14:26:34-05:00 Seasonal Staff Positions (North Platte, NE; Temporary) <div>The West Central Research, Extension and Education Center (WCREEC) in North Platte, NE seeks motivated individuals to fill temporary seasonal roles in a variety of positions, including:<br><strong>Groundskeeping</strong></div><ul><li>Performing basic outdoor grounds maintenance and landscaping duties.</li></ul><div><strong>Facilities maintenance and custodial</strong></div><ul><li>Performing basic building or facility maintenance tasks such as painting, cleaning indoor or outdoor areas, repairing fences.</li></ul><div><strong>Farm/Crops Research Assistant</strong></div><ul><li>Perform basic crop management tasks including planting, weeding, data collection.</li></ul><div><strong>Livestock Research Assistant</strong></div><ul><li>Perform basic livestock management tasks including feeding, watering, cleaning pens.</li><li>Must be at least 18 years of age.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Full- and part-time positions available. Applications are continuously reviewed. <br>Within the UNL system, these positions are categorized as Temporary Office/Service Hourly positions.<br><br><strong>Temporary employees may be appointed for a period of up to two years. Temporary employees appointed for six months or less are not eligible for benefits. Those appointed for more than six months are eligible for benefits from the beginning of the appointment, provided the position is half-time (.50 FTE) or greater. Benefits for eligible temporary employees include the following: health, dental, vision, and life insurance. </strong><br><br>As an EO employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a></div> West Central Research, Extension and Education Center-0944 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101707 2026-08-10T11:33:59-05:00 2026-08-10T11:33:59-05:00 Program Coordinator (2 Positions Available) <div>The William H. Thompson Scholars (WHT) Learning Community provides academic and life skills support to recipients of the Susan Thompson Buffett Foundation Scholarship at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Grounded in the Ecology of Validation model, scholars are given opportunities to connect closely with staff, faculty, and peers through a sequence of shared academic courses, learning community activities, and advising.<br><br>WHT is an energetic and student success focused environment, with Program Coordinators primarily focusing on providing support through individualized meetings with program scholars throughout the academic year. Working collaboratively with program staff to uphold the mission and core values of the WHT program, a Program Coordinator utilizes a holistic approach to support scholars in academics, personal wellness, social development, and professional development. Program Coordinators oversee individualized academic probation programming, connecting closely with at-promise scholars. Staff are responsible for teaching several sections of a first-year seminar course during the fall term and assist with the training and supervision of a peer mentor team.<br><br>In addition to student support duties, Program Coordinators are assigned leadership responsibilities in areas such as: program diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts, social engagement, event planning, housing, study cafe, tutoring services, and education abroad. Administrative experience with maintaining databases is preferred.<br><br>Peer mentors have mobile accessibility outside of the normal working hours and community programming occasionally require night or weekend obligations.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Undergraduate Programs-2975 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102014 2026-08-25T11:32:36-05:00 2026-08-25T11:32:36-05:00 Assistant Coach - Women's Tennis <div>Assist Head coach in all aspects of running a Division I Women’s Tennis program. Position requires working irregular hours. Compliance with all institutional, conference, and NCAA rules. Attendance at all monthly compliance rules education meetings. Collaboration with all support areas who serve support program to ensure positive student-athlete experience. Represent self, team, and institution as a positive role- model and ambassador at all times. Engagement with and event planning for letterwinner alumni. Promote individual student-athlete and team achievements on social media.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Athletics-0850 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101389 2026-07-23T12:35:59-05:00 2026-07-23T12:36:00-05:00 Assistant Director, TRIO Student Support Services <div><strong>The Assistant Director of TRIO Student Support Services (SSS)</strong> makes a positive impact in the University’s students by providing leadership for programs that support the persistence, retention, and graduation of first-generation, low-income, and disabled University of Nebraska-Lincoln students.<br><br></div><div>The <strong>Assistant Director, TRIO Student Support Services</strong> will:</div><ul><li>Administer and implement innovative and high-impact programs and services for SSS participants to aid in retention and graduation</li><li>Collaborate with University and community partnerships that will achieve the grants objectives and outcomes</li><li>Promote the services available to SSS programs and recruit eligible students to participate in the program</li><li>Recruit, hire, train, and lead a staff of professional staff, graduate assistants, and student workers to fulfill the mission of Student Support Services</li><li>Assist in yearly administration of Student Support Services grant budget</li><li>Assess and monitor program data and outcomes. Assist in daily documentation for yearly Annual Performance Reporting</li></ul><div><br><br><strong>About Us: </strong><br>TRIO Programs at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln are federally-funded outreach programs that offer academic, social, cultural and financial support for first-generation and underserved scholars. We engage with students in middle school through college to help them achieve educational goals by completing a college degree and exploring advanced education.<br><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.<br><br></div> TRIO Programs-0962 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102190 2026-09-04T16:03:39-05:00 2026-09-04T16:03:39-05:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor <div>The University of Nebraska College of Law invites applications for entry-level and lateral candidates for multiple tenure-track or tenured faculty positions, depending on the candidate’s experience.<br><br>The primary course needs are First-Year Property and Federal Income Tax. Other course needs include Torts, Corporate Tax, Partnership Tax, Tax-related seminar, Professional Responsibility, Privacy Law, Constitutional Law, Cyber Security Law, Employee Benefits, Real Estate Transactions, Environmental Law, Administrative Law, Natural Resources Law, and Wills and Trusts.</div><div><br>General information about the Law College is available at <a href=\"https://law.unl.edu/\"><strong>https://law.unl.edu/</strong></a><strong>.</strong> <br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> College of Law-0899 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101035 2026-06-30T16:31:09-05:00 2026-06-30T16:31:10-05:00 Hospitality Service Associate (4:00am-12:30pm, Thurs-Mon) <div>At the University of Nebraska where every person and every interaction matters, the Hospitality Service team plays a meaningful role in maintaining safe, healthy, and welcoming environments for students, staff, faculty, and/or guests in a variety of settings.</div><div>In this role you will:</div><ul><li>Performs routine cleaning and upkeep across housing facilities</li><li>Maintains offices, residential halls, public areas, bathrooms, conference rooms, and dining centers</li><li>Ensures a clean, safe environment for all guests</li><li>Cleans hard floors and carpets</li><li>Mixes cleaning solutions as directed</li><li>Assists with event setup and conference operations as needed</li></ul><div>The Hospitality Services position may be hired at a higher level depending upon candidate qualifications.<br><br>Depending upon level assigned, this position may:</div><ul><li>Train and oversee work of others</li><li>Respond to on-call duties and other emergency situations during shifts</li><li>Use all non-riding and non-autonomous equipment</li><li>Order supplies</li></ul><div>When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Attendant</strong>, the position will receive continuous supervision and specific guidelines in the process of training and development.<br> <br> When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Assistant, Hospitality Services Associate or Hospitality Services Sr. Associate</strong> the position will routinely perform the skills associated with that level.<br><br> Performance will be continuously assessed to determine ability to perform these skills at an acceptable level.<br><br></div><div><strong>About Us:</strong> <br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment.</em></div> Campus Recreation-0965 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101875 2026-08-19T10:19:02-05:00 2026-08-19T10:19:02-05:00 Associate RDN (Registered Dietitian/Nutritionist) <div>The Associate RDN provides comprehensive nutrition services to the University of Nebraska Athletic Department and serves as a senior performance nutrition practitioner within the department. Primary responsibilities include developing, implementing, and evaluating nutrition strategies for student-athletes; overseeing fueling stations and, supporting sports dietitians and the student internship program; and collaborating with nutrition, sports medicine, strength and conditioning, psychological services, food service, and team staffs. The Associate RDN serves as a nutrition resource for student-athletes, coaches, staff, prospective student-athletes and their families, and other athletic department partners. This position works independently within established departmental policies and professional standards and assists the Director of Olympic Performance Nutrition &amp; Assistant AD for Performance Nutrition with program development, quality management, and continuous improvement. Perform any additional duties as assigned by the Director of Olympic Performance Nutrition &amp; Assistant AD for Performance Nutrition. Must be able to work a non-standard work week which may include nights, weekends, holidays, and travel if needed with team.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Athletics-0850 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102075 2026-08-27T17:04:50-05:00 2026-08-27T17:04:51-05:00 Quick Service Team Leader: Husker Heroes (3:30pm-12:00am, Sun-Thurs) <div>The <strong>Quick Service Team Leader</strong> will provide guidance and supervision within one of Abel Dining’s mobile order quick service concepts and ensure that orders are accurate, timely and up to the high standards of the University Dining Services.<br><br>The <strong>Quick Service Team Leader</strong> will:</div><ul><li>Provide outstanding customer service</li><li>Ensure that food quality meets and/or exceeds University Dining’s and franchise standards</li><li>Assign daily tasks and assignments to student workers and staff during their shift</li><li>Oversee work in kitchen, dish room, and/or dining area</li><li>Train student workers and staff on recipes, production processes, and University dining standards</li><li>Perform all tasks in all areas/functions, such as; setting up, closing down stations, food production, restocking, daily food prep, cashiering, taking inventory food waste management, cleaning and monitoring food quality</li><li>Troubleshoot and solve concerns directly with customers as they arise</li></ul><div><br>This position is considered essential and schedule may include weekend, evening, or early morning shifts.</div><div><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Housing: AS Dining Service-1135 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101608 2026-08-04T10:19:09-05:00 2026-08-04T10:19:10-05:00 Passport Agent <div>The passport agent will oversee and execute the passport application process and ensure all materials and documents needed to process the application are correctly submitted. The agent works independently screening evidence of U.S. Citizenship, recording application identification documentation, collecting and forwarding required passport fees and securing all personal identity information along with federal documents. Greeting applicants/customers, directing customers to desired service areas, assisting walk-in applicants using a computer based scheduling software and other duties as assigned.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace, it's a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:<br><br></div><div><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays<br><br></div><div><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life<br><br></div><div><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education<br><br></div><div><strong>Generous retirement plans </strong>with a university match<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Passport Office-10100 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101992 2026-08-25T11:08:19-05:00 2026-08-25T11:08:19-05:00 Residence Director <div>The <strong>Residence Director</strong> is vital for engaging with students that live in residence halls at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Residence Directors are empowered to connect with their residential community to help students become engaged members of the community and to thrive as students at UNL with the goal of achieving graduation. An individual in this position will serve on a dynamic team of professionals that work together at a Big 10 institution to implement the Nebraska Residential Experience curriculum framework.<br><br></div><div><strong>As a Residence Director you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Focus on student success, engagement, and leadership.</li><li>Oversee daily operations of a residence hall.</li><li>Lead a team of student leaders.</li><li>Gain valuable experience in a multitude of areas including community engagement, supervision, crisis response, leadership development, and summer conferences.</li><li>Participate in departmental committees, collaborate across campus and build partnerships and contribute to the campus mission.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Strong communication, collaboration, creativity, and adaptability are essential qualities for a Residence Director. This role encourages providing feedback on department and campus initiatives, expanding knowledge on best practices to support college students, and offers professional development opportunities. Residence Directors collaborate within a large department, making collective decisions, and ensuring an optimal residential experience for University of Nebraska-Lincoln students. In the summer, the role extends to community engagement through conference services. This multifaceted position emphasizes personal and professional growth within a supportive and collaborative environment.<br><br></div><div>This position is considered essential, and schedules include office hours, some evenings, weekends, and being available in an on-call rotation.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination<br></em></strong></a><br></div><div><br><br></div><div><br><br></div> Housing: Residence Directors-11951 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101420 2026-07-24T14:47:27-05:00 2026-07-24T14:47:27-05:00 Supervisor, Controls (Open to University Staff Only) <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska and certified as a Lincoln Family-Friendly workplace, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. <br><br><strong>We invest in our employees:</strong></div><ul><li>Vacation, sick, and holiday pay.</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance.</li><li>No-cost life insurance.</li><li>Employee Assistance Program.</li><li>Parental leave</li><li>Retirement plans.</li><li>Tuition assistance for employees and dependents.</li><li>Exclusive employee discounts.</li><li>Professional development through training and education.</li><li>And many more!!</li></ul><div><br><strong>As the Supervisor, Controls, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Implement operational priorities established by leadership and communicate work status, resource needs, escalated issues, and service updates as applicable.</li><li>Monitor work activity, system performance trends, alarms, and operational performance metrics, and recommend improvements to controls services, workflow efficiency, and service delivery.</li><li>Coordinate controls system installations, inspections, troubleshooting, repairs, maintenance activities, programming and commissioning support, and related work assignments across assigned staff and projects.</li><li>Review estimates, project information, sequences, graphics, trend data, work plans, and related documentation for accuracy, timeliness, and alignment with assigned priorities.</li><li>Assign work, monitor staffing coverage, and adjust daily work assignments to support service needs, project schedules, operational priorities, and emergency response.</li><li>Track service work, project activity, and assigned tasks to help ensure completion in alignment with scope, schedule, budget, quality, and service expectations.</li><li>Coordinate with campus departments and stakeholders to ensure controls activities align with operational needs, project schedules, and institutional priorities.</li><li>Oversee campus controls work, such as building automation systems, direct digital controls, system interfaces, related low-voltage controls applications, and operational integration with building systems, and ensure work is completed safely, efficiently, and in accordance with applicable standards.</li><li>Participate in facilities condition assessments and provide input on controls system needs, deficiencies, and priorities.</li><li>Identify operational needs and recommend improvements to procedures, equipment, technologies, programming practices, and contracted services to enhance reliability, safety, and service quality.</li><li>Support and monitor compliance with safety, environmental, health, accessibility, cyber and data security expectations as applicable, and other operational standards, and reinforce a culture of safety and accountability.</li><li>Assist with contract coordination, vendor communication, and review of contractor performance to help ensure performance aligns with specifications, budgets, schedules, and institutional standards.</li><li>Maintain collaborative relationships with campus stakeholders, communicate work priorities and project status, manage service expectations, and share feedback with leadership to support continuous improvement.</li><li>Promote and reinforce a people-centered culture that emphasizes safety, continuous learning, collaboration, customer service, community, and operational excellence.</li><li>Provide leadership and oversight of staff performance, such as setting goals, communicating expectations, delivering coaching and training, conducting evaluations, documenting performance, and recommending salary adjustments.</li></ul><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> UO Building Systems Maintenance-1004 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101909 2026-08-19T10:42:23-05:00 2026-08-19T10:42:23-05:00 Career Coach <div>The Career Coach will serve undergraduate students in the College of Arts &amp; Sciences to increase their understanding of and preparation for quality post-graduation opportunities. Primarily, the Career Coach will facilitate students’ self-exploration of interests, abilities, and values as well as their understanding of career options related to their academic programs, with special consideration of the unique needs of different populations, especially historically underserved first-generation, low-income, and ethnic minority students. Additionally, the Career Coach will emphasize the importance of experiential learning opportunities that will contribute to students’ readiness to successfully pursue those career options. Collaboration with advisors and faculty across the College as well as with UNL Career Services will help inform and guide this work. Through direct interaction with students in 1-1 coaching sessions, classroom and student organization presentations, and teaching of an elective career development/experiential learning course, the Career Coach will help students develop the ability to articulate their skills and qualifications in their resumes, cover letters and interviews as well as through networking activities both in-person and online. The Career Coach will also build and maintain relationships with employers and alumni.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> College of Arts & Sciences-0906 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102121 2026-09-01T09:49:31-05:00 2026-09-01T09:49:31-05:00 Proposal Development Specialist, Coordinator, or Senior Coordinator <div>The Office of Research and Innovation (R&amp;I) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) is committed to promoting a culture and environment for success in research, scholarship, creative endeavors, and economic development. Conducting novel and impactful research that generates new knowledge, solves real-world problems, and enhances lives is among the most fundamental purposes of the institution.<br><br>The Office of Proposal Development seeks to hire a Proposal Development professional at one of three levels: Specialist, Coordinator, or Senior Coordinator. This position joins a team of research development professionals to provide comprehensive proposal development assistance to UNL faculty, staff, and administrators.<br><br>The primary responsibilities of the proposal development specialist and coordinator are to edit single investigator and small group grant proposals and provide editorial support for colleagues developing large, complex proposals. In addition, the proposal development coordinator also manages the development of large-scale, collaborative proposals.<br><br></div><div>The primary responsibilities of the senior proposal development coordinator are coaching faculty about best practices for proposal writing; preparing faculty to network with program officers; co-authoring, reviewing, and refining individual investigator and small group grant applications; and managing the development of large-scale, collaborative proposals.</div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> Research Development-13276 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100083 2026-04-08T14:30:27-05:00 2026-04-08T14:30:27-05:00 Reference Librarian - Open Rank Professor <div>The University of Nebraska College of Law invites applications for the position of Reference Librarian (Open Rank Professor) at the Schmid Law Library. This 12-month, tenure-track law library faculty position offers an opportunity to support student learning and faculty scholarship while contributing to the mission and values of the College of Law.<br><br>This role offers an exciting opportunity to contribute meaningfully to legal education, research, and law library services in a dynamic academic setting. Members of the law library faculty participate in faculty governance at the College of Law and may apply for faculty development fellowships (sabbatical). Initial appointment and rank will be commensurate with experience.<br><br></div><div>Law library faculty will participate in the University’s generous benefits package. Please use this link to see the full range of benefits: <a href=\"https://hr.unl.edu/health-benefits/\"><strong>https://hr.unl.edu/health-benefits/</strong></a><strong>. </strong>General information about the Law College is available at <a href=\"http://law.unl.edu/\"><strong>http://law.unl.edu/</strong></a>.</div><div><br>As an EO employer, the University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, gender, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran or military status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> College of Law-0899 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101729 2026-08-10T16:51:16-05:00 2026-08-10T16:51:17-05:00 Dispatcher (2 positions available) <div>Are you someone who thrives under pressure, cares deeply about helping others, and enjoys using technology to solve real-world problems? Join our team as a <strong>Dispatcher</strong> and play a vital role in keeping our UNL community safe. You’ll be the critical link between callers in need and emergency responders—making a difference every shift.<br><br></div><div><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></div><ul><li>Answer emergency and non-emergency calls for police, fire, and EMS services</li><li>Use multi-line phones, radio systems, and computer-aided dispatch (CAD) tools to coordinate rapid response</li><li>Communicate clearly and calmly with callers and first responders during high-stress situations</li><li>Relay essential information to public safety officials and partner agencies</li><li>Maintain accurate records and reports</li><li>Complete six months of paid training</li></ul><div><br><strong>What Makes You a Great Fit</strong></div><ul><li>A strong commitment to serving your community</li><li>Excellent customer service and communication skills</li><li>Ability to stay calm, focused, and detail-oriented during urgent situations</li><li>Interest in technology and learning new systems</li><li>Skill at multitasking and adapting to frequent interruptions</li><li>Familiarity with campus and city geography (helpful but not required)</li><li>Ability to work a variety of schedules (overnights, weekends, special events, etc.)</li></ul><div><br><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></div><ul><li>Meaningful work that directly impacts community safety</li><li>Opportunities to build valuable skills in communication, technology, and crisis response</li><li>A supportive team environment where your professionalism and dedication are valued</li></ul><div><br>If you’re ready to be a steady voice in critical moments and serve your community with purpose, we encourage you to apply.<br><br></div><div><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace, it's a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> University Police-0823 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102017 2026-08-25T11:33:05-05:00 2026-08-25T11:33:06-05:00 Starbucks Shift Manager <div>The Nebraska City Union <strong>Starbucks Shift Manager </strong>serves as a member of the management team by providing leadership, direction and supervision to Team Members during their shift and ensuring a high – quality experience for guests. Our management team acts with integrity, honesty and knowledge that promotes the culture, values, and mission of Starbucks.</div><div><br>In this role you will:</div><ul><li>Deliver legendary customer service to all customers by acting with a customer comes first attitude, connecting with the customer and providing quality beverages, whole bean and food products consistently for all customers by adhering to all recipe and presentation standards</li><li>Follow Starbucks, UNL, health, safety, and sanitation operational policies and procedures, including those for cash handling and safety and security, to ensure the safety of all partners during each shift</li><li>Execute store operations during scheduled shifts, including opening and closing duties</li><li>Supervise and lead a team of baristas during the shift to ensure the delivery of legendary customer service for all customers</li><li>Create a positive learning environment by providing clear, specific, timely and respectful coaching, training and feedback to partners on shift to ensure operational excellence and to improve barista performance</li><li>Maintain regular and consistent attendance and punctuality</li><li>Develop positive relationships with shift team by understanding and addressing individual motivation, needs and concerns</li><li>Maintain and model a calm demeanor during periods of high volume or unusual events to keep store operating to a high standard and set a positive example for the shift team</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>About Us:<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: Starbucks-12428 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101063 2026-07-06T11:00:50-05:00 2026-07-06T11:00:51-05:00 Animal Health Technician (Ithaca, NE) <div>The Eastern Nebraska Research, Extension, and Education Center (ENREEC) in Ithaca, NE is situated just 30 minutes from Omaha and Lincoln, close to Fremont, Ashland, and Wahoo. Beef research conducted at ENREEC includes the Klosterman Feedlot Innovation Center, a state-of-the-art, commercial-scale feedlot research center.<br><br><strong>As an Animal Health Technician, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Supervise and assist with daily observation of all cattle for disease or injury and maintain related health records.</li><li>Supervise and assist with daily management of cattle grazing pastures or crop residues.</li><li>Meet with supervisors to plan cattle movements, grazing plans, and fencing projects.</li><li>Perform daily checks of fencing, feed, and water of grazing cattle.</li><li>Assist graduate students with data collection.</li><li>Construct and maintain fences, cattle handling facilities, and equipment.</li></ul><div><br>Outdoor work environment and irregular hours required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician III.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Animal Science-0830 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101878 2026-08-19T10:26:57-05:00 2026-08-19T10:26:57-05:00 Analytical Laboratory Analyst <div>The Food Allergy Research and Resource Program (FARRP) works to develop and provide the food industry with credible information, expert opinions, tools, and services relating to allergenic foods, novel foods, and food ingredients including genetically modified products. FARRP takes a comprehensive approach, working and collaborating with research institutions, governmental authorities, consumer groups, and scientific societies around the globe to improve the safety of food products for consumers. <br><br><strong>As an Analytical Laboratory Analyst, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Perform confidential analysis for trace amounts of allergenic foods using immunochemical methods.</li><li>Maintain detailed documentation, identify appropriate extraction procedures, perform methods evaluations and comparisons, and perform ancillary lab functions.</li><li>Assist in client and accreditation official’s audits to help maintain the lab’s ISO:17025 accreditation.</li></ul><div><br>Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as a Research Technologist II.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place ot build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Food Science & Technology-0836 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102084 2026-08-28T11:34:43-05:00 2026-08-28T11:34:44-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - 4-H Youth Development (Merrick County) <div><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></div><div>This position is based in Central City, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Merrick and Hamilton Counties. The major responsibility of this position is to provide regional leadership for Nebraska Extension’s 4-H and Youth Development Program. This extension professional is expected to interact closely with 4-H clientele in these communities and deliver programs in their geographic area.</div><div><br></div><div>The Positive Youth Development – 4-H extension professional will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home unit and the IANR as an effective scholar and citizen, including supporting student recruitment and IANR science literacy. In 4-H, we believe in the power of young people. We see that every child has valuable strengths and real influence to improve the world around us. We are America’s largest youth development organization, empowering nearly six million young people across the U.S. with the skills to lead for a lifetime. Nebraska Extension is an organization that values excellence and as a member of the Nebraska Extension team you will create and deliver world-class learning experiences focused on critical issues that empower Nebraskans to improve their lives.</div><div><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an open rank educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress towards and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%)</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., schools or community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs innovative, revenue-generating strategies to secure funding and develop partnerships that expand Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%)</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator </strong></a>document as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<ul><li>Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.</li><li>Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.</li><li>Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li></ul></li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective well-being and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See the <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>Notice of Nondiscrimination</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 7-12356 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101613 2026-08-04T12:20:50-05:00 2026-08-04T12:20:50-05:00 Finance/Grants Specialist (Open to University Staff Only) <div>As a <strong>Finance/Grants Specialist </strong>you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial and post-award grant administration functions.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Managing an assigned portfolio of accounts, advising on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources which may include state accounts, grants, service centers, and/or revolving accounts.</li><li>Supporting unit leadership in budget analysis, preparing reports and identifying potential areas of concern.</li><li>Providing consultative guidance on university financial policies, sponsored programs, and business processes, helping departments navigate complex issues and identify practical, compliant solutions.</li><li>Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions.</li><li>Preparing and reviewing standardized and ad hoc financial reports, ensuring accuracy and investigating and resolving anomalies.</li><li>Ensuring that records are maintained according to policy.</li><li>Collaborating with university partners to deliver exceptional service and promote effective, compliant business services.</li></ul><div><br>Following an initial onsite training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule with 3-4 days per week working on campus. All hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Note:</strong> Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. <br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> Oldfather Business Cooperative-10225 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101995 2026-08-25T11:13:47-05:00 2026-08-25T11:13:48-05:00 Academic Services Specialist <div>The Academic Services Specialist will perform detailed verifications of major, minor, and degree requirements for the undergraduate colleges using the degree management system while maintaining a well-developed knowledge of degree requirements and office procedures. This position will work with college deans’ offices, faculty, and advisers concerning students’ graduation requirements and substitution/waivers. Perform accurate and timely proofing of graduation related materials including diplomas and program content, and assist with commencement preparations and ceremony student check-in.<br><br></div><div>In addition, the Academic Services Specialist will provide overall registrar customer service support to the campus by helping students with the enrollment process, troubleshooting issues and alleviating concerns. Support the campus community in connecting degree requirements, degree pathway building, and enrollment. Provide student customer service for transcripts, verifications, and other needed documents. Assist Faculty and Staff with questions regarding class schedule, grading, and other inquiries. This position will provide support for general office customer service duties related to academic services via phone, email, and other means of communication.<br><br>The Academic Services Specialist will maintain students’ academic records. Scan images of student records into the document retention system. Review transfer credit and other documentation in students’ academic records. Additional duties as assigned.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Office of the University Registrar-0961 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101430 2026-07-27T08:35:36-05:00 2026-07-27T08:35:37-05:00 Financial Accountant II <div>Manage institutional commitments, provide financial reports, reconcile accounts and coordinate special projects. Serve as the lead accountant and primary contact between the State of Nebraska and the University of Nebraska financial system (SAP). Must be able to analyze and problem solve reconciliation items. Record revenue internal billings transactions, batch upload files into SAP, reconciliations, miscellaneous journal entries, and year-end closing duties. Review cost center requests and determine the appropriate master data elements needed to accurately input in SAP and for appropriate financial statement presentation. Other miscellaneous accounting functions as needed or assigned.<br><br>As an EO employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</div> Accounting-0977 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101936 2026-08-20T12:28:42-05:00 2026-08-20T12:28:43-05:00 Media Services Supervisor <div>The Media Services Supervisor provides front-line technical and operational supervision for Nebraska Public Media’s Media Services department, including television, radio, and streaming traffic operations, underwriting contract services, metadata support, asset registration, and the Media Services Helpdesk. This position trains, supports, and supervises Media Services staff in the daily use of scheduling, automation, metadata, asset management, and related media delivery systems to ensure accurate broadcast logs, timely spot placement, reliable streaming support, and continuity of services.</div><div><br>The position supports implementation of approved systems, workflows, and process changes; troubleshoots operational and technical issues; assists with rights management, playlist, distribution, and metadata compliance; and serves as a working supervisor to maintain operational coverage when needed. This role works under the direction of Media Operations leadership to ensure Media Services processes are carried out consistently, accurately, and in alignment with established standards and organizational needs.</div><div><br>Nebraska Public Media offers a full spectrum of communications services to the citizens of Nebraska, the nation and the world. Some of these services include a nine-station, statewide noncommercial public television network affiliated with PBS; a nine-station, statewide noncommercial public radio network affiliated with NPR; a cutting-edge Digital Media Group; and state-of-the-art audio, video and multimedia production capability delivered via broadcast, satellite, cable, Internet and broadband delivery channels.</div><div><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> University Television-0912 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102137 2026-09-01T14:56:33-05:00 2026-09-01T14:56:33-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Health and Wellbeing (Hamilton County) <div><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></div><div>This position is based in Aurora, Nebraska, with a geographic accountability region of Hamilton, Merrick, Clay, Nuckolls, Thayer, and Fillmore Counties.<br><br></div><div>The Health &amp; Wellbeing Extension professional engages Nebraskans through research-based education, partnerships, and community-based approaches that help people live healthier, safer, and more resilient lives. The educator identifies local and regional needs, connects Nebraskans with the resources, research, and innovation of the University of Nebraska, and provides programming that creates meaningful and measurable impact.<br><br></div><div>As part of Nebraska Extension's Health &amp; Wellbeing program area, the educator delivers and contributes to educational programs that address identified needs of individuals, families, and communities and align with current program area priorities. Priority areas may include nutrition, physical activity, chronic disease prevention and management, mental wellbeing, food science and safety, food and nutrition security, and approaches that create healthier communities.<br><br></div><div>The educator works collaboratively with Extension professionals, University faculty and specialists, community organizations, healthcare and public health partners, and other local and statewide partners to translate research into practice, expand access to trusted educational resources, and increase the reach and impact of health and wellbeing programming across the lifespan.<br><br></div><div>Through education, strong local connections, and evaluation of program outcomes, the educator contributes to lasting impact for individuals, families, and communities across Nebraska.</div><div><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate-level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress toward and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%):</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., health and wellbeing, and community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs innovative, revenue-generating practices to secure funding and develop partnerships that expand Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximagely 20%):</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator document </strong></a>as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<ul><li>Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.</li><li>Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.</li><li>Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li></ul></li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br></div><div>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br></div><div>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor a temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See the <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>Notice of Nondiscrimination</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 7-12356 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100201 2026-04-20T09:59:40-05:00 2026-04-20T09:59:41-05:00 Lecturer (German Language) <div>The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures at UNL seeks a full-time, one-year lecturer to teach German language and culture classes at the 100 (introductory) through 400 (advanced undergraduate) levels.<strong> </strong>The proposed load for the 2026-2027 academic year is eight (8) courses (approximately 24 credit hours) over two semesters. The proposed salary range is $42,000 (M.A.) - $45,000 (Ph.D.). The department is unable to sponsor visa applications for this position.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See<a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Modern Language & Literature-1090 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101742 2026-08-11T10:43:06-05:00 2026-08-11T10:43:06-05:00 Prototype Fabrication and Lab Manager <div>The Department of Chemical &amp; Biomolecular Engineering at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is a dynamic, research-driven community advancing innovations across biomolecular engineering, nanotechnology, biotechnology, and molecular medicine. Students, staff, and faculty collaborate on cutting-edge, grant-funded research that addresses critical challenges in healthcare, sustainability, and advanced materials.<br><br><strong>As the Prototype Fabrication &amp; Lab Manager, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Collaborate with faculty, graduate students, and undergraduate researchers to conceptualize, design, fabricate, and refine custom experimental apparatus that support novel research projects, where commercially available equipment may not exist.</li><li>Assist with the design, fabrication, maintenance, and repair of laboratory equipment and devices.</li><li>Ensure that the teaching and research labs in the Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering meet the needs of the department, faculty, staff, and students.</li><li>Coordinate with Environmental Health and Safety and OSHA to ensure compliance with all safety requirements and eliminate safety hazards.</li></ul><div><br>In the UNL system, this position is categorized as a Lab Mechanic. <br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br>Note: </strong>Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Chemical & Biomolecular Engineering-1058 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102020 2026-08-25T11:33:24-05:00 2026-08-25T11:33:25-05:00 Hospitality Service Leader <div>University Housing is looking for a motivated, caring individual to join our team working daytime hours in a student residential community. We are looking for a <strong>Hospitality Service Leader</strong> to supervise a team of up to seven custodians responsible for maintaining the cleanliness of residential floors and public areas according to established standards. In this role, you will help ensure students have a clean, safe, and welcoming living environment.<br><br></div><div>As a <strong>Hospitality Service Leader,</strong> you will:</div><ul><li>Clean areas such as bathrooms, public lounges, laundry rooms, stairwells, dining room, tile floors and carpeting</li><li>Fill in for staff absences</li><li>Supervise full-time regular and student employees in cleaning residence hall facilities</li><li>Assisting in custodial training</li><li>Manage supply distribution and inventory control</li><li>Coordinate the transition from academic year schedules to summer conference schedules smoothly</li></ul><div><br><strong>May be required to be on-call during evening and weekend hours.</strong> <br><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br>When you join our team as a regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing Facilities Custodial-11051 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101997 2026-08-25T11:16:28-05:00 2026-08-25T11:16:28-05:00 Electrician <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. We invest in our staff by offering fantastic benefits like vacation, sick, and holiday pay, a variety of insurance options, retirement plans, and numerous others. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. <br><br>Building Systems Maintenance has four levels of Electricians, and the level is determined by a candidate’s knowledge, skills, abilities, and applicable licensure. <br><br><strong>Electrician I, II, III, and IV</strong>: Assist with the installation, alteration, addition, maintenance, troubleshooting, and/or repair of electrical systems, lighting controls, access control systems, building security systems, fire alarm systems, and building automation controls systems. You will learn to interpret and use schematics and blueprint drawings to complete the installation and troubleshooting of electrical conduit systems, wiring, and device termination, and ensure compliance with regulations. <br><br><strong>Electrician II</strong>: In addition to the duties and responsibilities above, a level II will work more independently and be given more complex duties, including testing electrical systems and continuity of circuits in electrical wiring, equipment, and fixtures, using basic features of testing devices.<br><br><strong>Electrician III</strong>: In addition to the duties and responsibilities above, a level III will confirm scope, schedule, and budget requirements of work assignments and coordinate changes, and communicate and coordinate with outside vendors and manufacturers relative to electrical equipment and systems.<br><br><strong>Electrician IV:</strong> In addition to the duties and responsibilities above, a level IV will provide as-built documentation at the completion of projects, coordinate work and schedules with supervisors, staff, contractors, building occupants, project managers, and engineers, train, mentor, and verify work of other staff, students, temp, and/or on-call personnel, and assist with project development, employee training, and safety coordination.<br><br>All levels will be assigned to a rotating on-call schedule and urgent situations occasionally require after-hours work.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> UO Building Systems Maintenance-1004 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101086 2026-07-07T13:22:26-05:00 2026-07-07T13:22:26-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Water & Cropping Systems (Platte Co.) <div><strong>Overview </strong><br>This position is based in Columbus, NE with the geographic accountability region of Platte, Boone, and Nance counties. The educator serves as a trusted, research-based educational leader connecting the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, the agricultural industry, and Nebraska communities through practical, science-based extension programming and applied research.</div><div>Primary responsibilities are developing and delivering impactful water and cropping systems extension programming that: a) improves agricultural profitability and sustainability, b) reduces environmental risk, c) encourages natural resources stewardship, d) enhances agricultural resiliency, and e) expands public understanding of food, forage, grain, and fiber production systems.</div><div>The educator translates complex research into practical, solution-based educational experiences for diverse audiences including farmers, ranchers, agribusiness professionals, community leaders, and the general public. Educational delivery methods may include workshops, field demonstrations, applied research trials, digital resources, consultations, media outreach, and collaborative partnerships.<br><br></div><div>As a member of the statewide Water and Cropping Systems team, the educator actively contributes to the development of innovative, research-based resources and interdisciplinary solutions addressing current and emerging agricultural challenges for their assigned region and across Nebraska. The position requires collaboration with university faculty, extension colleagues, industry partners, agencies, and local stakeholders to identify needs and deliver responsive programming.<br><br></div><div>The educator is expected to maintain a visible and engaged presence within the communities they serve and become a recognized first source of trusted, unbiased agricultural information. Success in this role requires strong teaching and communication skills, community engagement, relationship building, leadership in agricultural education, and the ability to foster meaningful partnerships that support Nebraska agriculture and rural communities.<br><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate-level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an open rank educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress toward and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%)</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., on-farm, ranch, or community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs entrepreneurial practices to obtain funding and partnerships, enhancing Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%)</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator</strong></a> document as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<br>o Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.<br>o Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.<br>o Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.<br><br></li></ul><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission. <br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 7-12356 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101884 2026-08-19T10:29:24-05:00 2026-08-19T10:29:25-05:00 Recruitment Specialist, College of Engineering <div>At the University of Nebraska’s College of Engineering, our mission is to train the next generation engineering workforce and solve problems of global importance. <br><br><strong>As a Recruitment Specialist, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Plan, implement and assess recruitment and outreach programs and efforts.</li><li>Implement strategies to attract students, locally and nationally, to the College of Engineering.</li><li>Work with prospective students, current students, faculty and staff in an intensive customer service environment.</li><li>Coordinate college campus visits, recruitment events and programming, and analyze applicant data as it relates to College of Engineering programs.</li><li>Work with members of the college to develop and deliver outreach programming and develop graduate recruitment strategy.</li><li>Work with the College of Engineering Director of Recruitment to analyze recruitment data and develop and initiate innovative strategies for recruitment of students.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Position requires understanding and sensitivity regarding diverse student populations; a high level of professionalism; and commitment to teamwork. Evening and weekend work will be required.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> College of Engineering-0907 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102089 2026-08-28T13:25:01-05:00 2026-08-28T13:25:02-05:00 Graduate Program Coordinator <div>As the <strong>Graduate Program Coordinator</strong>, you will:</div><ul><li>Serve as the primary coordinator for graduate student support and provide general office management for the School combining Entomology and Plant Pathology, with primary responsibility for the Entomology graduate program and associated academic and administrative functions.</li><li>Support prospective, incoming, and current M.S. and Ph.D. students throughout the graduate student life cycle.</li><li>Coordinate admissions, onboarding, assistantships, fellowships, scholarships, records, academic scheduling, and Graduate Committee activities</li><li>Serve as a key point of contact for graduate students.</li><li>Provide general office, building, event, and customer-service support to ensure effective daily operations of the School.</li></ul><div><br>This position is located on UNL's East Campus in Lincoln, NE. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Office Associate.<br><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. <br><strong><br>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time </strong>off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance </strong>options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><strong><em><br></em></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> Entomology-0834 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101619 2026-08-04T13:43:58-05:00 2026-08-04T13:43:59-05:00 Recruitment Coordinator & Academic Advisor <div>The Department of Biological Systems Engineering (BSE) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is a nationally recognized, comprehensive program with over 100 years of excellence in teaching, research, and extension.<br><br>As a <strong>Recruitment Coordinator and Academic Advisor</strong>, you will:</div><ul><li>Create and implement a strategic plan for marketing and recruitment of students into the Agricultural Systems Technology, Agricultural Engineering, and Biological Systems Engineering majors.</li><li>Conduct individual campus visits, school visits, and participate in statewide recruitment events to promote the Department and recruit prospective and transfer students.</li><li>Build and maintain strong relationships with high schools, community colleges, counselors, teachers, Extension Educators, alumni, and industry. stakeholders to strengthen recruitment pipelines</li><li>Coordinate on-campus recruitment activities and collaborate with the Recruitment Committee, Student Ambassadors, and other university partners to support engagement efforts.</li><li>Advise undergraduate students in one or more of the assigned majors and support advising efforts across the Department.</li><li>Provide support for recruits during the application and admission process, including new student enrollment, and manage the undergraduate recruitment data and reporting functions for the Department.</li></ul><div><br>Some travel is required, including evenings and weekends as needed for recruitment activities.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Biological Systems Engineering-0833 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101432 2026-07-27T09:39:14-05:00 2026-07-27T09:39:14-05:00 Virology Research Technologist II <div>The Nebraska Veterinary Diagnostic Center (NVDC) is a tier 1 USDA National Animal Health Laboratory Network (NAHLN) veterinary diagnostic laboratory fully accredited by the American Association of Veterinary Laboratory Diagnosticians. The NVDC employs state-of-the-art testing procedures to provide disease surveillance and diagnostic services to veterinarians, livestock producers, pet owners and researchers.<strong><br></strong><br></div><div><strong>As the Virology Research Technologist II, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Prepare samples and conduct virology, serology, and molecular diagnostic testing.</li><li>Determine, prepare, and analyze results for serology, virology and rabies testing and ensure compliance with federal programs.</li><li>Design, validate, and implement new diagnostic testing, as needed.</li><li>Review results in the Vetview system and prepare reports for veterinarians, pathologists and other clientele, including charting and monitoring data for the lab’s quality control systems.</li><li>Write, review, and revise standard operating procedures for final approval by the lab manager and faculty.</li><li>Be responsible for quality control of assays and continual improvement of documents and procedures that are part of the quality control and management systems.<br><br></li></ul><div>Following hire, the incumbent will need to obtain and maintain compliance with all applicable requirements for working with pathogens including proficiency testing and accreditation requirements from a variety of regulatory bodies. This position is responsible for following all applicable safety and infection control procedures.<br><br>Irregular hours, including evenings, weekends, and holidays may occasionally be required in situations of outbreak response and to ensure required turnaround times. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as a Research Technologist II.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> Vet Diagnostic Center-7278 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101949 2026-08-21T08:10:14-05:00 2026-08-21T08:10:15-05:00 Operations Coordinator- Scholar Programs <div><strong>The Peter Kiewit Foundation Engineering Academy </strong>provides income eligible students with the resources and support to pursue careers in engineering, computing, and construction, shaping the future workforce of Nebraska. The Engineering Academy seeks to recruit and retain all students in the program. Students must demonstrate interest and commitment to the advancement of women in engineering, computing, or construction.<br><br></div><div>We envision a future where all students achieve long-term economic success through rewarding careers in engineering, computing, and construction.<br><br></div><div><strong>As the Operations Coordinator, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide wide-ranging service to Scholar Programs operations</li><li>Serve as the front line contact for prospective and current scholars, scheduling interviews for scholar candidates</li><li>Assist with event planning</li><li>Aid in scholarship distribution and administration</li><li>Serve as a key professional in the management and logistics of the program</li></ul><div><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> College of Engineering-0907 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102142 2026-09-02T08:20:45-05:00 2026-09-02T08:20:46-05:00 Catering Server <div>The University Catering team is dedicated to delivering exceptional culinary experiences and outstanding guest service at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln. We are seeking a motivated <strong>Catering Server</strong> to join our team and help create memorable events through excellent service and teamwork. <br><br>As a <strong>Catering Server</strong> you will:</div><ul><li>Supervise catering event operations, including event setup, service, and cleanup for university dining events</li><li>Provide exceptional customer service to guests while ensuring a positive and welcoming dining experience</li><li>Coordinate the transportation, preparation, and management of food items and supplies for catered events and special meals</li><li>Hire, schedule, train, and lead support staff, including student employees, to ensure efficient event operations</li><li>Assist with menu planning, event coordination, and preparation to support successful catering services</li></ul><div><br><br></div><div><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: Catering-12429 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100334 2026-04-30T14:02:28-05:00 2026-04-30T14:02:28-05:00 Co-Director - Digital Research (Part-time, Open to CAS Faculty Only) <div>We seek applications and nominations for the CAS Co-Director of the Center for Digital Research in the Humanities (CDRH). The successful candidate will report to the CAS Dean at UNL, and the expected 1.0 FTE appointment will be split as 0.25 FTE administration with 0.75 FTE faculty.<br><br></div><div>Primary areas of responsibility are shared with the Libraries CDRH Co-Director and will likely include:</div><ul><li><strong>Administrative &amp; Financial Leadership</strong> Oversee Center operations, consult on budgets, prepare required reports, and assume additional responsibilities consistent with the Center’s mission.</li><li><strong>Strategic Planning &amp; Program Coordination</strong> Lead strategic planning efforts and provide overall coordination for Center programs, personnel, and space.</li><li><strong>Personnel Management &amp; Evaluation</strong> Provide input on staff performance and faculty merit, reappointment, tenure, and promotion as requested or as required by appointment letters.</li><li><strong>Research, Teaching &amp; Faculty Engagement </strong>Encourage and support CDRH Fellows’ research and teaching aligned with the Center’s mission, including consultation on funding opportunities.</li><li><strong>Advancement, Communication &amp; Outreach</strong> Assist in fundraising efforts with University leadership; communicate Center activities and developments transparently to the CDRH community and relevant Deans.</li><li><strong>Governance &amp; Representation</strong> Convene and chair Center meetings; represent the Center at College of Arts and Sciences Chairs and Directors meetings; report regularly to the Dean of UNL Libraries and the Dean of the College of Arts and Sciences.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> College of Arts & Sciences-0906 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101785 2026-08-12T17:21:42-05:00 2026-08-12T17:21:43-05:00 Immune Metabolism Modeling Scientist (Temporary) <div>As an <strong>Immune Metabolism Modeling Scientist</strong>, you will:</div><ul><li>Lead the development, validation, and application of genome-scale metabolic models using in-house computational tools.</li><li>Integrate transcriptomics, proteomics, metabolomics, lipidomics, and other omics data to contextualize metabolic models and investigate complex biological questions.</li><li>Interpret modeling and multi-omics results to identify biological mechanisms, generate hypotheses, and guide research direction.</li><li>Provide technical expertise and mentorship to students, research staff, postdoctoral researchers, and collaborators.</li><li>Contribute to manuscripts, grant proposals, research presentations, and professional conferences.</li></ul><div>Within the UNL system, this position is categorized an a M/P Temp Worker. <br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br><strong>Temporary employees may be appointed for a period of up to two years. Those appointed for more than six months are eligible for benefits from the beginning of the appointment, provided the position is half-time (.50 FTE) or greater. Those appointed for six months or less are not eligible for benefits.</strong></div><div><br>Benefits for eligible temporary employees include:</div><ul><li>Paid time off including vacation and sick leave</li><li>Comprehensive insurance options including health, dental, vision, and life insurance</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> Biochemistry-0831 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102023 2026-08-25T11:33:45-05:00 2026-08-25T11:33:45-05:00 Digital Marketing Specialist <div>The Digital Marketing Specialist executes Nebraska Public Media’s digital marketing campaigns across paid search, paid social, programmatic advertising, and audience targeting platforms. Reporting to the Marketing &amp; Audience Development Manager, this position implements approved campaign strategies, manages the Google Ad Grant program, builds and monitors paid campaigns, and leads digital promotional execution for assigned initiatives.<br><br></div><div>This role focuses on tactical campaign execution, paid media management, digital advertising operations, performance tracking, and coordination of promotional deliverables to support goals of the Communications &amp; Engagement Department and overall strategic priorities.<br><br></div><div>Nebraska Public Media offers a full spectrum of communications services to the citizens of Nebraska. Some of these services include a statewide noncommercial public television network affiliated with PBS; statewide noncommercial public radio network affiliated with NPR; a cutting-edge Digital Media Group; and state-of-the-art audio, video and multimedia production capability delivered via broadcast, satellite, cable, Internet and broadband delivery channels. <br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> University Television-0912 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101649 2026-08-05T15:12:48-05:00 2026-08-05T15:12:49-05:00 Finance/Grant Specialist (Lincoln or Omaha, NE) <div>At the University of Nebraska’s College of Engineering, our mission is to train the next generation engineering workforce and solve problems of global importance. We’re one college in two cities (Lincoln and Omaha) on three campuses. This position can be officed in either Lincoln or Omaha, NE.<br><br>As a <strong>Finance/Grants Specialist,</strong> you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial functions.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Managing an assigned portfolio of accounts, advising on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources which may include state accounts, grants, service centers, and/or revolving accounts.</li><li>Supporting sponsored research through post-award grant financial management and administration.</li><li>Providing consultative guidance on university financial policies, sponsored programs, and business processes, helping departments navigate complex issues and identify practical, compliant solutions.</li><li>Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions.</li><li>Preparing and reviewing standardized and ad hoc financial reports, ensuring accuracy and investigating and resolving anomalies.</li><li>Providing direction to other staff on financial or grants-related issues.</li><li>Ensuring that records are maintained according to policy.</li></ul><div><br>Following an initial onsite training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule consisting of four days per week in the office and one remote workday. All hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Note: </strong>Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> College of Engineering-0907 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102002 2026-08-25T11:24:25-05:00 2026-08-25T11:24:26-05:00 Electrician I (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility located near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As an Electrician I, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with the installation, alteration, addition, maintenance, troubleshooting, and/or repair of electrical systems, lighting controls, access control systems, building security systems, fire alarm systems, and building automation control systems.</li><li>Learn to interpret and use schematics and blueprint drawings to complete the installation and troubleshooting of electrical conduit systems, wiring, and device termination, and ensure compliance with regulations.</li><li>Urgent situations occasionally require after-hours work.</li></ul><div><br>Electricians are assigned to a rotating, on-call schedule.&nbsp;<br><br>This position requires registration as a Nebraska Apprentice Electrician upon hire. There is no exam to obtain an apprentice card.&nbsp;</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101090 2026-07-07T15:35:20-05:00 2026-07-07T15:35:21-05:00 Building Access Associate <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska and certified as a Lincoln Family-Friendly workplace, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.<br><br><strong>We invest in our employees:</strong></div><ul><li>Vacation, sick, and holiday pay.</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance.</li><li>No-cost life insurance.</li><li>Employee Assistance Program.</li><li>Parental leave</li><li>Retirement plans.</li><li>Tuition assistance for employees and dependents.</li><li>Exclusive employee discounts.</li><li>Professional development through training and education.</li><li>And many more!!</li></ul><div><br>The Building Access Associate will process all incoming requests and inquiries, via phone and email, regarding University access systems. Maintain up to date system knowledge to provide high level end-user customer service, as well as filling the role of central contact for all University key managers regarding inquiries, issues, and requests. Administer processes and analyze system issues as they arise to explore alternatives and provide solutions while maintaining security and system efficiency.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> University Police-0823 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101886 2026-08-19T10:30:16-05:00 2026-08-19T10:30:16-05:00 Recruitment Specialist <div>A recruitment specialist is a critical role focused on helping students, families, and supporters navigate the path to college. This individual will take a proactive role in supporting all efforts to grow new student enrollment but will have specific territories or populations of focus assigned specifically to them. A recruitment specialist is responsible for implementing recruitment strategy within assigned territory and provide regular updates to their supervisor and the Admissions Leadership Team. Recruitment specialists will utilize recruitment tactics to effectively provide college counseling to prospective students and their parents. Recruitment specialists are responsible for presenting the benefits of UNL to prospective students and their families within assigned territory. This position will represent UNL at high school visits, college fairs, community college visits, as well as on campus at events, daily visits, community engagement activities, and on-call. This role will interact with students and families in person, over the phone, and via email, or approved SMS messaging. The Recruitment Specialist may be responsible for additional projects connected to recruitment and admissions. This individual is responsible for interpreting admission, financial aid, and university policy to the general public. The individual will utilize data and access various systems to help the university meet enrollment goals. The individual will need the ability to understand the unique needs of students from all backgrounds throughout the enrollment experience. This position may require extensive travel depending upon focus areas of the recruitment funnel and assigned territory. This position requires many nights and weekends during peak times.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Admissions-0959 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102095 2026-08-28T16:11:04-05:00 2026-08-28T16:11:04-05:00 Disability Coordination Specialist (Open to University Staff Only) <div>The <strong>Disability Coordination Specialist </strong>provides support to the UNL community by providing outreach and assistance.<br><br></div><div>The <strong>Disability Coordination Specialist</strong> provides direct assistance to students with disabilities by:</div><ul><li>Setting up accommodations.</li><li>Assisting in the coordination of accommodations with Faculty/Staff.</li><li>Following up with students about their accommodations they are using.</li><li>Participating in campus activities that would involve students with disabilities.</li><li>Providing outreach and education to students, faculty, staff and parents on the services offered and resources available.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>. <strong><br></strong><br></div> Svcs for Students with Disabilities-0966 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102036 2026-08-26T07:45:27-05:00 2026-08-26T07:45:27-05:00 Creative Media Specialist <div>Create visual content that will be used for both print and digital applications. Among the responsibilities are: working with the Communications staff to develop, maintain and advance the athletics department brand identity through its various printed and digital publications, which include, but are not limited to: social media channels, official athletics website, media guides, game programs, posters, tickets and newsletters. Work with various sports and communications staff to create digital content across a variety of platforms to advance the brand identity of the Nebraska Department of Athletics. Work with the Creative and Emerging Media Department as part of a team to continue to develop and push the future brand of Nebraska.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Athletics-0850 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101447 2026-07-27T13:15:45-05:00 2026-07-27T13:15:46-05:00 Fire Life Safety Technician <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska, the University of Nebraska Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. We invest in our staff by offering fantastic benefits like vacation, sick, and holiday pay, a variety of insurance options, retirement plans, and numerous others. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. <br><br>Building Systems Maintenance has three levels of Fire Life Safety Technicians, and the level is determined by a candidate’s knowledge, skills, abilities, and applicable licensure. <br><br><strong>Fire Life Safety Technician I, II, and III:</strong> All Fire Life Safety Technicians assist with the installation, alteration, addition, maintenance, troubleshooting, and/or repair of fire life safety systems, interpret and use schematics and blueprint drawings to complete the installation and troubleshooting of wiring and device termination of fire life safety systems, ensure compliance with regulations such as applicable building, electrical, and fire codes, and university and departmental standards and guidelines, and complete work orders and utilize an electronic timekeeping system daily. <br><br><strong>Fire Life Safety Technician II</strong>: In addition to the duties and responsibilities above, a level II will work more independently and be given more complex duties such as to project and maintenance support of fire alarm panel device control and manipulation for system troubleshooting and shutdown, test low-voltage electrical systems and continuity of circuits in electrical wiring and equipment with testing devices to ensure compatibility and functionality of the system, collaborate and coordinate to ensure building code compliance, and perform inspection and acceptance testing of fire alarm systems. <br><br><strong>Fire Life Safety Technician III</strong>: In conjunction with the duties and responsibilities above, a level III installs and configures fire life safety systems networking communication and alarm monitoring system setup, assists with project development, employee training, and safety coordination, generates activity and outage notifications, coordinates and performs interfacing of auxiliary fire life safety systems, and confirms scope, schedule, and budget requirements of work assignments. A level 3 also communicates and coordinate with outside vendors and manufacturers relative to electrical equipment and systems, coordinates project changes and provide as-built documentation at the completion of the project, trains, mentors, and verifies work of others, contributes to fostering a positive work environment, motivates and encourages staff to improve, supports leadership, and contributes to the development and implementation of departmental vision and goals.<br><br>All levels will be assigned to a rotating on-call schedule and urgent situations occasionally require after-hours work.<br><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> UO Building Systems Maintenance-1004 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101953 2026-08-21T09:09:30-05:00 2026-08-21T09:09:31-05:00 Assistant to the Dean <div>The Hixson-Lied College of Fine and Performing Arts at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln is a vibrant community of artists, scholars, and educators committed to excellence in creative expression, academic inquiry, and public engagement. Home to nationally recognized programs in music, theatre, film, dance, visual art, and design, the College fosters interdisciplinary collaboration, innovation, and a deep connection between the arts and society.<br><br><strong>As the Assistant to the Dean, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide high-level administrative and strategic support to the Dean of the Hixson-Lied College of Fine and Performing Arts.</li><li>Function as a key advisor, project manager, and liaison to internal and external stakeholders.</li><li>Play a critical role in managing the execution of strategic initiatives, overseeing operational activities in the Dean’s Office, coordinating college-wide events and communications, travel, and supervising student support staff.</li><li>Exercise substantial independent judgment and discretion, managing multiple complex priorities while fostering a professional, inclusive, and service-oriented environment.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>This role requires a deep understanding of the College’s mission, its academic and artistic programs, and the ability to anticipate the needs of the Dean in a dynamic, highly visible setting. In the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Administrative Assistant.<br><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Hixson Lied Fine & Performing Arts-0898 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102172 2026-09-03T13:27:08-05:00 2026-09-03T13:27:09-05:00 Outreach Specialist <div>Are you passionate about making sure first-generation and income-eligible scholars know that a program built for them exists? Join our team as our <strong>Outreach Specialist</strong> and be the reason they find us.</div><div><br>As the<strong> Outreach Specialist</strong>, you will:</div><ul><li>Serve as the spokesperson for ETS (Educational Talent Search) in the community.</li><li>Build strong relationships with middle school and high school Counselors, teachers, and staff that will assist with identifying eligible students.</li><li>Meet with prospective students and families, answer questions and assist with the application process.</li><li>Conduct parent and community outreach, including information sessions and presentations.</li><li>Maintain accurate recordkeeping of recruitment efforts and progress toward enrollment objectives.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><em>Regular travel across all five service areas is required, with intensified recruitment cycles in September–October and March–April.</em><br><br></div><div><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>Educational Talent Search (ETS) engages, empowers and supports future first generation college and under-served scholars who have the desire and potential to pursue an education beyond high school. We provide access to academic, social, and financial resources to students across five Nebraska service areas — the Lincoln Metro area and regional extension services in Schuyler, Hastings, Grand Island, and Winnebago.</div><div><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br> <br></strong>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.<strong><br></strong><br></div> TRIO Programs-0962 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100424 2026-05-07T11:29:04-05:00 2026-05-07T11:29:05-05:00 Director, Buros Center for Testing; Full Professor <div>The Buros Center for Testing,<strong> </strong>housed in the<strong> </strong>Department of Educational Psychology (EDPS) in the College of Education and Human Sciences (CEHS) at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln (UNL), seeks an accomplished academic leader to serve as Director. The Director serves as the chief executive and academic leader of the Buros Center for Testing, a globally respected, non-profit organization committed to improving the science and practice of testing and assessment through rigorous scholarship, psychometric research, and editorial leadership of industry-standard test reviews. The director works at the intersection of academia and practical, high-stakes testing, focusing on ensuring that assessments meet rigorous standards for testing validity and reliability.<br><br><strong>Why this role, why now.</strong></div><div>The Center is entering a pivotal leadership transition following more than two decades of sustained growth and success under its current director. The Director plays a critical role in sustaining the Center’s financial self-sufficiency, advancing its research mission, and maximizing its economic and scholarly impact. A new Director is essential to provide leadership for long-term planning, interdisciplinary collaboration, and external partnerships, while ensuring continuation of the mission to improve the science and practice of testing and assessment.<br><br></div><div>The Center is financially stable, highly productive, and supported by an experienced team. The Center’s strong tradition of integrity coupled with its progressive vision has made it a premier research and resource center for testing that continues to influence the use and understanding of measurements. The work of the Center serves to enhance the quality of tests worldwide and to provide evaluation services and research leadership essential to improving the science and practice of testing and assessment.</div><div><br><strong>Key Responsibilities<br></strong><em>Academic and Editorial Leadership</em></div><ul><li>Co-editing key publications, including the <em>Mental Measurements Yearbook, Tests</em> <em>in Print, </em>and <em>Pruebas Publicadas en Español</em> <em>.</em></li><li>Editing the journal <em>Applied Measurement in Education.</em></li><li>Supervising personnel and managing the daily operations of the Center.</li><li>Teaching, advising, and mentoring students within the Department of Educational Psychology.</li></ul><div><br><em>Psychometric and Evaluation Services</em></div><ul><li>Directing projects related to the independent evaluation of test quality and fairness.</li><li>Providing technical consultation and oversight for proprietary testing programs in education, licensure, certification, and employment.</li><li>Ensuring the integrity of test reviews and maintaining the Oscar K. Buros Library of Mental Measurements, the world's largest collection of commercially available tests.</li></ul><div><br><em>Advocacy and Administration</em></div><ul><li>Promoting assessment literacy through outreach, webinars, and workshops.</li><li>Initiating, developing, and securing contract/grant activities to fund the Center's research and development work.</li><li>Representing the Center on national and international committees related to testing standards, policy, and ethics.</li><li>Managing financial resources, physical space, and personnel.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The Director will report to the CEHS Dean and will hold a faculty appointment within EDPS. The position is expected to be a fiscal year (FY) appointment with a split FTE of up to 0.51 FTE as Director apportioned as 100% administration. The position is expected to have an apportionment that is aligned with teaching a minimum of one course a year. The successful candidate should have academic and scholarly achievements that support the rank of Full Professor with tenure, according to CEHS and UNL standards.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Buros Center for Testing-1044 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101797 2026-08-13T16:28:01-05:00 2026-08-13T16:28:01-05:00 Director, Center for Grassland Studies (0.40 FTE; Open to IANR Faculty Only) <div>The director of the Center for Grassland Studies (CGS) (0.40 FTE) has oversight of all CGS programs and supervises CGS staff, administering the Grassland Systems undergraduate degree program in cooperation with the Grassland Systems curriculum committee, the four units contributing to the major (Agronomy/Horticulture, School of Natural Resources, Animal Science, and Ag Economics), and CASNR. <br><br>Also included is coordination of teaching for the Grassland Systems major in partnership with unit leaders, advising, recruiting, scholarships, assessment, curriculum, and bulletin updates. Outreach and extension activities of CGS include programmatic and administrative support for the Nebraska Grazing Conference; the GRAS 490 Grassland Seminar and Leu Lecture; coordinating the CGS website, newsletter, and social media; and engaging stakeholders through the CGS Citizens Advisory Council and outreach events. <br><br>The CGS director promotes grassland research through collaboration to develop grant proposals, encourage research at IANR’s grassland properties, award the Arthur W. Sampson Graduate Fellowship, and administer NU Foundation Funds assigned to CGS for grassland-related activities. <br><br>The CGS director manages IANR properties assigned to CGS in accordance with the long-term management objectives of each property, coordinates management efforts with stakeholders, including state and federal agencies and adjacent landowner as appropriate, and seeks ways to integrate IANR grassland properties into the teaching, research, and outreach missions of CGS.<br><br><strong>The Director will help position CGS as:</strong></div><ul><li>The University of Nebraska's convenor for grassland systems expertise and collaboration.</li><li>A catalyst for interdisciplinary research and innovation.</li><li>A trusted source of science-based solutions for grassland and grazing systems.</li><li>A leader in grassland workforce development and student success.</li><li>A connector of CGS strengths, stakeholder needs, and societal impact.</li></ul><div><strong><br></strong>The person hired into this position will retain 60% of their current position and responsibilities.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Grasslands Studies Center-0954 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101653 2026-08-05T16:38:28-05:00 2026-08-05T16:38:29-05:00 Designer-Compositor <div>The University of Nebraska Press (UNP), founded in 1941, is the largest university press between Chicago and California. It publishes scholarly and general-interest books (with more than 5,000 titles in print and an additional 120 new titles released each year) and journals (with more than 30 different journals published each year) in topics ranging from anthropology and literary criticism to history and sports.<br><br>This position will be part of the UNP's Editorial, Design, and Production (EDP) department, which oversees the editing, design, and production of approximately 120 frontlist books and 30 different journals each year. Responsibilites include:</div><ul><li>Design and typeset assigned number of full-length journals and books per year, both cover and interior, and other projects as assigned, to include: select cover art, design cover (front and back), determine type specifications for interior, conduct art review and adjustments, create line art as needed (tables, charts, etc.), create typeset pages, input proof corrections, create final print-ready PDF for print vendors, and export files for ebook production as appropriate.</li><li>Consult and coordinate with other staff (lead senior designer, project editors, and print production coordinator) to obtain information and maintain schedules.</li><li>Conduct quality-control checks of typeset files produced by others; conduct other design and typesetting reviews as required.</li></ul><div><br>This position may be considered for remote work in accordance with the University of Nebraska’s Alternative Worksite program. More information is available at <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/alternative-worksite\"><strong>https://nebraska.edu/alternative-worksite</strong></a>.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> University Press-0933 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102006 2026-08-25T11:27:25-05:00 2026-08-25T11:27:26-05:00 Police Officer <div>Commissioned police officer who will perform all related duties including, but not limited to, patrolling on foot or by vehicle, University property to prevent and discover the commission of crimes; enforce state laws and city ordinances; enforce traffic regulations; conduct investigations on criminal offenses and traffic accidents to gather evidence, obtain witnesses and make arrests; provide documentation and testimony to Judicial Board and courts; and provide general security for University properties and citizens on campus to insure a safe environment for all.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace, it's a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans </strong>with a university match</li></ul><div><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> University Police-0823 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101188 2026-07-13T15:36:18-05:00 2026-07-13T15:36:19-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Water & Cropping Systems (Burt Co.) <div><strong>Overview </strong><br>This position is based in Tekamah, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Burt, Dakota, and Thurston Counties. The Extension professional serves as a trusted, research-based educational leader connecting the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, the agricultural industry, and Nebraska communities through practical, science-based extension programming and applied research.</div><div><br>The professional is expected to maintain a visible and engaged presence within the communities they serve and become a recognized first source of trusted, unbiased agricultural information. Success in this role requires strong teaching and communication skills, community engagement, relationship building, leadership in agricultural education, and the ability to foster meaningful partnerships that support Nebraska agriculture and rural communities. Primary programmatic responsibilities are developing and delivering impactful water and cropping systems extension programming that: a) improves agricultural profitability and sustainability, b) reduces environmental risk, c) encourages natural resources stewardship, d) enhances agricultural resiliency, and e) expands public understanding of food, forage, grain, and fiber production systems.<br><br></div><div>The Extension Educator/Instructor translates complex research into practical, solution-based educational experiences for diverse audiences including farmers, ranchers, agribusiness professionals, community leaders, and the general public. Educational delivery methods may include workshops, field demonstrations, applied research trials, digital resources, consultations, media outreach, and collaborative partnerships.<br><br></div><div>As a member of the statewide Water and Cropping Systems team, the professional actively contributes to the development of innovative, research-based resources and interdisciplinary solutions addressing current and emerging agricultural challenges for their assigned region and across Nebraska. The position requires collaboration with university faculty, extension colleagues, industry partners, agencies, and local stakeholders to identify needs and deliver responsive programming.<br><br></div><div>As the sole Extension professional in the county, this position holds the primary lead educator responsibilities as listed in the organizational/lead educator responsibilities.</div><div><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate-level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an open rank educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress toward and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%)</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., on-farm, ranch, or community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs entrepreneurial practices to obtain funding and partnerships, enhancing Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%)</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator</strong></a> document as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<br>o Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.<br>o Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.<br>o Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.<br><br></li></ul><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission. <br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 8-12357 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101888 2026-08-19T10:30:57-05:00 2026-08-19T10:30:57-05:00 Certified Athletic Trainer <div>The Certified Athletic Trainer is a nine-month position paid over twelve months and is responsible for the day-to-day operations of the Injury Prevention &amp; Care facilities, personnel, within the Campus Recreation program.<br><br></div><div>As a <strong>Certified Athletic Trainer</strong>, you will:</div><ul><li>Provide immediate, on-site emergency care and first aid at practices, games, and within the Campus Recreation facilities; assessing injuries, and severity, including concussion management.</li><li>Coordinate and oversee first aid and emergency response services for recreational events.</li><li>Create and implement professional development opportunities for student staff members.</li><li>Assist with the leadership and management of a team, including, screening, hiring, scheduling, training, and evaluation.</li><li>Administrative responsibilities include budget, payroll, inventory, record keeping, analysis, and follow-up.</li><li>Develop and implement injury prevention training/clinics.</li><li>Actively participates in the athletic training education program through the development of lesson plans and educational materials, teaching credit and/or noncredit academic athletic training course(s)</li><li>Work cooperatively with Campus Recreation staff, sports programs, coaches and the University community.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>This position schedule is typically Tuesday – Saturday, with evenings, nights, and weekends based on sporting events, practices and tournament schedules. <br><br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Campus Recreation-0965 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102099 2026-08-31T07:56:16-05:00 2026-08-31T07:56:17-05:00 Academic Pathway Advisor (Grand Island) <div>Are you passionate about empowering first-generation and low-income students to reach their full potential? Join our team as an <strong>Academic Pathway Advisor </strong>and be a driving force in shaping brighter futures for youth in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>As the <strong>Academic Pathway Advisor</strong>, you will:<br><br></div><ul><li>Recruit, advise, and support students in the program and monitor their success.</li><li>Build relationships with school counselors, families and community partners within the Grand Island/Winnebago service area</li><li>Host interactive workshops, provide one-on-one advising, tutoring, and facilitate enrichment programs.</li><li>Assist int the planning and execution of the summer program.</li></ul><div><br>This is a regionally based role for someone who thrives on autonomy. Working from a Grand Island office. Regular travel within the service area and periodic travel to Lincoln is required.<br><br></div><div>About Us:</div><div><strong>Educational Talent Search </strong>(ETS) engages, empowers and supports potential first generation college and under-served scholars who have the desire and potential to pursue an education beyond high school. We provide access to academic, social, and financial resources to students across five Nebraska Service Areas. This position anchors our Grand Island and Winnebago service area, serving students in partnership with local school districts and the Nebraska College Preparatory Academy (NCPA).<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> <br> <br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> TRIO Programs-0962 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102052 2026-08-27T08:37:47-05:00 2026-08-27T08:37:48-05:00 Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate: Custodian (1:30pm-10:00pm, M-F) <div>At the University of Nebraska where every person and every interaction matters, the Hospitality Service team plays a meaningful role in maintaining safe, healthy, and welcoming environments for students, staff, faculty, and/or guests in a variety of settings.<br><br></div><div>In this role you will:</div><ul><li>Perform routine cleaning and upkeep across housing facilities</li><li>Maintain offices, residential halls, public areas, bathrooms, conference rooms, and dining centers</li><li>Ensure a clean, safe environment for all guests</li><li>Clean hard floors and carpets</li><li>Mix cleaning solutions as directed</li><li>Assist with event setup and conference operations as needed</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The Hospitality Services position may be hired at a higher level depending upon candidate qualifications.<br><br>Depending upon level assigned, this position may:</div><ul><li>Train and oversee work of others</li><li>Respond to on-call duties and other emergency situations during shifts</li><li>Use all non-riding and non-autonomous equipment</li><li>Order supplies</li></ul><div><br></div><div>When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Attendant</strong>, the position will receive continuous supervision and specific guidelines in the process of training and development.<br><br>When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Assistant, Hospitality Services Associate or Hospitality Services Sr. Associate</strong> the position will routinely perform the skills associated with that level.<br><br>Performance will be continuously assessed to determine ability to perform these skills at an acceptable level.<br><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: Selleck Dining Service-1148 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101483 2026-07-29T08:57:25-05:00 2026-07-29T08:57:25-05:00 Technical and Engineering Service Manager <div>The Nebraska Manufacturing Extension Partnership (NMEP) helps Nebraska manufacturers grow, evolve, and compete by delivering practical, results-driven expertise. The NMEP is part of the National Manufacturing Extension Partnership program, a federally supported network that enables access to best practices, specialized expertise, and shared resources across the country. Embedded within the University of Nebraska, NMEP leverages university research, talent, and technological capabilities to drive innovation. By combining national reach with local relationships and academic resources, NMEP partners with manufacturers to improve productivity, strengthen leadership and workforce capabilities, and adopt advanced technologies.<br><br></div><div>As the <strong>Technical and Engineering Service Manager</strong>, you will:</div><ul><li>Develop and lead new engineering programs and services to support Nebraska industry, with primary responsibility for program design, structure, and implementation.</li><li>Serve as subject matter expert in engineering and manufacturing by advising manufacturing clients, UNL stakeholders, and partners on emerging trends, technologies, and industry best practices to inform decision-making and future planning.</li><li>Lead the development and execution of technical program strategy for NMEP, with decision-making authority over program direction in collaboration with other service areas.</li><li>Lead, direct, coach, and oversee project managers and other staff by delivering leadership and team engagement.</li><li>Engage with business owners, CEOs, and executive leaders to justify client needs and demonstrate the return on investment of improving their businesses.</li><li>Independently assess complex, multi-disciplinary, strategic, managerial, operational, and technical problems and recommend appropriate and effective solutions to achieve desired goals.</li><li>Develop and maintain partnerships with internal and external stakeholders, including College of Engineering, IANR, educational institutions, and industry partners to support program development, service delivery, and outreach efforts.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we're proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn't just a workplace; it's a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you'll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> NE Manufacturing Exten Partnership-9028 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101978 2026-08-24T14:20:59-05:00 2026-08-24T14:20:59-05:00 Academic Navigator <div>The Academic Navigator is dedicated to University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) undergraduates’ persistence and degree completion, especially historically underserved first generation, low-income, and ethnic minority college students. The position will be part of a ten (10) member team that is responsible for supporting the creation of an ecology of validation by utilizing UNL reporting and student information systems to identify students in need of academic support and serving as a validating agent. This position reports to the Director of the Academic Navigator program with a dotted line report to the colleges of UNL.<br><br>Responsibilities will include facilitating a case management model that includes triaging student concerns (i.e. personal, academic, or financial) and collaborating with campus partners to facilitate communication and connections with appropriate resources. Proactively engaging with students identified by campus stakeholders including responding to referrals made by faculty and staff across campus and supporting their retention efforts. Using provided university analytics and data to coordinate appropriate outreach and response using a variety of methods (i.e. in-person, email, text, phone, etc.) to targeted student populations and recording contacts in digital notes system. Be able to understand how cultural context, differences, and institutional/social barriers influence the student experience to best employ inclusive advocacy strategies to all students. Engaging in a community of collaborative relationships with student success stakeholders across student and academic affairs including University Housing, UNL faculty, academic advisors, and University Career Services. Engaging in continuous training and professional development to remain informed on existing and emerging strategies to promote student persistence and academic success<br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Undergraduate Educ & Student Success-8450 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102177 2026-09-03T21:56:21-05:00 2026-09-03T21:56:22-05:00 Barista <div>The <strong>Barista</strong> will assist in the management of the Dining Tazza coffee shop within the Westbrook Music building.<br><br></div><div>In this role you will:</div><ul><li>Provide excellent customer service to all patrons of the Tazza coffee shop</li><li>Accurately create quality beverages and products</li><li>Maintain a clean environment</li><li>Order products and supplies while maintaining appropriate levels of inventory</li><li>Greet and provide a friendly atmosphere to guests, students, faculty, and staff</li><li>Partner with dining leadership to set prices, create beverage menu, and maintain profit margins</li><li>Train and lead student staff</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><strong><em>.</em></strong></div> Housing: Knoll C Store-6778 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100576 2026-05-21T10:28:11-05:00 2026-05-21T10:28:12-05:00 Human Resources Coordinator <div>The BPAC Business Center at the University of Nebraska Lincoln supports the College of Arts and Sciences within the following functional areas: Human Resources, Finance, and Pre-Award and Post-Award Grant support. The Human Resources Coordinator serves in a customer-facing role and is responsible for providing human resources support in a timely and accurate manner and in compliance with all applicable institutional, UNL, State, and Federal regulations, policies, and guidelines. The Human Resources Coordinator primarily provides departmental human resource-related support but may execute moderately complex payroll transactions in a subsidiary capacity. The Human Resources Coordinator will work closely with employees within the departments served, as well as functional office staff, providing a high level of customer service and professionalism in all interactions. This position functions under general supervision and is expected utilize sophisticated technology to provide professional services.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace, it's a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:<br><br></div><div><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays<br><br></div><div><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life<br><br></div><div><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education<br><br></div><div><strong>Generous retirement plans </strong>with a university match<br><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> BPAC Business Center-12176 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101823 2026-08-14T15:49:20-05:00 2026-08-14T15:49:20-05:00 Chick-fil-A Team Member (Temporary: Multiple Shifts and Positions available) <div>The Chick-fil-A Team Member serves as an integral member of the Chick-fil-A team.<br><br></div><div>The Team Member will provide excellent customer service to all guest through front end and back end operations which may include:<br><br></div><ul><li>Greeting all guests in a friendly manner.</li><li>Accurately entering orders into the POS system.</li><li>Cashier duties.</li><li>Food preparation.</li><li>Front end and kitchen stocking.</li><li>Ingredient preparation.</li><li>Inventory.</li><li>Dish machine operation.</li><li>Cleaning duties.</li><li>Opening and closing procedures.</li><li>Monitoring food quality and safety.</li><li>Assists with training new staff as necessary.</li><li>Operates the computer for some training, email, and other related tasks.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>At Chick-fil-A, the team member role is more than just a job, it’s an opportunity.</div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Housing: Chick-fil-A-12426 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/98837 2026-01-05T08:22:54-06:00 2026-01-05T08:22:54-06:00 2026 Clerical/Administrative Temporary Pool <div>On occasion, the University of Nebraska is in need of highly motivated candidates who truly enjoy working with a wide variety of people. The ideal candidates will possess great customer service skills, a willingness to be flexible and good attention to detail. Duties could include: Filing, typing correspondence, data entry, phone/receptionist coverage, accounting, making travel arrangements, event planning assistance, and other duties as needed. A criminal history background check will be conducted.<br><br>Temporary employees may be appointed for a period of up to two years. Those appointed for more than six months are eligible for benefits from the beginning of the appointment, provided the position is half-time (.50FTE) or greater. Those appointed for six months or less are not eligible for benefits. Benefits for eligible temporary employees include the following: health, dental, vision and life insurance.<br><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, qualified applicants are considered for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See: </em><a href=\"http://www.unl.edu/equity/notice-nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>http://www.unl.edu/equity/notice-nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Human Resources-0821 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101668 2026-08-06T12:03:04-05:00 2026-08-06T12:03:04-05:00 Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility located near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.</div><div><br><strong>As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle.</li><li>Maintain machinery and fences.</li><li>Assist with pasture management and the collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Position requires irregular hours and work in inclement weather. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102008 2026-08-25T11:29:36-05:00 2026-08-25T11:29:36-05:00 Building/Grounds Attendant (5:00pm-2:00am) <div>Repairs and performs minor preventive maintenance on a variety of equipment. Performs a variety of duties in and around buildings and grounds. Performs assignments such as light bulb change and fixture and equipment cleaning, painting, carpentry: assists maintenance personnel and other workers with their tasks or projects. Perform building snow removal as required. Performs housekeeping and janitorial duties to maintain offices, restrooms and public areas in a clean and orderly condition. Mixes cleaning solutions to appropriate strength. Removes trash from offices and lobby areas. Perform room set ups and strikes. Follows established routine. Ability to read and understand cleaning instructions and information. Other duties as assigned.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential.<br></em><br></div><div><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Lied Center for Performing Arts-0854 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101227 2026-07-14T16:45:04-05:00 2026-07-14T16:45:05-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Early Childhood (Red Willow County) <div><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></div><div>This position is based in McCook, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Chase, Dundy, Frontier, Furnas, Gosper, Harlan, Hayes, Hitchcock, Phelps, and Red Willow Counties. Focused on young children and their caregivers (e.g., parents, early childhood teachers), this position will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home unit and the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources as an effective scholar and citizen.</div><div>The primary responsibility for this position is to develop and deliver high quality, innovative educational programs and resources as an active participant in the work of the Early Childhood team and may be active in a statewide issue team that addresses current issues facing Nebraska. This position is expected to interact closely with parents, teachers, early childhood professionals, and caregivers of young children in their geographic area and possibly statewide based on the current projects and goals of the Early Childhood team.<br><br></div><div>Nebraska Extension’s Early Childhood team supports adults who play a role in young children’s lives by providing educational programming and resources about early child development and early care and education. Adults play a significant role in setting the stage for young children's lifelong learning, discovery, and success. The Early Childhood team is committed to empowering these adults to support and provide effective learning experiences for Nebraska’s young children. Such early learning experiences enhance children’s readiness (physical, cognitive, social, and emotional) for school and setting them up for lifelong success.</div><div><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate-level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress toward and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%):</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., health and wellbeing, and community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs entrepreneurial practices to obtain funding and partnerships, enhancing Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%):</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator document </strong></a>as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<ul><li>Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.</li><li>Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.</li><li>Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li></ul></li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR, we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 4-12353 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101890 2026-08-19T10:31:44-05:00 2026-08-19T10:31:44-05:00 Curator <div>Responsible for care and preservation of all artifacts in IQM collections in accordance with the highest professional and ethical standards. Responsible for research and interpretation as applicable to exhibitions and educational programs; responsible for disseminating results of research through publications, exhibitions, lectures.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> International Quilt Museum-5976 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102105 2026-08-31T11:03:59-05:00 2026-08-31T11:03:59-05:00 Marketing Associate <div>The University of Nebraska Press (UNP), founded in 1941, is the largest university press between Chicago and California. It publishes scholarly and general-interest books (with more than 5,000 titles in print and an additional 120 new titles released each year) and journals (with more than 30 different journals published each year) in topics ranging from anthropology and literary criticism to history and sports.<br><br>The Marketing Associate manages and creates content for all social media accounts for the Press. Assists marketing and sales manager with special projects related to online promotions, author requests, and design projects. Manages award submissions. Coordinates with publicity on sharing review coverage to Press networks. Assists the marketing department with ongoing tactics as needed, including blurb outreach and other communications.<br><br>This position may be considered for remote work in accordance with the University of Nebraska’s Alternative Worksite program.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> University Press-0933 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101843 2026-08-17T16:02:19-05:00 2026-08-17T16:02:20-05:00 Finance Coordinator <div>As a <strong>Finance Coordinator</strong>, you will coordinate a wide range of financial transactions across multiple fund types, providing responsive service and ensuring compliance with university policies.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Coordinating purchasing, procurement, and payment activities, including purchase orders, P-Cards, vendor setup, and contract routing, while ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures.</li><li>Reviewing expenditures for funding allowability across a variety of account types and preparing payment and transfer requests when appropriate.</li><li>Reviewing and approving travel and expense transactions and assisting faculty, staff, and students with travel and expense submissions.</li><li>Processing and reviewing accounts payable (A/P) and accounts receivable (A/R) transactions, including reimbursements, non-employee payments, invoices, refunds, internal charges, and outstanding receivables.</li><li>Preparing, reviewing, and processing accounting transactions, journal entries, reconciliations, and financial adjustments while maintaining accurate financial records.</li><li>Coordinating capital asset activities, including transfers, inventories, validations, and disposition processes in accordance with university requirements.</li><li>Assisting with training new staff members.</li><li>Providing guidance and customer support to faculty, staff, and colleagues regarding policies, procedures, and business processes.</li></ul><div><br>Following an initial onsite training period of up to six months, this position may become eligible for a hybrid work schedule with up to 1 remote day(s) per week. All hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> College of Engineering-0907 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102061 2026-08-27T12:27:08-05:00 2026-08-27T12:27:09-05:00 Cohort Program Manager <div>The <strong>Cohort Program Manager</strong> will support the advancement of the mission and purpose of the Center for Entrepreneurship. This position is primarily responsible for managing and enhancing the Center’s cohort programs (the Accelerator and the Catalysts cohort), coaching student teams through the startup development process and maintaining the mentor, service provider, and investor relationships that make those programs successful. This position also co-advises the Husker Venture Fund, the Center’s student-run venture capital fund, and supports the Cornhusker Venture Capital Investment Competition. Occasional evening and weekend hours will be required.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Center for Entrepreneurship-1302 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101488 2026-07-29T09:49:12-05:00 2026-07-29T09:49:13-05:00 Reading Teacher Coach Specialist (Part Time) <div>The Nebraska Center for Research on Children, Youth, Families and Schools is seeking a part time <strong>Reading Teacher Coach Specialist</strong> to work on the Nebraska Workshops on Reading Development Strategies (WORDS) Project, a program funded by the Nebraska Department of Education and Institute of Education Sciences that aims to provide rural schools with professional development and support to prepare all students for reading success by systematically delivering high-quality instruction tailored to meet their needs.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><div>• Serve as an active member of the WORDS project</div><div>• Conduct reading observations and evaluate reading instruction in schools across the state</div><div>• Provide consultation, training, and on-site implementation support services to school districts</div><div>• Provide reading professional development opportunities for school district and ESU staff and community professionals</div><div>• Work in close collaboration with the Reading Teacher Coach Lead to ensure all WORDS activities align with broader WORDS project goals</div><div>• Work in close collaboration with WORDS Reading Teacher Coach Lead to tailor training and supports to individual school needs</div><div>• Maintain the WORDS Resource Library with current publications related to the field of continuous improvement.</div><div>• Stay informed of evidence-based instructional materials, strategies, interventions, assessments, and technology for improved reading outcomes for ALL students.</div><div>• Be aware of new research and best practices around reading within Multi-tiered Systems of Support</div><div>• Maintain a database of all contacts and training and supports provided</div><div>• Contribute to the enhancement of the WORDS Website</div><div>• Participate in ongoing professional learning opportunities at the state and national level.</div><div>• Work involves travel to schools, but some work can be done remotely and through virtual conferencing.</div><div><br>This part-time position will work .50 FTE or 20 hours per week.<br><br><strong>About Us<br></strong>The College of Education and Human Sciences strives to be a vibrant, welcoming, and caring community driven by our mission to enhance the lives of individuals, families, schools, and communities, and strengthening the relationships among them.<br><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a part-time regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> NE Ctr Research on Youth, Fam & School-4425 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101982 2026-08-24T16:40:12-05:00 2026-08-24T16:40:13-05:00 Office Manager: Student Legal Services (9:00am-5:00pm, M-F) <div>Ranked as one of <strong>the best employers in the state of Nebraska</strong>, the University of Nebraska is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.<br> <br> <strong>We invest in our employees:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Vacation, sick, and holiday pay</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance</li><li>No-cost life insurance</li><li>Employee Assistance Program</li><li>Retirement plans with University match</li><li>Tuition assistance for full-time employees and dependents</li><li>Exclusive staff discounts</li><li>Continuous improvement and innovation</li><li>Professional development through training and education</li><li>And much more!</li></ul><div><br><strong>The Office Manager is responsible for overseeing the administrative operations, supporting the director and attorneys with legal administrative support in the Student Legal Services office, and providing front-facing customer service. The Office Manager also provides assistance with budget and fiscal management.</strong><br><br></div><div>As Office Manager you will:<br><br></div><ul><li>Work with our students, staff and faculty who are requesting services or departmental information.</li><li>Initiate and process confidential administrative case management by providing necessary documents and applications, correspondence on status, and update electronic files.</li><li>Support the Director and attorneys by performing a combination of administrative and complex office work associated with the office, program administration, and data collection/entry.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> ASUN-1321 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102179 2026-09-04T09:10:49-05:00 2026-09-04T09:10:49-05:00 Finance Specialist - HAPPI Business Center <div>The HAPPI Business Center is a collaborative team providing specialized business services that advance the teaching, research, and extension missions of our partner units. <br><br>As a <strong>Finance Specialist</strong>, you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial functions.</div><div><br>Responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Managing an assigned portfolio, advising on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources which may include state accounts, grants, service centers, and revolving accounts.</li><li>Supporting sponsored research through post-award grant financial management and administration.</li><li>Providing consultative guidance on university financial policies, sponsored programs, and business processes, helping departments navigate complex issues and identify practical, compliant solutions.</li><li>Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions.</li></ul><div><br>We seek a collaborative, service-oriented professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate builds trusted relationships, communicates effectively with diverse stakeholders, and exercises sound judgment to make and communicate decisions that support responsible stewardship, compliance, and exceptional service.<br><br>This position is located on UNL's East Campus in Lincoln, NE. <br><br>Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with a minimum of 3 days per week worked on site. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Note:</strong> Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about UNL benefits and your <strong>total compensation</strong> at: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> HAPPI Business Center-3027 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100707 2026-06-02T10:40:22-05:00 2026-06-02T10:40:23-05:00 Forage Technician (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility located near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries. <br><br><strong>As a Forage Technician, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide support to the Range &amp; Forage Production Manager with pasture monitoring and pasture improvement programs.</li><li>Collect, organize, and summarize data and samples to assess pasture composition, quality, and grazing utilization.</li><li>Advise other staff members on issues related to grazing including environmental conditions and utilization data.</li><li>Provide assistance to other operation areas including movement of cattle between pastures, farm and hay crews, and livestock management.</li></ul><div>This position requires significant computer work, some evening and weekend hours, and work in inclement weather. Due to the size of the facility, a valid driver's license is required to travel between sites. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I.<br><br><strong>Note: Sponsorships will not be offered for this position.</strong> <br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102113 2026-08-31T16:04:17-05:00 2026-08-31T16:04:17-05:00 Hospitality Service Attendant/Assistant/Associate/Sr. Associate (10:30pm-7:00am, Weds-Sun) <div>At the University of Nebraska where every person and every interaction matters, the Hospitality Service team plays a meaningful role in maintaining safe, healthy, and welcoming environments for students, staff, faculty, and/or guests in a variety of settings.</div><div>In this role you will:</div><ul><li>Performs routine cleaning and upkeep across housing facilities</li><li>Maintains offices, residential halls, public areas, bathrooms, conference rooms, and dining centers</li><li>Ensures a clean, safe environment for all guests</li><li>Cleans hard floors and carpets</li><li>Mixes cleaning solutions as directed</li><li>Assists with event setup and conference operations as needed</li></ul><div>The Hospitality Services position may be hired at a higher level depending upon candidate qualifications.<br><br>Depending upon level assigned, this position may:</div><ul><li>Train and oversee work of others</li><li>Respond to on-call duties and other emergency situations during shifts</li><li>Use all non-riding and non-autonomous equipment</li><li>Order supplies</li></ul><div>When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Attendant</strong>, the position will receive continuous supervision and specific guidelines in the process of training and development.<br><br>When hired as a <strong>Hospitality Services Assistant, Hospitality Services Associate or Hospitality Services Sr. Associate</strong> the position will routinely perform the skills associated with that level.<br><br>Performance will be continuously assessed to determine ability to perform these skills at an acceptable level.<br><br></div><div><strong>About Us:</strong><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Campus Recreation-0965 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/99285 2026-02-05T16:16:01-06:00 2026-02-05T16:16:01-06:00 Administrative Specialist <div>The Administrative Specialist provides highly skilled professional support and performs administrative duties for the Associate and Assistant Vice Chancellors within the Executive Vice Chancellor’s office. The Administrative Specialist serves as the first point of contact for office guests and is responsible for ensuring a professional and welcoming environment, overseeing general office management and maintenance functions. The Administrative Specialist is responsible for managing and coordinating multiple calendars for members of the leadership team, scheduling appointments, and assisting with prioritization of requests and re-prioritization when new issues arise. The position manages an array of general office functions and office suite locations, and provides broad support as needed (e.g. event support, special project support, backup to EVC Executive Assistant). The Administrative Specialist provides impeccable client service to a wide range of constituents and guests, including university faculty, administrators, staff, students and alumni, campus guests, and external consultants and the general public. The Administrative Specialist will join an energetic and supportive administrative team in an office with opportunities that strive to leverage individual strengths, talents, and interests.<br><br></div><div><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Office of the Exec Vice Chancellor-50000085 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101678 2026-08-06T16:02:02-05:00 2026-08-06T16:02:03-05:00 Assistant Director of Admissions <div>The Assistant Director of Admissions will have direct responsibility for undergraduate recruitment efforts for the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. This individual will coordinate undergraduate recruitment efforts for transfer, military, low-income, and first generation prospective students. This team member will also provide supervision for assigned recruitment areas. The team member will supervise multiple staff in the office and will serve as a consultant to many other teams and campus partners on transfer, military, low-income, and first generation prospective students. This position will serve as a liaison between UNL and high schools, community programs, and community colleges and will help grow partnerships for the university. This person will work with associate director to set priorities as it relates to transfer, military, low-income and first generation prospective students. The position will provide updates to associate director on analysis of data and ensure that goals are met; actions taken consistent with this analysis and provide recommendations on recruitment strategies; interpretation of recruitment policies and exercises authority and independent judgment in making recruitment decisions on a case-by-case basis.<br><br><strong>Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br></strong><br>As an EO employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</div> Admissions-0959 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102010 2026-08-25T11:31:25-05:00 2026-08-25T11:31:25-05:00 Director of Career Development & Leadership <div>Provide student-athletes with life skills guidance, program assistance and total person development for Nebraska Athletics. Meet with prospective student-athletes and families on regular basis. Coordinate, monitor and document various outreach events and student-athlete appearances in compliance with NCAA and conference rules. Plan, organize, and direct multiple major life skills events and seminars. Serve as advisor to leadership groups. Meet with individual student-athletes for career development. Coordination of various seminars, workshops and special functions. Evening hours and weekends required.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Athletics-0850 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101249 2026-07-15T16:53:57-05:00 2026-07-15T16:53:58-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - 4-H Youth Development (Lincoln County) <div><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></div><div>This position is based in North Platte, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Lincoln, Logan, and McPherson Counties. The major responsibility of this position is to provide regional leadership for Nebraska Extension’s 4-H and Youth Development Program. This extension professional is expected to interact closely with 4-H clientele in these communities and deliver programs in their geographic area.</div><div><br></div><div>The Positive Youth Development – 4-H extension professional will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home unit and the IANR as an effective scholar and citizen, including supporting student recruitment and IANR science literacy. In 4-H, we believe in the power of young people. We see that every child has valuable strengths and real influence to improve the world around us. We are America’s largest youth development organization, empowering nearly six million young people across the U.S. with the skills to lead for a lifetime. Nebraska Extension is an organization that values excellence and as a member of the Nebraska Extension team you will create and deliver world-class learning experiences focused on critical issues that empower Nebraskans to improve their lives.<br><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an open rank educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress towards and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%)</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., schools or community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs entrepreneurial practices to obtain funding and partnerships, enhancing Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%)</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator </strong></a>document as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<ul><li>Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.</li><li>Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.</li><li>Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li></ul></li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR, we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective well-being and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 3-12352 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101896 2026-08-19T10:33:50-05:00 2026-08-19T10:33:51-05:00 Director of Enrollment Marketing, Communications & Visitor Experiences <div>The Director of Enrollment Marketing, Communications, and Visitor Experiences will be responsible for developing the processes and procedures to facilitate the execution of an integrated, effective campus-wide recruitment and enrollment strategy. The director will lead the strategic development and execution of enrollment-focused marketing, communications, and visitor experiences to support achieving the university’s recruitment, admissions, and enrollment goals. The director will develop strategies and tactics to inform and positively impact Academic Services and Enrollment Management (ASEM) and academic colleges’ collective recruitment and matriculation of new students and retention of continuing students.</div><div><br>The Director will primarily develop and support the strategic initiatives of ASEM, which includes the Offices of Admissions, Husker Hub, Scholarships &amp; Financial Aid, and University Registrar, New Student Enrollment and the Nebraska College Preparatory Academy. Pursuant to those goals, the director will oversee the ASEM marketing &amp; communications and on-campus experiences teams. Additionally, the director will ensure a consistent, impactful communication approach as students’ transition from prospective to enrolled students. The director will be an integral subject matter expert along with numerous university-wide professionals who are challenged to align complimentary enrollment-focused marketing and communication strategies and tactics that elevate the university amongst competitor institutions. Along these lines, the director will assist in the development and management of university’s brand by connecting all strategic recruitment objectives to the overall university marketing and communication strategy.</div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Academic Services & Enrollment Mgmt-7776 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100709 2026-06-02T10:41:57-05:00 2026-06-02T10:41:57-05:00 Multispecies Livestock Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The <strong>U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC)</strong> is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. cattle, sheep, and swine industries.</div><div><br><strong>As a Multispecies Livestock Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Work with and around cattle, pigs, and sheep.</li><li>Be responsible for weighing, sorting, and animal health.</li><li>Perform daily maintenance of machinery and fences.</li><li>Treat sick animals.</li><li>Feed livestock in the winter.</li><li>Help with hay in the summer.</li><li>Assist with collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>This position requires some evening and weekend hours and work in inclement weather. Due to the size of the facility, a valid driver's license is required to travel between sites. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. <br><br>Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock or beef industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.<br><br><strong>Note: Sponsorships will not be offered for this position.</strong><br><br><strong>About Us:</strong><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101848 2026-08-18T09:32:42-05:00 2026-08-18T09:32:42-05:00 Finance Specialist <div>Join the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) Business Centers, where we strive to deliver exceptional service, innovative solutions, and responsible stewardship that advance IANR's teaching, research, and extension missions.</div><div><br>As a <strong>Finance Specialist</strong>, with focus on cost accounting and contract administration; you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial functions.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Serving as a primary resource for service center and contract administration across IANR, providing strategic guidance and ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures.</li><li>Partnering with departments to develop, manage, and improve service center operations and contractual agreements, promoting effective business practices and sound financial stewardship.</li><li>Working with faculty and staff to forecast expenses and calculate appropriate service rates based on anticipated activity. Regularly review budget to actual amounts to determine if established rates need to be adjusted.</li><li>Managing an assigned portfolio, advising on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources including but not limited to state accounts, grants, service centers, and revolving accounts.</li><li>Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions.</li></ul><div><br>We seek a collaborative, service-oriented professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate builds trusted relationships, communicates effectively with diverse stakeholders, and exercises sound judgment to make and communicate decisions that support responsible stewardship, compliance, and exceptional service. <br><br>This position is located on UNL's East Campus in Lincoln, NE. Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with a minimum of 3 days per week worked on campus. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Note:</strong> Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br> <br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> AVE Business Center-3026 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102070 2026-08-27T15:48:41-05:00 2026-08-27T15:48:42-05:00 Research Development Manager <div>The Research Development Manager provides research administration and research development support for the Rural Drug Addiction Research (RDAR) Center. This position supports investigators and research teams through assistance with administrative processes, research development, project communications, and other research-promotion activities.<br><br>The role emphasizes strong organizational skills, clear written and verbal communication, collaborative team engagement, and the ability to concurrently manage multiple responsibilities. The Research Development Manager is expected to be a self-starter who demonstrates initiative, applies problem-solving skills to routine challenges, and effectively switch focus to meet competing deadlines while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Salary support for this position is derived from sponsored grants and contracts.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Rural Drug Addiction Research Center-10950 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101538 2026-07-30T14:55:41-05:00 2026-07-30T14:55:42-05:00 Chick-fil-A Manager <div>The <strong>Chick-fil-A Manager</strong> is responsible for overseeing the daily operations and long-term strategic management of the Chick-fil-A restaurant located in the Nebraska City Union, ensuring operational excellence, exceptional customer service, and achievement of business objectives.<br><br>The <strong>Chick-fil-A Manager</strong> will:</div><ul><li>Demonstrate a commitment to exceptional leadership and customer service</li><li>Foster and maintain a safe, welcoming environment for customers and team members</li><li>Exercise independent judgment and discretion in managing the overall operations of the retail location</li><li>Recruit, hire, train, supervise, and develop team members</li><li>Ensure all staff meet the operational, service, and brand standards of Chick-fil-A and University Dining</li><li>Maintain high levels of customer satisfaction and product quality</li><li>Monitor and manage financial performance, including reviewing sales trends and implementing strategies to achieve business goals</li><li>Forecast inventory needs and order products and supplies to support efficient operations</li><li>Ensure compliance with safety, security, and operational policies and procedures within the store</li><li>Uphold the brand standards for branded restaurant concepts it oversees</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Schedule varies and includes evenings, late nights, and weekend shifts.<br><br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a><em><br></em><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div> Housing: Chick-fil-A-12426 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101989 2026-08-25T11:03:52-05:00 2026-08-25T11:03:53-05:00 Library Services Assistant (3:30pm-12:30am, Sun-Thurs) <div>This position is responsible for the Weekend and Evening service point coverage of the Love Library Complex, including the Adele Hall Learning Commons and Dinsdale Family Learning Commons, including but not limited to service point and functional student worker supervision, and for building issues, including but not limited to security, closing, and emergency protocols.<br><br>Scheduled work hours will be Sunday-Thursday, 3:30 pm-12:30am with a 1-hour lunch break.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>About Us</strong><br><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> University Libraries-0905 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102181 2026-09-04T09:19:30-05:00 2026-09-04T09:19:30-05:00 Farm Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Farm Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Perform all activities associated with irrigated forage crop production including but not limited to tillage, planting, chemical applications, irrigation and harvesting operations.</li><li>Perform routine equipment maintenance and repair.</li><li>Assist other operational areas including but not limited to livestock feeding and care, fence installation and repair, building /facility maintenance.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather required. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I.<br><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and have been named a Family Friendly Workplace. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li>Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li>Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li>Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education</li><li>Robust retirement plans with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about UNL benefits and <strong>your total compensation</strong>: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101903 2026-08-19T10:39:55-05:00 2026-08-19T10:39:56-05:00 Engineering and Technology Education Lead <div>The Raikes School Engineering and Technology Education Lead collaborates with Design Studio staff and Capstone Project Sponsor technical contacts to assess and define hardware, software, and data needs for capstone projects. This role is responsible for establishing initial technical requirements and providing ongoing support for projects throughout each project’s lifecycle.<br><br></div><div>Key responsibilities include supporting the onboarding of annual capstone projects; serving as a technical advisor and resource for student teams in partnership with other Design Studio staff; procuring and managing IT equipment inventory; manage software-as-a-service (SaaS) usage and expenditures; and coordinating and executing the technical components of annual Design Studio and Raikes School events.<br><br></div><div>In addition to supporting the Raikes School Design Studio capstone program, the Engineering and Technology Education Lead provides technical support across the Raikes School. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, administering cloud-based services, source control systems, and collaboration platforms. This position serves as the primary administrator of the Raikes School website and acts as the technical liaison between the Raikes School and University ITS and audio-visual teams.<br><br>For more information on the Design Studio, please visit https://raikes.unl.edu/design-studio/.<br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> J S Raikes School of Comp Sci & Mgmt-1313 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102117 2026-08-31T16:49:10-05:00 2026-08-31T16:49:11-05:00 Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide a variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle.</li><li>Maintain machinery and fences,</li><li>Assist with pasture management</li><li>Assist with the collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather required. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position may be referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Learn more about UNL benefits and your <strong>total compensation</strong> at: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/99864 2026-03-19T16:21:04-05:00 2026-03-19T16:21:05-05:00 Solidworks Drafting Coordinator <div>This position will be responsible for ensuring technical drawings are completed accurately using the 3D computer-aided drafting program, SOLIDWORKS. The individual will complete and coordinate engineering drawings including layouts, parts details, construction or fabrication plans, and Bill of Materials (BOM’s). This employee will review and ensure all drawings completed by student employees are accurate and meet quality requirements. They will also coordinate the modification of existing designs/drawings and other documentation based on feedback and collaboration with engineering team, faculty, and technical personnel. The individual will maintain a priority list and calendar to ensure all deadlines and key dates are met. This individual will be trained to assist with maintaining and completing backup of the server; troubleshooting computer and server problems; upgrade software programs; purchasing computer equipment, and answer computer related questions. In addition, the individual will be trained to perform crash test video processing and analysis. This individual will follow a developed training procedure when training all new staff/students in video analysis, departmental use of the primary design tool SOLIDWORKS and AutoCAD. The individual will assist the Quality Manager in the management of departmental accreditation. These duties will include, but not be limited to, maintaining files, reviewing work procedures, investigating errors, recommending corrective actions, and documenting processes. This individual must maintain a safe and clean work environment by complying with procedures, rules and regulations, and other duties as assigned.<br><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Midwest Roadside Safety Facility-1070 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101698 2026-08-10T09:14:37-05:00 2026-08-10T09:14:37-05:00 Director of Memorial Stadium Complex <div>Provide leadership and oversight for the daily operations, maintenance, and event readiness of Memorial Stadium, Hawks Championship Center, Osborne Legacy Complex, and other assigned facilities. This position is responsible for ensuring facilities are maintained to the highest standards while supporting the operational needs of Nebraska Athletics, student-athletes, coaches, staff, and guests.<br><br></div><div>The Director serves as the primary facilities lead for the assigned complex, providing leadership for facility operations, maintenance planning, event coordination, staff supervision, and project management. This position participates in an on-call rotation for facility-related emergencies and works evenings, weekends, and holidays as required to support athletic competitions and special events.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Athletics-0850 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102012 2026-08-25T11:32:09-05:00 2026-08-25T11:32:10-05:00 Lead Water Analyst <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska and certified as a Lincoln Family-Friendly workplace, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.</div><div><br><strong>We invest in our employees:</strong></div><ul><li>Vacation, sick, and holiday pay.</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance.</li><li>No-cost life insurance.</li><li>Employee Assistance Program.</li><li>Parental leave</li><li>Retirement plans.</li><li>Tuition assistance for employees and dependents.</li><li>Exclusive employee discounts.</li><li>Professional development through training and education.</li><li>And many more!!</li></ul><div><br><strong>As the Lead Water Analyst, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Plan, design, maintain, and/or improve campus-wide water chemistry testing and treatment programs to ensure safe, compliant, cost-effective, and high-performing operation of boilers, chillers, cooling towers, and conditioned water systems.</li><li>Administer and execute water and steam chemistry programs to maintain regulatory compliance, maximize thermodynamic efficiency, support system reliability and capacity, and reduce corrosion, forced outages, and maintenance costs.</li><li>Develop, implement, maintain, and oversee operational procedures, logs, documentation tools, and daily water chemistry practices to ensure consistent performance, regulatory compliance, and adherence to safety and environmental programs.</li><li>Oversee daily water chemistry testing and treatment, including collection, analysis, documentation, and interpretation of water samples to verify compliance with established guidelines.</li><li>Collect, monitor, analyze, and document water chemistry across plant conditioning systems, fuel samples, calculate and adjust chemical treatment requirements, and recommend or make equipment adjustments, including blow downs and chemical feed controls, to maintain proper system performance.</li><li>Verify compliance with water treatment procedures and notify plant management of deviations from established guidelines.</li><li>Monitor system performance, troubleshoot equipment issues, and perform preventive maintenance, repairs, outage-related testing, initiate testing to determine root cause analysis, and notify applicable personnel when applicable.</li><li>Oversee and perform metallurgical testing and intervention activities for boilers and other plant systems and components.</li><li>Evaluate, recommend, and install chemical treatment equipment and electronic programming for chemical feed control systems.</li><li>Receive, prioritize, and complete work orders related to water and wastewater systems.</li><li>Coordinate and manage chemical, water treatment, equipment, and regulatory projects, including cost estimates and ongoing cost control.</li><li>Participate in planning activities related to treated water and wastewater systems to support future operational needs.</li><li>Lead compliance activities related to wastewater, stormwater, hazardous waste management, chemical safety documentation (MSDS/Right to Know), spill prevention, and pollution incident prevention requirements.</li><li>Coordinate with Environmental Health and Safety to support compliance for water chemistry operations and hazardous materials and participate in safety committees to promote adherence to applicable safety standards, regulations, and internal procedures.</li><li>Maintain, prepare, and submit all necessary water treatment, equipment, and chemical safety documentation, and ensure records are current and accessible.</li><li>Train and support plant personnel on safe water treatment operations, including systems, equipment, chemical controls, and disinfection products, through ongoing coordination, coaching, and EHS collaboration.</li><li>Research vendors and coordinate purchasing of specialized supplies, equipment, and contracted services, and manage and evaluate contractor performance by providing feedback to support plant water chemistry and water treatment operations.</li><li>Monitor and control chemical inventory, track chemical usage and expenditures, and provide budget input for chemistry operations, projects, and regulatory compliance needs.</li><li>Oversee and perform safe storage, handling, transfer, delivery notification, and disposal of hazardous and corrosive chemicals.</li><li>Participate in an on-call rotation to respond to and support emergency situations involving water chemistry issues.</li><li>Provide leadership and oversight of staff performance, including setting goals, communicating expectations, delivering coaching and training, conducting evaluations, documenting performance, and recommending salary adjustments.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</strong></div><div><br></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> UO Husker Energy & Power-12300 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101359 2026-07-22T13:48:28-05:00 2026-07-22T13:48:29-05:00 Supervisor, Electrical <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska and certified as a Lincoln Family-Friendly workplace, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year. <br><br><strong>We invest in our employees:</strong></div><ul><li>Vacation, sick, and holiday pay.</li><li>Medical, dental, and vision insurance.</li><li>No-cost life insurance.</li><li>Employee Assistance Program.</li><li>Parental leave</li><li>Retirement plans.</li><li>Tuition assistance for employees and dependents.</li><li>Exclusive employee discounts.</li><li>Professional development through training and education.</li><li>And many more!!</li></ul><div><br><strong>As the Supervisor, Electrical, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Implement operational priorities established by leadership, and communicate work status, resource needs, escalate issues, and provide reports and updates when applicable.</li><li>Monitor work activity, service trends, and operational performance metrics, and recommend improvements to electrical services, workflow efficiency, and service delivery.</li><li>Coordinate electrical installations, inspections, troubleshooting, repairs, maintenance activities, and related work assignments across assigned staff and projects.</li><li>Review estimates, project information, and work plans for accuracy, timeliness, and alignment with assigned priorities.</li><li>Assign work, monitor staffing coverage, and adjust daily work assignments to support service needs, project schedules, and operational priorities.</li><li>Track service work, project activity, and assigned tasks to help ensure completion in alignment with scope, schedule, budget, quality, and service expectations.</li><li>Coordinate with campus departments and stakeholders to ensure electrical activities align with operational needs, project schedules, and institutional priorities.</li><li>Oversee campus electrical work, such as low voltage, fire alarm, card access, service work, and medium voltage utility-related activities, and ensure work is completed safely, efficiently, and in accordance with applicable codes and standards.</li><li>Participate in facilities condition assessments and provide input on electrical system needs, deficiencies, and priorities.</li><li>Identify operational needs and recommend improvements to procedures, equipment, technologies, and contracted services to enhance reliability, safety, and service quality.</li><li>Support and monitor compliance with safety, environmental, health, accessibility, electrical code, and other applicable standards and reinforce a culture of safety and accountability.</li><li>Assist with contract coordination, vendor communication, and review of contractor performance to help ensure performance aligns with specifications, budgets, and institutional standards.</li><li>Maintain collaborative relationships with campus stakeholders, communicate work priorities and project status, manage service expectations, and share feedback with leadership to support continuous improvement.</li><li>Promote and reinforce a people-centered culture that emphasizes safety, continuous learning, collaboration, customer service, community, and operational excellence.</li><li>Provide leadership and oversight of staff performance, such as setting goals, communicating expectations, delivering coaching and training, conducting evaluations, documenting performance, and recommending salary adjustments.</li></ul><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> UO Building Systems Maintenance-1004 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100974 2026-06-23T15:27:12-05:00 2026-06-23T15:27:13-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Early Childhood (Dawson County) <div><strong>OVERVIEW</strong></div><div>This position is based in Lexington, NE with the geographic accountability region of Arthur, McPherson, Logan, Custer, Dawson, Lincoln, Perkins and Keith Counties. Focused on young children and their caregivers (e.g., parents, early childhood teachers), this position will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home unit and the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources as an effective scholar and citizen.<br><br></div><div>The primary responsibility for this position is to develop and deliver high quality, innovative educational programs and resources as an active participant in the work of the Early Childhood team and may be active in a statewide issue team that addresses current issues facing Nebraska. This position is expected to interact closely with parents, teachers, early childhood professionals, and caregivers of young children in their geographic area and possibly statewide based on the current projects and goals of the Early Childhood team.<br><br></div><div>Nebraska Extension’s Early Childhood team supports adults who play a role in young children’s lives by providing educational programming and resources about early child development and early care and education. Adults play a significant role in setting the stage for young children's lifelong learning, discovery, and success. The Early Childhood team is committed to empowering these adults to support and provide effective learning experiences for Nebraska’s young children. Such early learning experiences enhance children’s readiness (physical, cognitive, social, and emotional) for school and setting them up for lifelong success.</div><div><br></div><div>This twelve-month, non-tenure track position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate-level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress toward and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%):</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., health and wellbeing, and community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs entrepreneurial practices to obtain funding and partnerships, enhancing Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%):</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific Lead Educator roles as described in the <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator document </strong></a>as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<ul><li>Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.</li><li>Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.</li><li>Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li></ul></li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR, we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 3-12352 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101850 2026-08-18T09:35:26-05:00 2026-08-18T09:35:26-05:00 Finance Specialist <div>Join the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) Business Centers, where we strive to deliver exceptional service, innovative solutions, and responsible stewardship that advance IANR's teaching, research, and extension missions.</div><div><br>As a <strong>Finance Specialist with focus on cost accounting and contracts</strong>, you will serve as a trusted resource to departments, providing expert guidance and support across a broad range of financial functions.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Serving as a primary resource for service center and contract administration across IANR, providing strategic guidance and ensuring compliance with university policies and procedures.</li><li>Partnering with departments to develop, manage, and improve service center operations and contractual agreements, promoting effective business practices and sound financial stewardship.</li><li>Working with faculty and staff to forecast expenses and calculate appropriate service rates based on anticipated activity. Regularly review budget to actual amounts to determine if established rates need to be adjusted.</li><li>Managing an assigned portfolio, serving as a trusted advisor on financial management, funding strategies, and compliance across a variety of funding sources including but not limited to state accounts, grants, service centers, and revolving accounts.</li><li>Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>We seek a collaborative, service-oriented professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate builds trusted relationships, communicates effectively with diverse stakeholders, and exercises sound judgment to make and communicate decisions that support responsible stewardship, compliance, and exceptional service.<br><br>This position is located on Nebraska Innovation Campus in Lincoln, NE. Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with a minimum of 3 days per week worked on campus. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br><strong>Note:</strong> Sponsorship will not be offered for this position. <br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> NE Innovation Campus Business Ctr-3028 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102074 2026-08-27T17:03:16-05:00 2026-08-27T17:03:16-05:00 Quick Service Team Member: Cook (6:00am-2:30pm, M-F) <div>The <strong>Quick Service Team Member</strong> is an key position within Dining Services. This position will work within Abel Dining Center, which is one of the quick serve made to order concepts that relies on the mobile ordering platform for orders.<br><br>As a <strong>Quick Service Team Member</strong> you will:</div><ul><li>Provide excellent customer service</li><li>Perform all back of the house kitchen duties, including ingredient and food preparation, inventory, cooking and assembling orders, setting up and closing down stations, recipe preparation, dish machine operations and cleaning</li><li>Build orders based on established processes, procedures, guidelines and recipes</li><li>Monitor food quality, food presentation and control food waste</li><li>Assist within other areas as needed and other duties assigned</li></ul><div><br>This position is considered essential and may have weekend or evening shifts.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong><br></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Housing: AS Dining Service-1135 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101578 2026-08-03T08:59:53-05:00 2026-08-03T08:59:53-05:00 Extension Assistant - Raising Nebraska (Grand Island, NE) <div><strong>Raising Nebraska</strong> is a dynamic 25,000 square foot educational experience located in Grand Island, NE. The experience is designed to help visitors better understand and appreciate where their food comes from and features state-of-the-art technology across dozens of interactive exhibits. Raising Nebraska is the premier destination for understanding how agriculture is grown and raised and the science and innovation that are fundamental to farming and ranching in Nebraska. Learn more about Raising Nebraska at <a href=\"https://raisingnebraska.net/\"><strong>raisingnebraska.net</strong></a>.<br><br><strong>As an Extension Assistant, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Transform lives by delivering, teaching and managing effective educational programming in Food Confidence and Ag Literacy at the Raising Nebraska facility in Grand Island, NE.</li><li>Engage youth and adults through diverse learning strategies.</li><li>Market the Raising Nebraska facility, including Raising Nebraska Outdoors, and its programs.</li><li>Build support and engagement and create programming/learning experiences both inside and beyond the Raising Nebraska facility.</li></ul><div><br>This position is located in Grand Island, NE and requires the ability to travel within the service area and occasionally outside the service area for programming or professional development.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> 4-H Youth Development-0940 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101991 2026-08-25T11:07:30-05:00 2026-08-25T11:07:31-05:00 Export Control Coordinator I, II, or III <div>The Office of Research and Innovation at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (UNL) is committed to promoting a culture and environment for success in research, scholarship, creative endeavors, and economic development. Conducting novel and impactful research that generates new knowledge, solves real-world problems, and enhances lives is among the most fundamental purposes of the institution.<br><br>UNL Research and Innovation has an opportunity for qualified candidates to apply for an Export Control Coordinator position within the Office of Research Compliance, Integrity, and Security at one of three levels: Coordinator I, II, or III.<br><br>The Export Control Coordinator performs functions related to the oversight, guidance and direction of the UNL Export Control Program, processes, and policies. The primary focus of this position is applying policies and regulations to provide expert advice and training to university administrators and employees on matters relating to Export Control and preventing non-compliance with organizational policies and procedures relating to export controlled research.<br><br>In addition to the above responsibilities, the Export Control Coordinator II and III are responsible for other duties specific to training, creation of TCPs and interaction with the National Strategic Research Institute (NSRI.)<br><br></div><div><em>This position will involve/require access to EAR/ITAR related information, materials, or equipment and may require a license approval from the U.S. government.</em><strong><br></strong><br>This position may be considered for remote work in accordance with the University of Nebraska’s Alternative Worksite policy.<br><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Rsch Compliance, Integrity, Security-1315 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102189 2026-09-04T14:33:58-05:00 2026-09-04T14:33:59-05:00 Grants Specialist <div>The Grant Specialist serves in a customer-facing, consultative role and is responsible for providing grant support in a timely and accurate manner and in compliance with all applicable institutional, UNL, State, and Federal regulations, policies, and guidelines. The Grant Specialist primarily executes and reviews routine and complex pre- and post- award grant transactions. The Grant Specialist will work closely with employees within the College of Education and Human Sciences as well as functional office staff, providing a high level of customer service and professionalism in all interactions. This position functions under limited supervision and is expected utilize sophisticated technology to provide professional services.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options </strong>including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> College of Education & Human Sciences-0910 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101906 2026-08-19T10:41:13-05:00 2026-08-19T10:41:13-05:00 Research Communications Specialist <div>The Research Communications Specialist is an integral part of the team that leads communications and marketing efforts for the Office of Research and Innovation (R&amp;I). The team promotes research, scholarly and creative endeavors at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln and ensures that the university researcher community is aware of the resources, opportunities and support available through R&amp;I.<br><br></div><div>The position is geared toward a strong writer and editor who is able to translate complex information and convey the impact of Nebraska researchers’ work in an engaging and accessible manner. The Research Communications Specialist is responsible for writing and editing content that is used across a variety of platforms, including news releases, websites, reports and newsletters.<br><br></div><div>This position also executes communications and marketing tasks for lectures, conferences, workshops and other events hosted by R&amp;I. Additionally, the specialist regularly updates website content on research.unl.edu. The ideal candidate demonstrates exceptional attention to detail and works well in a collaborative, team-oriented environment.</div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Research Communications-13275 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102119 2026-08-31T17:01:31-05:00 2026-08-31T17:01:32-05:00 Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. All work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide a variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle.</li><li>Maintain machinery and fences,</li><li>Assist with pasture management</li><li>Assist with the collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather required. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position may be referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Learn more about UNL benefits and your <strong>total compensation</strong> at: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100064 2026-04-07T14:12:43-05:00 2026-04-07T14:12:43-05:00 Outreach and Engagement Specialist <div>For over 30 years, the High Plains Regional Climate Center (HPRCC) has been providing the public with access to the most up-to-date climate data and information available. We provide a variety of resources, including near real-time and historical climate data, national and regional climate data maps, agricultural climate products, and regional climate summaries.<br><br><strong>As an Outreach and Engagement Specialist, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Analyze, interpret, and retrieve climate data to produce educational materials for the public on the HPRCC website, including informational material on HPRCC products, product updates, and instructional guides.</li><li>Work independently to produce summaries or recaps of notable weather and climate events within the High Plains region.</li><li>Use MS Office programs, Adobe InDesign, and ArcGIS products to create educational materials and custom maps based on user and stakeholder needs.</li><li>Serve as the point of contact for outreach and engagement activities, coordinating and leading in-person and virtual public presentations, meetings, workshops, conferences, and joint outreach events.</li><li>Assist HPRCC staff with ongoing projects and daily activities, including QA/QC of climate databases, feedback on product and tool development, and external work requests.</li><li>Track and evaluate the success of the education and outreach programs.</li></ul><div><br>In the UNL system, this position is categorized as a Field Training Specialist.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> School of Natural Resources-0844 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101727 2026-08-10T16:21:24-05:00 2026-08-10T16:21:25-05:00 Sheep Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The <strong>U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC)</strong> is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.<br><br><strong>As a Sheep Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Be responsible for care of livestock to include feeding, observation, and treatment of sheep population.</li><li>Service and maintain equipment and buildings in the sheep facilities.</li><li>Maintain the sanitation of sheep facilities.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather is required. Ability to travel between locations onsite is required.&nbsp; In the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I.&nbsp; In the livestock industry, this position may be referred to as a herdsman or shepherd.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a> &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a><em>&nbsp;</em></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102016 2026-08-25T11:32:58-05:00 2026-08-25T11:32:58-05:00 Cattle Ranch Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC) is a 34,000-acre facility located near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. beef cattle, sheep, and swine industries.</div><div><br><strong>As a Cattle Ranch Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide variety of basic agricultural duties to support research and production activities at an agricultural research facility in the beef livestock production area.</li><li>Provide general care and husbandry for approximately 800-1200 cattle.</li><li>Maintain machinery and fences.</li><li>Assist with pasture management and the collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Position requires irregular hours and work in inclement weather. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.</div><div><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this positon.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101413 2026-07-24T13:03:25-05:00 2026-07-24T13:03:26-05:00 Finance/Grant Specialist <div>The Finance/Grant Specialist serves in a customer-facing, consultative role and is responsible for providing finance and grant support in a timely and accurate manner and in compliance with all applicable institutional, UNL, State, and Federal regulations, policies, and guidelines. The Finance/Grant Specialist primarily executes and reviews routine and complex finance and pre-and post-award grant transactions. The Finance/Grant Specialist will work closely with employees within the departments served, as well as functional office staff, providing a high level of customer service and professionalism in all interactions. This position functions under limited supervision and is expected utilize technology to provide professional services.<br><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Big Red Business Center-11350 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101059 2026-07-06T08:40:56-05:00 2026-07-06T08:40:57-05:00 Early Childhood Data Collector (Part-Time: On-Call) <div>Part-time, on-call data collectors needed to help fulfill many research functions in the Nebraska Center for Research on Children, Youth, Families and Schools at the University of Nebraska – Lincoln.</div><div><strong>Responsibilities Include:</strong></div><div><strong>Field-based data collection and professional representation</strong></div><ul><li>Travel to schools across Lincoln and rural areas of Nebraska,.</li><li>Serve as the face of the research team in the field, coordinating schedules, conducting assessments, and upholding confidentiality and professional standards</li></ul><div><strong>Administering assessments and maintaining reliability</strong></div><ul><li>Conduct questionnaires with parents and administer standardized assessments to young children (ages 3–6)</li><li>Complete training to achieve and maintain reliability on all assessment measures</li></ul><div><strong>Supporting logistics and data management</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with scheduling assessments, scoring, checking data, and coordinating with other data collectors</li><li>Contribute to data management tasks and ensure accurate documentation</li></ul><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> NE Ctr Research on Youth, Fam & School-4425 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101877 2026-08-19T10:26:36-05:00 2026-08-19T10:26:36-05:00 Facility Services Manager <div>Facility Services Manager oversees all care, maintenance and project needs for the Lied Center for Performing Arts, including physical plant and its operating systems, interior furnishings and fixtures. Directs all aspects of building maintenance and housekeeping, conversion and engineering tasks related to the operation of the Lied Center. Oversees the supervision of the building maintenance staff and manages the custodial staff. Conducts yearly staff performance evaluations and ensures adherence to building policy and procedures. Plans and budgets for renovation projects, building upkeep, repairs, furnishing replacements and fire, life and safety projects. Creates the scope of work required for projects to be worked in-house, or seeks out contractors and bids and works with UNL FMP code officials on acquiring permits, scheduling work, quality control, ensuring regulatory and code compliance and ensuring deadlines are met and work is performed in a professional manner. Prioritizes all building events with repairs and project needs.<br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Lied Center for Performing Arts-0854 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102081 2026-08-28T09:17:20-05:00 2026-08-28T09:17:20-05:00 Educational Specialist <div>The Education Specialist works in the High Schools within the Lincoln Metro area to support students within the TRIO Upward Bound program.<br><br></div><div>As an Education Specialist, you will:</div><ul><li>Formulate and implement an educational plan that addresses each participant’s individualized academic, educational, and leadership needs and interests</li><li>Provide academic advising and instructional support that enables participants to be retained with the program</li><li>Develop and implement college preparatory activities and programs</li><li>Actively assist in the development and implementation of the Upward Bound summer program at the University of Nebraska – Lincoln</li><li>Assist program participants with Post Secondary Pathway planning</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br> <br> </strong><strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em></strong><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> TRIO Programs-0962 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101612 2026-08-04T11:23:13-05:00 2026-08-04T11:23:14-05:00 Program Coordinator, Student Culture and Community <div>We’re looking for someone to join our team to support a dynamic student community. The <strong>Program Coordinator</strong> advances student belonging and holistic success by coordinating programs, services, and engagement opportunities that support all students at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln. This position helps cultivate welcoming spaces and campus-wide connections where students can access resources, build supportive relationships, and participate in meaningful community experiences. Through intentional programming, partnership development, and student-centered engagement, the Program Coordinator strengthens inclusive excellence and contributes to a campus climate where all students can thrive. <br> <br>The <strong>Program Coordinator</strong> will:</div><ul><li>Support the development of a campus-wide culture of belonging.</li><li>Facilitate and support programming efforts, including affinity-based communities, dialogue spaces, and mobile engagement opportunities that promote identity exploration, connection, and belonging.</li><li>Coordinate and implement embedded gender and sexuality engagement initiatives across campus including; student spaces, and campus environments to increase access, visibility, and impact.</li><li>Serve as a key partner with Residence Life and campus collaborators, supporting the integration of identity-affirming practices within daily student environments.</li><li>Assist with training initiatives for student-facing staff (e.g., Resident Assistants, desk staff, and student leaders).</li><li>Contribute to outreach and engagement strategies that expand participation and reduce barriers to access for students across varying stages of identity development.</li><li>Assist in building and maintaining internal and external partnerships that enhance student engagement, community connection, and holistic support.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us:<br></strong>The Office of Student Culture &amp; Community fosters dynamic and supportive environments, provides empowering experiences, and supports all students to strengthen a sense of belonging and holistic success. We cultivate spaces, programs, and partnerships where all Huskers can engage genuinely, meaningfully, and thrive in community.<br><br>We advance student success by connecting individuals to resources that address basic needs, support academic and personal development, and build leadership capacity. We empower students not only to navigate campus life but also to shape it.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.<br><br></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Student Culture & Community-11400 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101994 2026-08-25T11:11:29-05:00 2026-08-25T11:11:30-05:00 Registrar Information Systems Developer <div>Create new reports, electronic forms, workflows, and other electronic processes using the suite of development tools within the student information system. Write XSL expressions within system tools to create electronic documents and communications. Deliver content to the student information system’s end-users in easy to consume formats. Use SQL, WebFOCUS coding and other system tools to write queries against the student information system. Create system interfaces between the Student Information System and other subsidiary systems. Create data branching logic to create datasets that can be consumed by reporting and data analysis tools. Determine means to meet end-users’ reporting and analysis needs throughout the university. Act as a resource to UNL system users and functional administrators, provide regular updates, and answer questions. Possess and maintain a practical knowledge of university policies and processes. Communicate effectively with individuals of varying system expertise and business needs.<br><br><strong>Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</strong><br><br>The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential. As an EO/AA employer, qualified applicants are considered for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See: http://www.unl.edu/equity/notice-nondiscrimination</div> Office of the University Registrar-0961 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101422 2026-07-24T15:49:34-05:00 2026-07-24T15:49:35-05:00 Finance Specialist <div>The Finance Specialist serves in a customer-facing, consultative role and is responsible for providing finance support in a timely and accurate manner and in compliance with all applicable institutional, UNL, State, and Federal regulations, policies, and guidelines. The Finance Specialist primarily executes and reviews complex travel, procurement, contracts, accounts payable, accounts receivable, accounting, foundation, budgeting, and asset management transactions. The Finance Specialist will work closely with employees within the departments served, as well as functional office staff, providing a high level of customer service and professionalism in all interactions. This position functions under limited supervision and is expected to utilize sophisticated technology to provide professional services.<br><br><em>As an EO/AA employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Big Red Business Center-11350 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101913 2026-08-19T10:56:56-05:00 2026-08-19T10:56:57-05:00 Research Specialist I, II, or Senior Research Specialist <div>Work with dynamic teams on variety of public policy projects, including those in behavioral health, public participation, and other applied social sciences endeavors. Will conduct and facilitate research, coordinate projects and stakeholder involvement processes, design survey instruments, collect and analyze data, assist with writing reports, and present findings that impact state, local and federal policy. Some travel required.<br><br><strong><em>Please note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.</em></strong><br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> Public Policy Center-1525 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102132 2026-09-01T13:12:42-05:00 2026-09-01T13:12:43-05:00 Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - HLES (Scotts Bluff County) <div><strong>OVERVIEW<br></strong>This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position based in Scottsbluff, NE, with a geographic accountability region including Banner, Box Bute, Cheyenne, Dawes, Deuel, Garden, Kimball, Morrill, Scotts Bluff, Sheridan, and Sioux Counties. This education professional’s primary responsibility is to develop and deliver educational programs and resources in horticulture or related fields. They will be an active participant in the Horticulture, Landscape, and Environmental Systems (HLES) program and one or more of its focus teams, as well as other state-wide and multidisciplinary teams. They will be expected to interact closely with individuals, homeowners, producers, institutions, and organizations working in communities to deliver programs in their geographic area as well as statewide based on the intentions of the statewide team.<br><br></div><div>Nebraska thrives when there are robust, thriving communities. Nebraska Extension’s role is to catalyze opportunities for communities and individuals within communities to make informed decisions that are supported by research. Extension is a co-solution development centric organization. Core to this role is the ability to engage clientele in learning and sharing opportunities. Expected outcomes include: 1) engagement strategies based on lasting and trusted relationships with clientele and associated business and industry leaders that positively impact communities, 2) educational opportunities that result in better stewardship of resources that enhances quality of life, and 3) engagement in education that results in solutions that are sustainable and, where applicable, include a financial and well-being component.</div><div><br>The HLES Extension professional will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home unit and IANR as an effective scholar and citizen. In HLES we educate and engage Nebraskans, from youth and home gardeners and homeowners to commercial growers, industry, partner organizations, and local leaders and stakeholders that impact communities and sustainably manage community spaces.</div><div><strong><br></strong>This position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an open rank educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress towards and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers <a href=\"https://nebraska.edu/faculty-and-staff/resources/employee-dependent-scholarship-program\"><strong>tuition remission</strong></a> for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment.<br><br></div><div><strong>PROGRAMMATIC RESPONSIBILITIES (approximately 80%)</strong></div><ul><li>Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations.</li><li>Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally.</li><li>Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues.</li><li>Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels.</li><li>Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information.</li><li>Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities.</li><li>Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., on-farm, ranch, or community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms.</li><li>Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information.</li><li>Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute.</li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve.</li><li>Employs entrepreneurial practices to obtain funding and partnerships, enhancing Extension’s program reach and impact.</li><li>Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System.</li><li>Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams.</li><li>Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role.</li><li>Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment.</li><li>Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate.<ul><li>Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.).</li><li>Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute.</li></ul></li><li>Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve.</li><li>Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments.</li><li>Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements.</li><li>Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>ORGANIZATIONAL CITIZENSHIP/LEAD EDUCATOR ROLE (approximately 20%)</strong></div><ul><li>Serves in, contributes to, or supports the specific lead educator roles as described in the Roles <a href=\"https://myextension.unl.edu/lead-educator-position-description\"><strong>and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator document</strong></a> as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s).</li><li>Coordinates with Engagement Zone Coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by<ul><li>Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county.</li><li>Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community.</li><li>Supporting engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors.</li></ul></li><li>Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts.</li><li>Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</li></ul><div><br>Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license.<br><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR, we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br></div><div>This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> NE Ext Engagement Zone 1-12350 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100143 2026-04-13T16:57:50-05:00 2026-04-13T16:57:51-05:00 Associate Dean for Academic Affairs (Open to CEHS and CEHS/IANR Faculty Only) <div>The University of Nebraska’s College of Education and Human Sciences (CEHS) is one of nine colleges at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, a comprehensive, land grant, Big10 research-intensive university. CEHS is one of the few colleges in the country whose programs span broad fields of education, health, wellness and fitness, human services, and hospitality industries. Our mission is to enhance the lives of individuals, families, schools and communities and strengthen the relationships among them. The Associate Dean for Academic Affairs has leadership and administrative responsibilities focused on undergraduate and graduate curriculum, program evaluation, innovative pedagogy that prepares graduates to be life-long learners and contributors to the workforce, and creating a climate that emphasizes and fosters a welcoming and engaged college community. This will be an Academic Year (AY) or Fiscal Year (FY) appointment, at up to 0.70 FTE apportioned as 100% administration, and supported with an administrative stipend up to $15,000 and summer salary (AY only). There would be at least a .30 FTE faculty position with a negotiable apportionment in the faculty member’s department home. For more information on the College of Education and Human Sciences visit https://cehs.unl.edu/.<br><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities include:<br>1) Student Success and Academic Support <br></strong>a. Work collaboratively with the Senior Director of Student Services to support and cultivate innovative advising, retention, and degree completion initiatives.<br>b. Address academic appeals, grievances, and policy exceptions in accordance with university and college procedures.<br>c. Promote and develop initiatives that support co-curricular and applied experiences that promote student success and career development.<br><br></div><div><strong>2) Academic Leadership and Program Oversight<br></strong>a. Provide leadership and oversight of the college’s undergraduate and graduate curriculum committees, Academic Affairs (including curriculum development, reviews, and assessment), and instructional technology.<br>b. Provide leadership and oversight of the Teachers Scholars Academy.<br>c. Provide leadership and oversight of the Interactive Distance Education Alliance (IDEA).<br>d. Foster collaborations and partnerships among units with the Osher Lifelong Learning Institute (OLLI).<br>e. Oversee academic policies, procedures, and standards related to instruction, grading, progression, and program completion.<br>f. Foster a respectful and inclusive culture in which contributions are appreciated and recognized, collaboration and innovation are encouraged, and the abilities of all are engaged to fully recognize the potential of the team.<br><br></div><div><strong>3) Accreditation and Compliance<br></strong>a. Lead and coordinate accreditation efforts, including HLC, CAEP, and other specialized program accreditation.<br>b. Work collaboratively with the CEHS Office of Accreditation, Placement and Licensure team related to educator preparation program compliance with state standards, licensure, regulatory requirements and accreditation.<br>c. Oversee the quality assurance system of data collection, analysis, and reporting related to student learning outcomes, program effectiveness, and continuous improvement.<br><br></div><div><strong>3) Communication and Collaboration<br></strong>a. Work collaboratively with the Dean of Undergraduate Studies and Dean of Graduate Studies; facilitate linkages with university offices, committees, and other partners; serve as a college representative on the University Wide Assessment Committee, Academic Solutions Council and others as needed.<br>b. Engage external stakeholders – including P-12 partners, community organizations and industry and global partners – to cultivate, nurture and sustain collaborative relationships that advance high quality initiatives and mutually beneficial partnerships.<br>c. Foster collaborative, interdisciplinary activities among academic units.<br>d. Ensure opportunities are open to all, encompass all constituencies and efforts are made to engage with a variety of audiences.<br>e. Partner with the college Strategic Communications Director to share successes and outcomes of Academic Affairs.<br><br></div><div><strong>4) Vision and Innovation<br></strong>a. Contribute to strategic planning and implementation related to Academic Affairs, enrollment management, and instructional innovation.<br>b. Support the development of new programs, concentrations, and delivery modalities (e.g., online, hybrid, certificates, micro-credentials).<br>c. Develop a future direction with input from departments, students, and stakeholders that encompasses all programs and facilitates individual and collective efforts to hold high standards for Academic Affairs and student learning.<br>d. Seek and deploy strategic resources to advance and elevate Academic Affairs.<br><br></div><div><strong>5) Teaching, Research, and Service: </strong>There would be a .30 FTE faculty position with a negotiable apportionment in the faculty member’s department home. Candidate would engage in academic activities based on applicant’s strengths, interests and needs of the home department and college.<br><br><strong>Why this role, why now.</strong></div><div>This position is critical for the success of the college, particularly as it pertains to the national accreditation and state certification requirements for our educator preparation programs. We also have several nationally accredited programs across the college – each of our five departments has at least one accredited program. The need for this position certainly extends beyond accreditation. Improving the student experience, both in and out of the classroom, is a priority given the current importance of attracting and retaining students in our challenging budget climate. This position will also be important to help us strengthen and develop new enrollment pathways, including community colleges and online initiatives.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> College of Education & Human Sciences-0910 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101739 2026-08-11T08:58:38-05:00 2026-08-11T08:58:38-05:00 Chick-fil-A Team Member (Part-Time) <div>The Chick-fil-A Team Member serves as an integral member of the Chick-fil-A team.<br><br>The Team Member will provide excellent customer service to all guest through front end and back end operations which may include:</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Greeting all guests in a friendly manner.</li><li>Accurately entering orders into the POS system.</li><li>Cashier duties.</li><li>Food preparation.</li><li>Front end and kitchen stocking.</li><li>Ingredient preparation.</li><li>Inventory.</li><li>Dish machine operation.</li><li>Cleaning duties.</li><li>Opening and closing procedures.</li><li>Monitoring food quality and safety.</li><li>Assists with training new staff as necessary.</li><li>Operates the computer for some training, email, and other related tasks.</li></ul><div><br>At Chick-fil-A, the team member role is more than just a job, it’s an opportunity.<br><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.<br><br>When you join our team as a regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> Housing: Chick-fil-A-12426 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102018 2026-08-25T11:33:12-05:00 2026-08-25T11:33:12-05:00 Dining Team Member (Husker Heroes) <div>The Nebraska Unions Food Commons features a variety of dining options, including local favorites such as Valentino’s and Imperial Palace, as well as popular concepts like Sossy’s BBQ, Husker Hero’s, and Choolaah. We are seeking a <strong>Dining Team Member</strong> to maintain daily operations of one of these dining concepts while helping deliver an outstanding guest experience.<br><br>As a <strong>Dining Team Member</strong>, you will:<br><br></div><ul><li>Provide friendly, professional customer service to all guests</li><li>Process customer orders accurately using the POS system</li><li>Prepare food and beverages according to company standards and customer requests</li><li>Fulfill mobile and in-store orders efficiently</li><li>Stock front-of-house and kitchen supplies</li><li>Prepare ingredients and assist with inventory management</li><li>Operate dishwashing equipment and maintain cleanliness throughout the facility</li><li>Perform opening and closing procedures</li><li>Ensure food quality, safety, and sanitation standards are met</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Schedule varies and includes evenings, late nights, and weekend shifts.</strong><br><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><br><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Housing: Retail Operations-12425 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101996 2026-08-25T11:14:33-05:00 2026-08-25T11:14:33-05:00 Utility Project Engineer <div>Ranked as one of the Best Employers in Nebraska, the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success and satisfaction. We invest in our staff by offering fantastic benefits like vacation, sick, and holiday pay, a variety of insurance options, retirement plans, and numerous others. By joining our team, you will be given opportunities to grow as an individual and contribute to the significant impact that we make within the University of Nebraska community and Nebraska’s economy each year.<br><br>Husker Energy &amp; Power has three levels of Utility Project Engineers, and the level is determined by a candidate’s knowledge, skills, abilities, and applicable licensure.<br><br></div><div><strong>Utility Project Engineer Level I:</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with providing technical support and review for new installations and upgrades of district energy infrastructure, including production and distribution systems for steam, chilled water, and medium voltage electricity.</li><li>Provide continuous communication to internal staff, suppliers, contractors, university project managers, and design firms to ensure projects are executed on time and within budget.</li><li>Assist with the preparation and facilitation of design reviews with internal stakeholders.</li><li>Review and comment on drawings and submittals from design firms and contractors.</li><li>Collaborate with contractors, design professionals, and internal staff to schedule and manage project execution.</li><li>Develop knowledge of plant MEP systems and applicable codes, standards, and regulatory requirements.</li><li>Assist in developing and reviewing technical specifications, standards, drawings, and contracts for engineering services and construction projects.</li><li>Assist with the design and management of small to medium-scale infrastructure upgrade projects, collaborating with internal stakeholders to define the appropriate scope for repairs and upgrades.</li><li>Manage project documentation, including operating and maintenance procedures for new equipment and updating existing technical documentation to reflect infrastructure modifications.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Utility Project Engineer Level II:</strong></div><div>In addition to the Level I requirements, the Level II engineer will:</div><ul><li>Provide technical support and review for new installations and upgrades of district energy infrastructure, including production and distribution systems for steam, chilled water, and medium voltage electricity.</li><li>Prepare and facilitate design reviews with internal stakeholders.</li><li>Review and approve drawings and submittals from design firms and contractors.</li><li>Assist with the development of departmental standards, processes, and tools for the design and review of new equipment, replacements, repairs, and upgrades.</li><li>Collaborate with internal stakeholders to develop and review technical specifications, standards, drawings, and contracts for engineering services and construction projects.</li><li>Design and manage small to medium-scale infrastructure upgrade projects, collaborating with internal stakeholders to define the appropriate scope for repairs and upgrades.</li><li>Collaborate with internal stakeholders to develop operating and maintenance procedures for new equipment and update existing technical documentation to reflect infrastructure modifications.</li></ul><div><strong><br>Utility Project Engineer Senior:</strong></div><div>In addition to the Level I and Level II requirements, the Senior engineer will:</div><ul><li>Provide continuous communication to internal staff, suppliers, contractors, university project managers, and design firms to ensure projects are executed on time and within budget.</li><li>Lead the preparation, execution, and continuous improvement of design reviews with internal stakeholders.</li><li>Develop departmental standards, processes, and tools for the design and review of equipment installations, replacements, repairs, and upgrades.</li><li>Lead the development and review of technical specifications, standards, drawings, and contracts for engineering services and construction projects.</li><li>Evaluate small to medium-sized infrastructure improvement initiatives within the department to verify compliance with relevant codes and the application of proper engineering design methodologies.</li><li>Develop and maintain processes for continual review of department technical documentation to confirm accuracy.</li><li>Support leadership and contribute to long-range infrastructure planning efforts and the development and implementation of departmental vision and goals.</li><li>Train, mentor, and verify work of other staff, students, temp, and/or on-call personnel.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> UO Husker Energy & Power-12300 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101079 2026-07-07T10:55:08-05:00 2026-07-07T10:55:08-05:00 Multispecies Livestock Hand (Clay Center, NE) <div>The <strong>U.S. Meat Animal Research Center (USMARC)</strong> is a 34,000-acre facility near Clay Center, NE. The work performed at USMARC supports research that is focused on solving high priority problems for the U.S. cattle, sheep, and swine industries.</div><div><br><strong>As a Multispecies Livestock Hand, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Work with and around cattle, pigs, and sheep.</li><li>Be responsible for weighing, sorting, and animal health.</li><li>Perform daily maintenance of machinery and fences.</li><li>Treat sick animals.</li><li>Feed livestock in the winter.</li><li>Help with hay in the summer.</li><li>Assist with collection of research data.</li></ul><div><br>Irregular hours and work in inclement weather required. Travel between pastures and facilities required. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Ag Research Technician I. In the livestock or beef industry, this position is sometimes referred to as a herdsman or cowboy.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we're proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn't just a workplace; it's a place ot build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you'll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Ample paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance</li><li><strong>Employee &amp; dependent scholarship program</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Generous retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working for UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>As an EO employer, the University of Nebraska considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> USMARC-0937 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101879 2026-08-19T10:27:21-05:00 2026-08-19T10:27:21-05:00 AI Integration Specialist <div>The AI Integration Specialist serves as a foundational technical role within the College of Business, supporting the application of artificial intelligence and automation technologies to improve teaching, research, and administrative operations.<br><br></div><div>This position performs technical and analytical tasks under general supervision and assists with the design, development, and maintenance of AI-enabled applications and automated workflows. The specialist collaborates with faculty and staff to identify opportunities for using technology to streamline processes, increase efficiency, and support innovation across the college.<br><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong><em>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</em></strong></a><em>.&nbsp;</em></div> College of Business-0897 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102088 2026-08-28T13:01:26-05:00 2026-08-28T13:01:26-05:00 Fitness Coordinator <div>The Fitness Coordinator provides leadership for the daily operation of Campus Recreation's fitness facilities and Personal Training program. <br><br>In this role you will oversee:<br><br><strong>Fitness Operations</strong></div><ul><li>Oversee daily operation of all strength and cardiovascular fitness areas.</li><li>Supervise student staff.</li><li>Ensure safe, clean, and welcoming fitness environments.</li><li>Develop and implement operational policies and procedures.</li><li>Coordinate risk management practices and facility inspections.</li><li>Assist with the coordination of equipment maintenance, inventory management, and recommendations for equipment replacement planning.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Personal Training Program</strong></div><ul><li>Recruit, hire, train, supervise, and evaluate Personal Trainers.</li><li>Develop and grow the Personal Training program.</li><li>Monitor program quality, participation, and customer satisfaction.</li><li>Coordinate client onboarding and trainer assignments.</li><li>Develop new services and programming.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Student Staff Leadership</strong></div><ul><li>Supervise a large student employee team.</li><li>Develop student leaders.</li><li>Provide ongoing training and mentorship.</li><li>Conduct evaluations.</li><li>Create a positive team culture.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Instruction &amp; Education</strong></div><ul><li>Teach or assist in the administration of academic credit courses each semester as assigned, such as FITN 222: Intro to Personal Training.</li><li>Assist with educational workshops.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Administration</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with budgeting.</li><li>Supervise the Fitness Graduate Assistant.</li><li>Collect assessment data.</li><li>Collaborate with other Campus Recreation staff and campus partners.</li><li>Support departmental initiatives.</li></ul><div><br><strong>About Us:</strong></div><div>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li><li>A workplace culture that <strong>values your time outside of work</strong></li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br></div><div>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\"><strong>https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</strong></a>.</div> Campus Recreation-0965 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101618 2026-08-04T13:41:04-05:00 2026-08-04T13:41:05-05:00 Ag Research Technician I (Part-Time, On-Call) <div>At the UNL Panhandle Research, Extension and Education Center in Scottsbluff, NE, we innovate and conduct research to make life better for Nebraska ag producers and rural communities.<br><br><strong>As an Agricultural Research Technician I (Part-Time, On-Call), you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with field and laboratory research supporting irrigation and digital agriculture projects</li><li>Conduct field setup and maintenance</li><li>Perform sensor installation and data collection</li><li>Conduct crop and soil sampling</li><li>Take laboratory measurements</li><li>Clean and organize equipment</li><li>Perform data entry and other tasks needed to complete funded project deliverables.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Work may occur outdoors in variable weather and may require occasional early mornings or extended hours. On-Call positions are hired to work during peak activity periods and may work up to 693 work hours per fiscal year. On-call employees are not eligible for any leave with pay or any other university benefits. Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an O/S On-Call Worker. <br><br>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Panhandle Research, Extension and Education Center-0942 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101431 2026-07-27T09:17:57-05:00 2026-07-27T09:17:58-05:00 FARRP Program Coordinator <div>The Food Allergy Research and Resource Program (FARRP) works to develop and provide the food industry with credible information, expert opinions, tools, and services relating to a broad range of food allergen topics. FARRP takes a comprehensive approach, working and collaborating with research institutions, governmental authorities, consumer groups, and scientific societies around the globe to improve the safety of food products for consumers.<br><br></div><div>As a <strong>FARRP Program Coordinator</strong>, you will:</div><ul><li>Lead day-to-day financial operations for FARRP, providing operational and financial support to the co-directors across a complex portfolio of funding sources, projects, program activities, and revenue streams.</li><li>Serve as a primary financial advisor to the co-directors, conducting critical, time-sensitive financial analyses, identifying trends, and developing recommendations to support strategic and operational decision-making related to budgeting, compliance, and resource allocation.</li><li>Serve as the primary point of contact for industry stakeholders on all non-scientific matters, managing ongoing relationships, coordinating communications, and facilitating access to program resources.</li><li>Develop and execute strategic member engagement and communication initiatives that strengthen relationships, support long-term program objectives, and enhance the value of FARRP membership.</li><li>Lead the planning and execution of the large-scale annual FARRP Board meeting, workshops, and other events by independently managing complex logistics, budgets, vendor relationships, contractual negotiations, and external partners.</li><li>Lead operational implementation of FARRP outreach initiatives developed by leadership, including in-person events, virtual programming, online courses, publications, and other educational resources.</li><li>Provide strategic input to support the program's communication objectives and manage day-to-day operations of the FARRP website and external communication channels.</li><li>Provide direct supervision and leadership for the administrative support team, focusing on workload coordination, performance management, and professional development.<br><br></li></ul><div>Occasional travel is required for program events.</div><div><br>Within the UNL system, this position is categorized as an Admin Associate.</div><div><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> Food Science & Technology-0836 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101947 2026-08-20T16:08:15-05:00 2026-08-20T16:08:15-05:00 Associate Director of Academic Advising Initiatives (Open to University Staff Only) <div>The Associate Director of Academic Advising Initiatives provides oversight of academic advising, new student onboarding, and student success initiatives within the College of Arts and Sciences. Responsibilities include coordinating college participation in new student enrollment and orientation programs; supervising, developing, and assessing professional advising staff; leading advisor training and workload management; supporting college-wide retention, persistence, and graduation initiatives; maintaining a limited advising caseload while providing complex academic guidance; collaborating with academic departments and campus partners to improve student success outcomes; and contributing to assessment, data analysis, and continuous improvement efforts. The role also serves on college and university committees and advances professional development and best practices in academic advising.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. Our campus is known for its welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong>, including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong>, including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Robust retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> College of Arts & Sciences-0906 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102139 2026-09-01T15:23:47-05:00 2026-09-01T15:23:47-05:00 Director, International Student/Scholar Office <div>The Director of the International Student and Scholar Office (ISSO) serves as a member of the University of Nebraska-Lincoln’s global leadership team. The Director provides vision, oversight, and leadership to all areas of this comprehensive office: immigration advising, employment-based visas, sponsored students, and incoming exchange programs, to ensure that students and scholars maintain their legal status in the United States.<br><br></div><div>ISSO also supports student engagement and intercultural initiatives to enhance student success, including significant programming dedicated to international students’ personal development and adjustment to UNL, in addition to leading programming that integrates international students, scholars, and their dependents. The Director oversees the delivery of exceptional services in all of these areas in collaboration with 7.5 professional staff who are all direct reports.<br><br>Additional Duties: Provides vision, strategic management, expert policy interpretation and analysis, and leadership to the International Student &amp; Scholar Office (ISSO); Serves as UNL’s Principal Designated School Official (PDSO) and Responsible Officer (RO) in overseeing the student and scholar programs in the government’s Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS). Responsible for UNL’s participation in SEVIS and institutional compliance with federal immigration regulations. As such, oversees the training and support of Designated School Officials (DSOs) and Alternative Responsible Officers (AROs) on campus. Provides administrative leadership and oversight of ISSO operations, budgets, and personnel.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/.</div> Intl Student & Scholar Office-8401 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100212 2026-04-20T14:36:04-05:00 2026-04-20T14:36:04-05:00 Open Rank Research Professor - Water Sciences Lab Director <div>The Water Sciences Laboratory (WSL), is a core research facility at the University of Nebraska, administered by the Nebraska Water Center, part of the Daugherty Water for Food Global Institute (DWFI) and the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR).<br><br>With a 100% administrative research apportionment, this 12-month (calendar year) non-tenure track, renewable appointment will have a 3-5 year initial appointment based on rank at time of hire. The position reports to the Nebraska Water Center director and leads all WSL activities, supervising a laboratory manager and technical staff, while supporting staff and users in day-to-day facility operations. This position is located in Lincoln, Nebraska, and will be affiliated with an academic unit in IANR to ensure the incumbent has a pathway to promotion conforming to UNL policies and guidelines. To learn more about Lincoln, please visit <a href=\"https://aboutlincoln.unl.edu/\"><strong>About Lincoln | Nebraska</strong></a>. <br><br><strong>Position Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Demonstrate strong communication skills, vision, and leadership to further the WSL mission to provide advanced, high quality, defensible results for water and environmental research</li><li>Seek out and develop relationships with external stakeholders and faculty from the university system to support joint research and service projects, enhancing laboratory services to meet user requirements while implementing practical ways to maintain quality and improve operation efficiency.</li><li>Actively collaborate on publications, contracts and grant opportunities, and work with the Nebraska Water Center staff to promote the facility widely to potential users on and off campus.</li><li>Mentor laboratory users and staff to ensure timely processing of client samples, facilitate problem-solving, and assist the laboratory manager in implementing a robust quality assurance program using a new laboratory information management system.</li><li>Prepare annual facility reports to the Office of Research and Innovation which integrate fiscal and technical input from an administrative advisory board, laboratory user group, and business office staff.</li></ul><div><br>In addition to the above-described duties, the individual will be expected to accept committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level.</div><div><br>Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources (IANR) and the Water Sciences Laboratory in the Nebraska Water Center are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. Consistent with the University’s N2025 Strategic Plan, we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission.<br><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/\">https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/</a>.&nbsp;</div> Water Center-2225 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/101745 2026-08-11T11:49:07-05:00 2026-08-11T11:49:08-05:00 Budget Analyst I <div>At the University of Nebraska’s College of Engineering, our mission is to train the next generation engineering workforce and solve problems of global importance. <br><br><strong>As a Budget Analyst I, you will:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide budget and financial analysis for the College of Engineering Dean's office.</li><li>Review and analyze overall College and department budgets to aid in decision making processes.</li><li>Perform ad hoc analysis of financial data for dean-level decision-making.</li><li>Troubleshoot budget and financial commitment issues, understanding the complex requirements of each fund type and providing advice to unit leaders.</li><li>Reconcile and monitor financial status of college funds on a monthly basis including state, revolving, and foundation accounts.</li><li>Assist with the development of the annual operating budget, day-to-day operating budget, and the update and maintenance of SAP Org Management.</li><li>Represent interests in college and university committees and task forces.</li><li>Be administratively responsible to the Assistant Dean of Business and Financial Affairs,</li></ul><div><br>Following an initial training period of up to six months, this position may become eligible for a hybrid work schedule, with four days in office and one day remote each week. Hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace</strong> certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li><strong>Generous paid time off</strong> including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li><strong>Comprehensive insurance options</strong> including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li><strong>Employee and dependent scholarship programs</strong> to pursue higher education</li><li><strong>Retirement plans</strong> with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br><em>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See </em><a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong><em>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</em></strong></a></div> College of Engineering-0907 https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102022 2026-08-25T11:33:38-05:00 2026-08-25T11:33:39-05:00 Grants Specialist - Lead <div>As a<strong> Grants Specialist-Lead,</strong> you will serve as a trusted resource to faculty and departments, providing expert guidance and support throughout the sponsored research proposal process.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Partnering with faculty and departments to support the successful development and submission of sponsored research proposals.</li><li>Providing consultative guidance on grants administration policies, procedures, and best practices.</li><li>Coordinating proposal budgets, documentation, submissions, and grant startup activities.</li><li>Collaborating with university partners to deliver exceptional service and promote effective, compliant research administration.</li><li>Ensuring that records are maintained according to policy.</li><li>Supervising employees by providing work direction, coaching, training, and mentoring to support employee development and ensure consistent, accurate, and timely completion of responsibilities.</li><li>Supporting sponsored research through post-award grant financial management and administration.</li><li>Assisting with training new staff members.</li><li>Reviewing and coordinating complex financial activities, including travel, contracts, journal entries, accounts receivable, capital assets, and other financial transactions.</li><li>Supporting unit leadership in budget analysis, preparing reports and identifying potential areas of concern.</li></ul><div><strong><br></strong>Following an initial onsite training period of up to six months, this position may become<strong> </strong>eligible for a hybrid work schedule with up to 1 remote day(s) per week. All hybrid arrangements are subject to supervisor approval and are determined based on operational needs.<br><br>Note: Sponsorship will not be offered for this position.<br><br><strong>About Us</strong></div><div>At the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and recently earned the <strong>Lincoln Family Friendly Workplace </strong>certification. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska.</div><div><br>When you join our team as a full-time, regular staff member, you’ll enjoy:</div><ul><li>Generous paid time off including vacation, sick leave, parental leave, and holidays</li><li>Comprehensive insurance options including medical, dental, vision, and life coverage</li><li>Employee and dependent scholarship programs to pursue higher education</li><li>Robust retirement plans with university match</li></ul><div><br>Learn more about working at UNL: <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/aboutus\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/aboutus</strong></a></div><div><br>The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=\"https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination\"><strong>https://go.unl.edu/nondiscrimination</strong></a></div> College of Engineering-0907"
