f Law invites applications for the position of Reference Librarian (Open Rank Professor) at the Schmid Law Library. This 12-month, tenure-track law library faculty position offers an opportunity to support student learning and faculty scholarship while contributing to the mission and values of the College of Law.This role offers an exciting opportunity to con... View Details Bookmark Lecturer (German Language) Modern Language & Literature-1090 Faculty 04/20/2026 05/21/2026 The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures at UNL seeks a full-time, one-year lecturer to teach German language and culture classes at the 100 (introductory) through 400 (advanced undergraduate) levels. The proposed load for the 2026-2027 academic year is eight (8) courses (approximately 24 credit hours) over two semesters. The proposed salary range is $42,000 (M.A.) – $45,000 (Ph.D.). ... View Details Bookmark Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - HLES (Scotts Bluff County) NE Ext Engagement Zone 1-12350 Faculty 07/27/2026 10/16/2026 OVERVIEWThis is a full-time, 12-month non-tenure track position based in Scottsbluff, NE, with a geographic accountability region including Banner, Box Bute, Cheyenne, Dawes, Deuel, Garden, Kimball, Morrill, Scotts Bluff, Sheridan, and Sioux Counties. This education professional’s primary responsibility is to develop and deliver educational programs and resources in horticulture or related fiel... View Details Bookmark Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - 4-H Youth Development (Garden County) NE Ext Engagement Zone 1-12350 Faculty 07/28/2026 10/02/2026 OVERVIEWThis position is based in Oshkosh, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Garden and Morrill Counties. The major responsibility of this position is to provide regional leadership for Nebraska Extension’s 4-H and Youth Development Program. This extension professional is expected to interact closely with 4-H clientele in these communities and deliver programs in their geographic... View Details Bookmark Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Early Childhood (Dawson County) NE Ext Engagement Zone 3-12352 Faculty 02/23/2026 08/17/2026 OVERVIEWThis position is based in Lexington, NE with the geographic accountability region of Arthur, McPherson, Logan, Custer, Dawson, Lincoln, Perkins and Keith Counties. Focused on young children and their caregivers (e.g., parents, early childhood teachers), this position will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home unit and the Institu... View Details Bookmark Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - 4-H Youth Development (Lincoln County) NE Ext Engagement Zone 3-12352 Faculty 07/15/2026 09/04/2026 OVERVIEWThis position is based in North Platte, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Lincoln, Logan, and McPherson Counties. The major responsibility of this position is to provide regional leadership for Nebraska Extension’s 4-H and Youth Development Program. This extension professional is expected to interact closely with 4-H clientele in these communities and deliver programs in ... View Details Bookmark Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Early Childhood (Red Willow County) NE Ext Engagement Zone 4-12353 Faculty 07/14/2026 08/17/2026 OVERVIEWThis position is based in McCook, NE, with the geographic accountability region of Chase, Dundy, Frontier, Furnas, Gosper, Harlan, Hayes, Hitchcock, Phelps, and Red Willow Counties. Focused on young children and their caregivers (e.g., parents, early childhood teachers), this position will contribute to the integrated (extension, research, and teaching) land-grant mission of the home un... View Details Bookmark Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - Water & Cropping Systems (Platte Co.) NE Ext Engagement Zone 7-12356 Faculty 06/24/2026 07/24/2026 Overview This position is based in Columbus, NE with the geographic accountabi