    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/100201": {
      "title": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Lecturer (German Language)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Lecturer (German Language) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lecturer (German Language) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Letter of interest describing your qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching experience and philosophy. Attach as \"Other Document.\" In addition, candidates must arrange for three (3) letters of reference, one of which must focus on teaching, to be sent via email to Samantha Deline at sdeline2@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Lecturer (German Language) Department Modern Language & Literature-1090 Requisition Number F_260032 Posting Open Date 04/20/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 05/21/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Modern Languages and Literatures at UNL seeks a full-time, one-year lecturer to teach German language and culture classes at the 100 (introductory) through 400 (advanced undergraduate) levels. The proposed load for the 2026-2027 academic year is eight (8) courses (approximately 24 credit hours) over two semesters. The proposed salary range is $42,000 (M.A.) – $45,000 (Ph.D.). The department is unable to sponsor visa applications for this position. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Master’s degree in German studies or a closely related field by August 2026. Professional-level proficiency in German and English. Experience teaching elementary and intermediate German in a university setting. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in German studies or a closely related field by August 2026. Experience teaching German culture courses in a university setting. Experience developing courses. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Letter of interest describing your qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Statement of teaching experience and philosophy. Attach as “Other Document.” In addition, candidates must arrange for three (3) letters of reference, one of which must focus on teaching, to be sent via email to Samantha Deline at sdeline2@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Lori Ratzlaff lratzlaff@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Non-Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/17/2026 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
